\f0 \cf2  The Abhorsen stands straight.                               \
\
  Not rigid \'97 the posture of someone who has waited for this without knowing they were waiting. The bells do not stir. The Dead are elsewhere. This room is very much among the    \
  Living, and the man crossing toward her is just a man \'97 tired, dignified, carrying more history than his suitcase.\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She does not look away.                                   \
\
  He stops at arm's length. The courthouse light falls across the striped shirt and the floral tie beneath where the robe had been. He is shorter without the bench beneath him.   \
  More present.\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  He extends his hand.                                      \
\
  "The High Court of the Loganic Archetypal Framework," he says, with the measured cadence of a man who has read this language before and believes it still means something,       \
  "recognizes the standing of the Abhorsen within the county jurisdiction. You are entitled to act in formal capacity within these proceedings."\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  A pause. Something in his shoulders releases \'97 a fraction. Professional.\
\
  "Welcome to the road."                                                                                                                                                           \
   \
  The Abhorsen takes his hand. The grip is firm on both sides. Two professionals who have been alone too long in separate rooms, meeting at a threshold neither of them built.     \
                                                            \
  "The suitcase," she says. "The Geminiaeus matter."                                                                                                                               \
                                                            \
  "Delegated to me by the High Court. The false GRIMOIRE, the Antigravity Lich \'97 that trial needs a venue large enough." He picks up the case. "The Hotel Denouement is large      \
  enough."                                                  \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  "And the Five Wizards."                                   \
\
  "WHO is already there, I would wager." The dry amusement again. "That old wizard never stops asking."                                                                            \
   \
  They walk toward the door together. The courthouse is empty behind them \'97 the bench unmanned, the gavel set down, the crack in it from the Triumvirate days still visible across \
  the wood.                                                 \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She does not look back.                                                                                                                                                          \
   \
