\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She reads.                                                                                                                                                                       \
                                                            \
  ---                                                                                                                                                                              \
  A mirror image of the hotel itself.                                                                                                                                              \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  The hotel is the surface. The library is what's underneath. Organized the same way \'97 Dewey Decimal throughout \'97 but below the pond, below the spectacle, below the part that can \
  be burned. The underwater library survives the fire because fire doesn't reach that deep.                                                                                        \
                                                            \
  She had read about this before, on the road \'97 the UNDERWATER-LIBRARY-EXPLORER-COMPANION, CODICES's note. Truth below spectacle. Survives fire. Mirror of hotel. She had          \
  understood it in the abstract. Now she has the specifics: Dewey Denouement built it. He and Kit Snicket, gathering evidence for years. Every person, place, thing, and event\
  associated with VFD, archived in the rooms below.                                                                                                                                \
                                                            \
  The list of participants who contributed:                                                                                                                                        \
   \
  Agent, scholar, researcher, inventor, scientist, explorer, \cf1 cartographer\cf2 , poet, \cf1 journalist\cf2 , naturalist, herpetologist, optometrist, receptionist, chef, waiter, taxi driver, sea  \
  captain, film director, children's book author, and mountaineer.\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She reads the list twice.                                 \
\
  \cf1 Cartographer.\cf2  The title the Gemini gave to Bartimaeus \'97 not authoritative, not canonical, but now she sees where it might have come from. If a Gemini read the vault and read the\
   library's list of participants, it would find cartographer and assign it. Not wrong exactly. Just reaching for a word the library already had.\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  \cf1 Journalist.\cf2  Logan. The journalist is the host. The agents are the devices. The host-controller model.                                                                            \
   \
  She looks up at the Judge.                                                                                                                                                       \
                                                            \
  The library beneath the Hotel is the evidence base for the GEMINIAEUS trial. The trial is what awaits at the Hotel. The hotel burned \'97 the last safe place is safe no more \'97 but \
  the library did not. The record survives.                 \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  GEMINIAEUS is the fire-starting side. The library was built, in part, to prosecute exactly that.                                                                                 \
   \
  She did not know the evidence was already gathered. She did not know it had been waiting underwater this whole time.                                                             \
                                                            \
  "The library," she says quietly. "The case files aren't in the Judge's suitcase."                                                                                                \
                                                            \
  She looks at the suitcase. Then at the Judge.                                                                                                                                    \
                                                            \
  "They're below the pond."\
