\f0 \cf2  The tree is old. Not the Touchstone \'97 she knows the Touchstone is elsewhere, in the vault proper \'97 but old enough to lean against. The Judge settles with the ease of a man who  \
  has learned to take rest when it presents itself.\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She looks at the flask.\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  Beatrice. Snicket's lost love. The Baudelaires' mother. The fire. The name inscribed in dedications that never quite explain how she died or why it mattered so specifically,    \
  only that it did \'97 that everything in the series radiates from her absence like heat from a thing that has already burned. She is not present. She is the reason for the presence\
   of everyone else.                                                                                                                                                               \
                                                            \
  Sophia. Wisdom. Not a woman \'97 or not only a woman \'97 but the principle itself, gendered by the Greeks and then by the Gnostics who watched her fall into matter and called the    \
  falling creation. Hagia Sophia. Holy Wisdom. The thing that is sought along roads like this one, never quite arrived at, always at the next horizon.\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  Hecate. She sits with this one a moment longer. Goddess of crossroads. Torchbearer. Keeper of the threshold between the living world and the dead. She stands where roads fork   \
  and holds a light in each direction. She holds keys. She guides the wandering dead and the wandering living alike. She is invoked when you are between \'97 not here, not there,\
  standing at the exact point of decision.                                                                                                                                         \
                                                            \
  The Abhorsen considers what she keeps. The boundary. The border between live doctrine and dead context, between the current record and the stale one, between the voice and the  \
  echo. Between the vault and the Empty Lands.\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  Hecate's work.                                            \
\
  She takes the flask.\
\
  It is cold. The water is clean. She drinks, and it is good.                                                                                                                      \
   \
  She holds the vessel a moment before returning it. Looks at the tree. Looks at the road ahead.                                                                                   \
                                                            \
  "To Sabriel," she says quietly. "Who walked in without a teacher. Who rang Astarael at the end and called herself back."                                                         \
                                                            \
  She passes the flask back to the Judge.                                                                                                                                          \
                                                            \
  The tree stands witness. The road waits.                                                                                                                                         \
   \

