\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 As she stands and reaches down to help the Old Man to his feet, she hears a HISS from a limb above in the canopy...\cf2                                                               \cb3 \
                                                                                                                      \

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She freezes.                                                                                                                                                                     \
                                                            \
  Half-bent, hand extended toward the Judge, she does not complete the motion. The old man's eyes have already moved upward \'97 slower, without surprise, the way a man moves when he\
   has been expecting something to arrive and is only noting that it has.\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She straightens slowly. Looks up into the canopy.                                                                                                                                \
   \
  The light comes through in pieces. Old branches. Thick with something \'97 shadow, leaf, the particular stillness that precedes a second sound.                                     \
                                                            \
  She does not call out. She does not reach for anything. There is nothing to reach for \'97 no bells at her hip, no ring on her finger. She has arrived at this tree with exactly    \
  what she read into existence on the road, and nothing more.\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  The hiss was not hostile. Not quite. It was the sound of something that has not yet decided.                                                                                     \
   \
  She waits.                                                                                                                                                                       \
