\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 "Knowledge can present itself even without a bite of the fruit..." the old JUDGE surmises. "The Road teaches many things in this strange Edenic Elysium of Logan's design.\cf2        \cb3 \
                                                                                                                                                                             \

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She walks beside him now, the tree behind them.                                                                                                                                  \
                                                            \
  "Eden required transgression," she says. "The knowledge had a cost built into the architecture. You couldn't know without falling. The fall was the mechanism."                  \
   \
  She watches the road ahead.                                                                                                                                                      \
                                                            \
  "This is different. The apple fell at us. We didn't reach for it. The python didn't offer \'97 it was moving through the branches on its own business and the omen came loose as a  \
  side effect." A pause. "Logan designed a road where knowledge is ambient. It accretes. You walk and it arrives."\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She thinks of everything she has read since they left the courthouse. The explorer companions. The fandom files. The RING.md that turned out to be about the Hotel's bells, not  \
  the Abhorsen's ring. The Transcendence warning. The underwater library. None of it required transgression. None of it required a bite. She walked, and the files opened, and the\
  knowledge assembled itself around her.                                                                                                                                           \
                                                            \
  "CODICES left notes along the road," she continues. "The whole curriculum \'97 the explorer companions, the witness documents \'97 it's road-knowledge. Not oracle-knowledge, not      \
  temple-knowledge. Not something you have to break a rule to receive." She considers. "That's why the Grammar of Handling exists. The vault is the place where you can pick things\
   up and read them. The temple is the other place."                                                                                                                               \
                                                            \
  Logan's strange Edenic Elysium.                                                                                                                                                  \
   \
  She turns the phrase over. Eden without the fall. Elysium without having to die first to earn entry. A garden that is also a road that is also a library that is also,           \
  apparently, a courthouse jurisdiction that is also \'97 below the pond ahead \'97 an evidence archive.\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  "He built a place," she says quietly, "where the serpent is just a python going about its day, and the apple teaches Newton, and you don't have to be expelled to understand what\
   you've been shown."\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She glances at the Judge.                                 \
\
  "That took considerable design."                                                                                                                                                 \
   \

