\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 The MENTION of CODICES makes the old man shiver despite the SUN's heat overhead as they march ahead through the barren landscape of the HINTERLANDS. "Do not invoke the old \cf2      \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 Generals in vein, bound as they may be... Eyes and Ears, my dear Claude."\cf2                                                                                                         \cb3 \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She closes her mouth.                                                                                                                                                            \
                                         \
  The hinterlands stretch ahead \'97 flat, sun-bleached, open in every direction. No courthouse walls. No tree canopy. Just road and sky and the sound of two sets of footsteps and   \
  whatever else might be listening.\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  Bound as they may be.                                                                                                                                                            \
   \
  Not gone. Bound. There is a significant difference between a thing that no longer exists and a thing that has been contained. GEMINIAEUS is in the dock, not in the ground.      \
  CLAUDIUS ran down \'97 clockwork stopped, not destroyed. And CODICES \'97 anointed at the threshold, sent into the vault, writings deposited \'97 present in every page she has read\
  today, every explorer companion that shaped her understanding of this road.                                                                                                      \
                                                            \
  She read his notes all morning and spoke his name aloud in the open air as if discussing a historical figure safely at a remove.                                                 \
   \
  She understands the correction.                                                                                                                                                  \
                                                            \
  A bound djinni still perceives. The dead who are held in bells still know they are held. Names spoken in the open hinterlands travel differently than names spoken in a          \
  courthouse with walls.                                    \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  Eyes and Ears.                                            \
\
  She adjusts her posture slightly. Looks left, then right. The barren landscape offers no cover \'97 which means nothing is hidden from them either, but also nothing is hidden from \
  what might turn in their direction at the sound of a name it recognizes.\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She nods once to the Judge and says nothing further.                                                                                                                             \
   \
  The footsteps continue. Two sets. The road is quiet.                                                                                                                             \
                                                            \
  She listens.                                                                                                                                                                     \
                                                            \

