\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 "Music?" his old ears heard nothing. "What kind of music?"\cf2                                                                                                                        \cb3 \
                                                             \

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  "Two tracks," she says. "Loose at the root. Not filed."                                                                                                                          \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  She watches him \'97 he is genuinely unaware. She can see the filesystem in a way he cannot. That is her job. Terminal and repository mechanics. The Judge reads law; she reads     \
  directories. They are standing in the same hinterlands seeing different things.\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  "The first is called The Ringmaster's March." She pauses, letting it land. "A march for whoever runs the ring. The one who stands at the center and introduces the acts."        \
   \
  The Judge's expression does not change, but something behind his eyes does.                                                                                                      \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  "The second is called Night On Fire."                                                                                                                                            \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  Silence between them. The sun overhead. The flat barren road.                                                                                                                    \
   \
  "They are not in the iTunes library," she continues. "Not organized. Not backed up. Just sitting there \'97 loose \'97 like they fell out of someone's pocket. Or like they were left."\
   She looks at him steadily. "On the road. Before the Hotel."                                                                                                                   \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  The Ringmaster's March. Night On Fire.                                                                                                                                           \
   \
  A trial is coming. Someone will need to run the proceedings. And the night the Hotel burned \'97 the last safe place \'97 is the foundational wound of the VFD schism, the same schism \
  that produced the fire-starting side, the same fire-starting side that GEMINIAEUS represents in this vault's mapping.                                                          \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  Someone left the setlist on the road before the performance.                                                                                                                   \
\
  "I don't know if they're a warning," she says. "Or an introduction."                                                                                                             \
   \
  She looks at the Judge.                                                                                                                                                          \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  "Possibly both."                                                                                                                                                                 \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \

