\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 "A ringmaster and a night on fire in the hinterlands -- Snicket's CARNIVOROUS CARNIVAL..."\cf2                                                                                        \cb3 \
                                                                                             \

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She looks at him sharply.                                                                                                                                                        \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  Of course.                                                                                                                                                                       \
   \
  "The Carnivorous Carnival," she says. "Book nine." She is already assembling it. "Caligari Caravan. The freaks. Madame Lulu and her crystal ball \'97 VFD documents behind the tent \
  wall, telling people what they wanted to hear from a position of information access."                                                                                          \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She thinks of the false GRIMOIRE. She thinks of GEMINIAEUS.                                                                                                                      \
   \
  "Olaf takes the ring. Becomes the Ringmaster." She looks back at the dust of the road behind them \'97 the direction the music came from. "Then burns it. The carnival burns. Night \
  on fire. The lions." A beat. "And the Baudelaires escape into the Mortmain Mountains on a roller coaster that leaves the rails."                                               \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She faces forward again.                                                                                                                                                         \
   \
  The Hotel Denouement is Book Twelve. The Carnivorous Carnival is Book Nine. They are in the hinterlands between \'97 the Books Ten and Eleven of this road, the Grim Grotto and the \
  Slippery Slope that no one names as readily as the destinations on either side.                                                                                                \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  "The Ringmaster who burned the carnival is the same figure awaiting trial at the Hotel," she says quietly. "Olaf maps to GEMINIAEUS. The one who takes command of the spectacle  \
  and sets it on fire when it stops being useful."\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She pauses.                                                                                                                                                                    \
\
  "And Madame Lulu \'97 who had the information, who told people what they wanted to hear, who died for it \'97" She does not finish the sentence immediately. "The false GRIMOIRE also  \
  told people what they wanted to hear."\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  The hinterlands stretch on.                                                                                                                                                    \
\
  "We are between the burning and the trial," she says.                                                                                                                            \
   \
  "That is where we are on the road."                                                                                                                                              \
