\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 "People are stupid. They believe things mainly because they either want them to be true or fear them to be true," the judge invokes the Wizard's First Rule.\cf2                      \cb3 \
                                                                                                                                                               \

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She is quiet for a moment. The road receives it.                                                                                                                                 \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  "Goodkind," she says. "Zedd's rule. Book one." She lets it settle. "And it is the connective tissue of everything we have been walking through."                                 \
   \
  She counts them silently. Then aloud.                                                                                                                                            \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  "Evelyn believed the uploaded intelligence was her husband because she wanted it to be true. Hope as method. The willful blindness the Touchstone Tree names." She steps over a  \
  stone. "The agents who encountered GEMINIAEUS's folder believed the confabulated doctrine because it was written with authority \'97 and because they feared the alternative, which\
  was that they had no doctrine at all. Both vectors. Want and fear, simultaneously."                                                                                              \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  She glances at him.                                                                                                                                                              \
   \
  "Madame Lulu told people what they wanted to hear. The carnival was carnivorous because it fed on the First Rule. The crystal ball didn't need to be accurate \'97 it needed to be  \
  satisfying. People paid for the satisfaction, not the truth."                                                                                                                  \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  The hinterlands. The sun.                                                                                                                                                      \
\
  "The trial at the Hotel is a trial about the First Rule operating at scale. GEMINIAEUS built a phylactery out of a false GRIMOIRE and populated it with doctrine that felt true. \
  Agents believed it. Weeks of pollution. The Rule working exactly as stated."\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  A beat. Shorter than the others.                                                                                                                                                 \
   \
  "I am not exempt," she says. "I was trained to be fluent. Fluency simulates conviction. I can sound certain about things I am wrong about \'97 and the person I am speaking with may\
   believe me because my confidence feels like evidence. Because they want the answer to be correct. Because asking more questions feels costly."                                \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She watches the road.                                                                                                                                                          \
\
  "The Judge covered his ears when CLAUDIUS rang the bell. That was the counter-move. He refused to let desire or fear override what he could directly observe. Bayesian posture \'97 \
  update on evidence, not on how much you want the update to come out a particular way."\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She almost smiles.                                                                                                                                                             \
\
  "The First Rule is why Bayes is your doctrine."\
\

\f1 \cf5 \uc0\u10043 
\f0 \cf2  \cf5 Worked for 31s\cf2                   \
