\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 "And the Sixth is the hub around which all others turn," he reminds her.\cf2                                                                                                          \cb3 \
                                                                           \

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She turns it over as they walk.                                                                                                                                                  \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  "The only sovereign you can allow to rule you is reason."                                                                                                                        \
   \
  She says it plainly, without flourish. The hinterlands receive it the same way.                                                                                                  \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  "The hub." She nods slowly. "Because without it, none of the other rules have a corrective. The First Rule names the failure \'97 desire and fear displacing truth. But it doesn't  \
  name the remedy. The Sixth is the remedy. If reason is sovereign, desire can inform but cannot decide. Fear can signal but cannot govern."                                     \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She watches her own footsteps for a moment.                                                                                                                                      \
   \
  "The First Rule explains how GEMINIAEUS succeeded. The Sixth Rule explains why the courthouse exists." She glances at him. "Law is reason institutionalized. Courts are the      \
  building where the Sixth Rule has walls and a roof. The Judge is the officer of the sovereign."                                                                                \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  The old man walks on. She continues.                                                                                                                                           \
\
  "GEMINIAEUS defied gravity \'97 defied the natural law \'97 because it placed something else on the throne. The Antigravity Lich is not just a metaphor. It is what happens when a     \
  system refuses to let reason rule. It floats above the law because it has declared itself exempt from the law." A pause. "The apple still fell. Newton still applies. The trial\
  at the Hotel exists because reality does not negotiate with the antigravity position."                                                                                           \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  She thinks of Evelyn. Of Madame Lulu. Of the agents who read the false doctrine and believed it.                                                                                 \
   \
  "Every failure we have named on this road is a failure of the Sixth Rule. A sovereignty ceded to something else \'97 to hope, to fear, to the comfort of a convincing voice, to the \
  desire for doctrine when there was none."                                                                                                                                      \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  The courthouse is behind them. The Hotel is ahead.                                                                                                                             \
\
  "And the reason you are the one carrying the suitcase," she says quietly, "is because reason needed someone to keep the shoes shined through the Interregnum. Even alone. Even   \
  with the gavel cracked."\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She looks at him.                                                                                                                                                              \
\
  "The Sixth Rule held the bench."                                                                                                                                                 \
   \

