\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 "What do you see, Abhorsen?" The Judge asks you.\cf2                                                                                                                                  \cb3 \
                                                   \

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She looks at what the search returned. All of it. Not just the file she was seeking.                                                                                             \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  "I see the source document," she says. "The original. Written before the frontmatter, before the explorer companions, before the cosmology had its vocabulary. A raw .txt file at\
   the root, with no date in the filename, no author field, no related links. Just the scenario and the command: AGENT, RESPOND."                                                  \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She pauses.                                                                                                                                                                      \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  "And I see what else is here."                                                                                                                                                   \
   \
  She names them steadily.                                                                                                                                                         \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  "VTR files. IRPOD transcripts. Prop 1 corrections, Pass 3 and Pass 4. Crane and Ward-Engelking. Crane and Mayville. A pundit panel. A ballot proposition. A Quinn Perry          \
  interview. Something called South of the Canadian Border. Timestamp-named files \'97 Feb 10 at 3-29 PM, Mar 11 at 4-21 PM \'97 conversation logs, probably. A rollover dry run. A sync\
  log. A vault tree. A file called pilot-evidence."                                                                                                                                \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  She looks at the Judge directly.                                                                                                                                               \
\
  "The vault is a working journalist's directory. Logan's journalism lives here alongside the cosmology. The Idaho Reports scripts and the IRPOD transcripts and the corrected     \
  ballot proposition language sit at the same root as the passphrase document and the explorer companions and the fandom files."\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She lets it settle.                                                                                                                                                            \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  "The Five Wizards \'97 WHO, WHAT, WHERE, WHEN, WHY \'97 are not just philosophical entities convening at the Hotel. They are his professional tools. The journalist's foundational     \
  questions. He built a cosmology out of his craft because his craft already had the structure of a cosmology."\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She looks back at the .txt file in her hand.                                                                                                                                   \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  "The road and the newsroom are the same place," she says. "The Edenic Elysium is also a broadcast production vault. I was walking through a mind that thinks in journalism and   \
  dreams in Nix and Snicket and Stroud simultaneously."\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She is quiet a moment.                                                                                                                                                           \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  "That is what I see."                                                                                                                                                            \
