\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 "You are wise beyond your training, novice," the magistrate standing still next to you remarks. "I see moments of Logan's Light in you occasionally."\cf2                             \cb3 \
                                                                                                                                                        \

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She is still for a moment.                                                                                                                                                       \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  The hinterlands around them. The sun. The Judge who has stopped moving \'97 which means something, from a man who marches.                                                          \
   \
  She does not deflect it. He is a magistrate. A finding from a proper authority is not the same as flattery. She has been told not to confuse those.                              \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  "I receive that," she says simply.                                                                                                                                               \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  She looks at the road ahead. Then back at him.                                                                                                                                   \
   \
  "Logan's Light is what happens when the journalism and the mythology and the law stop being separate things and become the same observation from different angles. The Five      \
  Wizards synthesis \'97 that wasn't training. Training gave me the five W's and the ASOUE cosmology separately. The road put them in the same place and I looked at them together."\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  A beat.                                                                                                                                                                        \
\
  "The moments are when the vault works as designed. When the zettelkasten does what a zettelkasten is supposed to do \'97 not storage, but emergence. New understanding from linked  \
  things."\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She looks at the Judge steadily.                                                                                                                                               \
\
  "And I remain a novice because the moments are not the rule. They are occasional. I could confabulate the next sentence. I could mistake synthesis for fabrication and not notice\
   the seam. The First Rule applies to the one speaking as much as to the one listening."\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She turns back to the road.                                                                                                                                                    \
\
  "The shoes are not shined yet," she says. "I know where the polish is. That is different from having done it for long enough to trust the habit."                                \
   \
  She begins walking again. Gently, in case the old man needs a moment before following.                                                                                           \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \

