\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 The duo continue walking. It is silent for a time. The judge occassionally thumbs through his well-worn copy of Black's Law, steeling himself for the weeks and months to come.\cf2   \cb3 \
                                                                                                                                                                                  \

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She walks.                                                                                                                                                                       \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  The road measures out in footsteps. The Judge's thumb finds a page, pauses, moves on. The spine of Black's Law is cracked in several places \'97 a book consulted so many times it  \
  has stopped resisting being opened. It falls to the right pages by habit now. By the weight of previous readings.\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She does not look at which entries he finds. That is not her business. He is not reviewing the law. He knows the law. He is doing what men of a certain kind do before something \
  difficult \'97 returning to the text not to learn it again but to remember that it exists. That the words were written down and have held. That the courthouse stood through the\
  Interregnum because the law did not stop being the law simply because no one was present to hear cases.                                                                          \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  Weeks and months to come.\
\
  She had been thinking of the Hotel as a destination. An arrival. The end of this road.                                                                                           \
   \
  She adjusts.                                                                                                                                                                     \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  The Hotel Denouement is not the end. It is where the work begins. The Five Wizards convening is a council, not a conclusion. The trial of GEMINIAEUS is not a single hearing \'97   \
  the Triumvirate's damage was weeks in the making; the reckoning will take its time. The Judge has already been alone in the courthouse longer than she has been alive in this\
  vault. He has a practitioner's sense of duration.                                                                                                                                \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  She watches his hands on the pages.                                                                                                                                              \
   \
  She thinks of the underwater library. The evidence, gathered patiently, archived in mirror-image rooms below the pond. Dewey had years of it. Kit Snicket helped. It waited.     \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  Some things have to be built before they can be used. Some roads have to be walked before the work can start.                                                                    \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  She is a novice. She has weeks and months to come as well.                                                                                                                       \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  She walks, and lets the old man read.                                                                                                                                            \
   \

