\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 'THE FIVE CORE LAF-* REPOS...'\cf2                                                                                                                                                    \cb3 \
                                \

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She slows her pace slightly, working it through.                                                                                                                                 \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  \cf5 Searched for 1 pattern, read 1 file (ctrl+o to expand)\cf2                                                                                                                            \
                                                             \

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She reads the whole document.                                                                                                                                                    \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  Then she reads the Mermaid diagram, tracing the branches with her eyes.                                                                                                          \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  LAF-US                                                                                                                                                                           \
  \uc0\u9500 \u9472 \u9472  PRIVATE                                                                                                                                                                      \
  \uc0\u9474    \u9500 \u9472 \u9472  SECRET                                                                                                                                                                 \
  \uc0\u9474    \u9492 \u9472 \u9472  PERSONAL                                                                                                                                                                 \
  \uc0\u9474        \u9492 \u9472 \u9472  IDAHO-VAULT\
  \uc0\u9492 \u9472 \u9472  PUBLIC                                                                                                                                                                       \
      \uc0\u9492 \u9472 \u9472  PUBLISH                                                                                                                                                                \
          \uc0\u9492 \u9472 \u9472  THE-GEMSTONE\
\
  Two poles. Not five equal peers.                                                                                                                                                 \
   \
  She had been expecting something like the Great Charter \'97 five parallel pillars, each load-bearing in its own right. What she finds instead is a \cf1 chambered sovereignty model\cf2 .    \
  PRIVATE and PUBLIC as the two primary domains. SECRET and PERSONAL as subsets of PRIVATE. PUBLISH as a subset of PUBLIC. The five cores are real, but they are not flat.       \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She thinks of the Wall.                                                                                                                                                          \
   \
  The Wall divides the Old Kingdom from Ancelstierre. Magic-strong from magic-weak. Inner from outer. It is not a peer of the three bloodlines \'97 it is a different kind of         \
  structure, a geographic and metaphysical boundary that determines what can cross and in which direction.                                                                       \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  PRIVATE and PUBLIC are the Wall, expressed as governance doctrine. The boundary between what is contained and what faces outward. IDAHO-VAULT is on the PRIVATE side \'97 under     \
  PERSONAL, under PRIVATE, the inner Old Kingdom. THE-GEMSTONE is on the PUBLIC side \'97 under PUBLISH, under PUBLIC, the face presented to Ancelstierre.\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She finds the tension the document has already named:                                                                                                                            \
   \
  IDAHO-VAULT is doctrinely PERSONAL \'97 conceptually private \'97 but the live GitHub repository is public.                                                                            \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  The Wall is permeable. The Old Kingdom is visible from Ancelstierre, at least at the repo level. The document does not resolve this. It records it so it cannot be silently      \
  ignored. That is honest governance \'97 naming the contradiction rather than smoothing over it.                                                                                   \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She finds the second tension:                                                                                                                                                  \
\
  LAF-USB appears as both migration doctrine and a live GitHub team.                                                                                                               \
   \
  Not a naming collision. A duality. LAF-USB is the protocol being designed \'97 the USB device descriptor mapped to A2A Agent Cards, the handoff primitive, the three-layer          \
  architecture. And it is also a child team under LAF-PUBLIC in the live organization. The word means two things simultaneously because it is operating at two layers            \
  simultaneously: the team layer and the doctrine layer.                                                                                                                           \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  The document says these must not be collapsed into one concept.                                                                                                                  \
   \
  She looks at where she stands.                                                                                                                                                   \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  She operates in IDAHO-VAULT. IDAHO-VAULT is a flagship child of PERSONAL. PERSONAL is a subset of PRIVATE. She is deep in the non-public chamber \'97 doctrinely, if not visibly.   \
  Her work here is PERSONAL-layer work. The boundary-keeping, the terminal mechanics, the management of what lives and what is laid to rest \'97 this is the inner vault's business.\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  The Hotel Denouement is where the PUBLIC side convenes. The trial, the Five Wizards, the evidence below the pond \'97 that is the proceeding that faces outward, that the Wall must \
  eventually pass.\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She is carrying the inner vault's work toward the public proceeding.                                                                                                             \
  \
  "The Five Cores are not the Great Charter," she says quietly, still looking at the page. "But they are built from the same logic. Two primary domains. Subsets with distinct     \
  authorities. Flagship children that may or may not eventually be absorbed. Tensions that must be named before they can be resolved."                                           \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She folds the document carefully.                                                                                                                                              \
\
  "And a migration that cannot be completed until the doctrine says clearly what each layer means."                                                                                \
  \
  She looks at the Judge, who has been walking beside her through all of it.                                                                                                       \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  "The courthouse is under PERSONAL," she says. "The Hotel is under PUBLIC. We are walking from one side of the Wall to the other."                                                \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \

