\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 "Let us leave behind the ashes and freakish ghosts of Caligari Carnival and continue on our way," he says. "One cannot get lost in fiction when the way is long to walk still."\cf2   \cb3 \
                                                                                                                                                                                  \

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  "Yes," she says simply.                                                                                                                                                          \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  She does not linger. The Carnival has given what it has. The ashes of Caligari are behind them \'97 the burning, the march, the two motions of the soul, Logan at sixteen with his  \
  hands on an instrument he loved. All of it received, filed, understood well enough to carry without being carried by it.\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  Fiction is a lens. The Judge has said it in his way. A lens is a tool. You use it to see and then you put it down and walk toward what you saw.                                  \
   \
  She falls into step beside him. The familiar rhythm. Two sets of footsteps on the hardscrabble road. The Judge's suitcase. Her bandolier. The Hotel somewhere ahead in the       \
  distance, organized by Dewey Decimal, waiting with its bells and its evidence and its Five Wizards and its unresolved trial.                                                   \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  The road is long.                                                                                                                                                              \
\
  The soul has many motions.                                                                                                                                                       \
   \
  She walks.                                                                                                                                                                       \
