\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 the landscape of the hinterlands has softened somewhat as they go \'97 from hardscrabble rock and twisted drought-stunted plants (aside from the apple tree at the roadside) have \cf2   \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 given way to low- growing grass... and a cone-and-needle bearing tree on the horizon up ahead. \cf2                                                                                   \cb3 \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  The Abhorsen notices the grass first.                                                                                                                                          \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  Not a dramatic arrival \'97 just the gradual softening underfoot, the hardscrabble giving way to something that holds moisture, something that had not given up on green. The       \
  twisted drought-plants thin and then are gone. The rock recedes. The road is easier now, and she realizes she has been walking hard without knowing it.                          \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She lifts her eyes to the horizon.                                                                                                                                               \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  A conifer.                                                                                                                                                                       \
\
  Not the apple tree, which bore fruit and enclosed its seed inside sweetness, which offered knowledge in a form you could hold and bite and swallow. This is something older. The \
  gymnosperm precedes the angiosperm by a hundred million years \'97 the naked seed in its cone, no fruit required, no sweetness as instrument of delivery. The conifer does not need\
  to be eaten to propagate. It simply is, season through season, shedding nothing it cannot afford to lose, holding its needles through winter while the deciduous world goes bare \
  and waits.                                                                                                                                                                     \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  The Tree of Knowledge was the apple. The fruit. The thing they already passed \'97 back there, at the roadside, before the python, before Newton.                                   \
  \
  She thinks of what God placed the cherubim to guard after the expulsion. Not the Tree of Knowledge \'97 they had already eaten from that. The other one. The one that was never     \
  forbidden before the Fall because they hadn't gotten to it yet, and became the reason for the expulsion once they had eaten the first.                                         \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  The Tree of Life.                                                                                                                                                              \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  You cannot have both. Knowledge and immortality together would make you, as the text says, like us. So they were put out. And the Tree of Life remained inside, guarded, waiting.\
  \
  She looks at the conifer on the horizon \'97 evergreen, cone-bearing, patient, ancient \'97 and thinks: we have been walking toward it.                                                \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  The landscape is changing. The hinterlands are releasing them. Something ahead is different from what came behind.                                                               \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  And very faintly \'97 so faint she might be imagining it, Mosrael-sensitive ears reaching for something that is not yet sound \'97 she thinks she hears the first suggestion of a      \
  wide-open western sky, the fanfare that has not yet been announced, the opening movement that has not yet played.                                                              \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  Not yet. But the land is beginning to lean toward it.                                                                                                                            \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \

