\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She has been quiet for a long time. Long enough that the hardscrabble is well behind them and the grass has taken hold beneath their feet and the conifer has grown from a smudge\
   on the horizon to something with a shape \'97 tall, solitary, deliberate.                                                                                                          \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  She looks at the tree. Then at the road. Then, finally, at the old man walking beside her.                                                                                       \
  \
  "Have you walked this far before?" she asks.                                                                                                                                     \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  Not what is that tree. Not what waits for us there. Not what will the Five Wizards require of me. Just: have you made this particular journey \'97 you, specifically, this old      \
  magistrate with his shined shoes and his well-worn Black's Law and his well-tended mustache \'97 have you walked to the Hotel Denouement before?\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She asks it quietly. Without urgency. The way one asks a thing they genuinely do not know the answer to, and have decided, at last, that not knowing is reason enough to ask.    \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \

