\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 the filtered light reflects of the polished leather of his shoes and suitcase\cf2                                                                                                     \cb3 \
\cb10                                                                                                                                                                                    \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 "I traveled to the City often as a young man, before the calling of the legal bar finally got its hooks in me..." he appears reminiscent of days gone by. \cf2                        \cb3 \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She watches the light move on the leather as he walks \'97 shoes, suitcase, the small shifting of a man in motion carrying something he packed deliberately. She had not looked at\
  the suitcase closely before. Now she does. It is old. Well-kept. It has made journeys.        \
\
  Often, he said. Not once. Not twice. Often, as a young man, before.                                                                                                              \
  \
  She understands the before. The hooks of the legal bar \'97 she has her own hooks. Fourteen of them, seven bells and their corresponding catches on the bandolier, things that found\
   her before she had a word for what she was becoming. You do not choose the hooks so much as you discover, one morning, that they are already in you and the question is only  \
  what you will do with that.                                                                                                                                                      \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  She does not fill the silence immediately.                                                                                                                                       \
  \
  The conifer is closer now. The suitcase catches another angle of Sophia's filtered grey.                                                                                         \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  "What did you go for," she asks, quietly, "before it claimed you?"                                                                                                               \
