\cb10   \cf11  to take over his role prior to his death and the transition was painless.[8] Kynes took on his father's mantle and served as both the planetary ecologist of Dune, and leader \cf2   \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 of the Fremen. He continued his father's vision of gradually terraforming the planet from a harsh desert world into a temperate world with precipitation, greenery, and open \cf2     \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 water. Compared to his father, Pardot Kynes, who almost entirely focused on the ecologic reformation of Dune and at times appeared to be tactless (though he was kind \cf2            \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 nonetheless), Liet-Kynes paid more attention to the Fremen and was overall significantly more Fremen and less single-minded than Pardot.\cf2                                          \cb3 \
