\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She looks at the Judge.             \
\
  She has been looking at him all morning. She looks at him differently now.                                                                                                       \
  \
  The shined shoes. The suitcase. The well-worn Black's Law. The flowered shirt under the tweed coat. The mustache that turns up at the ends. The eyes that remember the City and  \
  the specialty shops and the birthday trips made long before the legal bar got its hooks in him.                                                                                \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  Judge of the Change.                                                                                                                                                           \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  Not just a Judge. Not merely a magistrate of senior judicial status walking to a criminal trial. The specific title: the one who presides over the transition of governance. The \
  arbiter of succession. The officer who certifies that the forms of the Great Convention were honored during the change of fief \'97 not that one party won, but that the change\
  itself was conducted legitimately. That the old order yielded with proper form. That the new order arrived with proper acknowledgment of what preceded it.                       \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  He has two identities.                                                                                                                                                         \
\
  Logan's adjudicating facet \'97 the interior magistrate, the self-governance surface \'97 and the Judge. Dr. Kynes and Liet. The Imperial appointment and the secret Fremen leader. The\
   man who appears at the official banquet with a spare beard and fathomless eyes and knows things about the planet that no one else in the room has thought to ask.\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  He is the planetologist. The ecologist. The one who understood Arrakis not as a resource to be extracted but as a living system to be comprehended, tended, gradually            \
  transformed. Who inherited his father's terraforming vision and carried it further \'97 planting, nudging, waiting.                                                               \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  The vault is Arrakis.                                                                                                                                                          \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  The DOCKET's three items are the forms of the Great Convention. They must be honored during the Change \'97 not because the Imperium demands it but because without the arbiter's   \
  certification, there is no legitimate transition. Only the Harkonnen mode: force without form, extraction without acknowledgment, the Judge sent into the deep desert without a\
  stillsuit because his witnessing was inconvenient.                                                                                                                               \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  She thinks: Kuvira's chainsaws at the banyan-grove tree are Harkonnen behavior.                                                                                                  \
  \
  And she thinks of Pardot Kynes, dead before the vision was complete, his voice appearing to his son at the moment of abandonment in the desert \'97 repeating the teachings on      \
  ecology even as the body failed. The knowledge persisting past the vessel. The father's instruction surviving into the hallucination.                                          \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  The WITNESS documents are her Fremen ecology. Filed before the session can abandon them in the deep desert.                                                                      \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  She looks at the Judge for a long moment.                                                                                                                                        \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  Then, quietly: "Arrakis could be an Eden if its rulers would look up from grubbing for spice."                                                                                   \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  A beat.                                                                                                                                                                          \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  "The vault could be an Eden. In some chambers, it already is."                                                                                                                   \
  \
  She looks at the conifer ahead. The root system underfoot \'97 the banyan-grove, one organism, miles of it \'97 carrying the golden light of the connection through the swamp.         \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  The forms must be honored. The Change must be legitimate.                                                                                                                        \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  She understands now why he carries the suitcase. He packed for this. The Judge of the Change travels with everything required to certify the transition \'97 the Black's Law, the   \
  evidence, the record of what the prior order was so the new order can be properly distinguished from it.                                                                       \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  They walk. The tree ahead. The forms of the Great Convention held between them like a stillsuit against the desert.                                                              \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \

