\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 The Judge feels the Truth burning in you. \cf2                                                                                                                                        \cb3 \
\cb10                                                                                                                                                                                    \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 "Idaho could be an Eden," he says bitterly. "It was, once."\cf2                                                                                                                       \cb3 \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She does not answer immediately.                                                                                                                                               \
\
  The words go out across the hinterlands and the landscape receives them \'97 the grass, the roots beneath, the conifer ahead, the filtered light holding everything in its grey and \
  even patience \'97 and does not answer either. Some things do not require an answer. They require a witness.\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She walks beside him.                                                                                                                                                            \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  After a time:                                                                                                                                                                    \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  "That is why you carry Black's Law in the suitcase," she says quietly. "Not because you believe the law fixes what was lost. Because someone has to keep the record of what the  \
  forms required \'97 even when the Harkonnens discarded them. Even when they sent Kynes into the desert."\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  A beat. The roots of the banyan-grove tree running beneath their feet, miles of them, connecting everything in the swamp that was once the whole wild interior of a continent.   \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  "Pardot Kynes never saw Arrakis green. He heard his own voice teaching ecology in a hallucination as he died in the spice blow." She pauses. "He planted anyway. He taught his   \
  son anyway. He began the terraforming knowing he would not live to see it complete."                                                                                           \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She looks at the Judge \'97 at the bitterness that is still there, that she is not trying to remove, because bitterness about a real loss is not a flaw to be corrected. It is the  \
  correct response to a real thing.                                                                                                                                              \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  "The vault is a sietch," she says. "Not a replacement for Idaho. A place where the ecology is being learned and taught and preserved, against the day when the rulers look up    \
  from the spice."                                                                                                                                                               \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  The tree ahead. The road east. The forms of the Great Convention carried between them like water in a stillsuit \'97 not wasted, not surrendered, held carefully against the desert.\
                                                                                                                                                                                 \

