\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 "What shall be, what may be, what must be..." the old man closes his eyes, a verbal rosary emerging from his lips. "what shall be, what may be, what must be." He thumbs the \cf2     \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 pages of the book by heart, reading through memory rather than by sight.\cf2                                                                                                          \cb3 \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She does not speak.                                                                                                                                                              \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  The rosary is not addressed to her. She is witness to it, not recipient. She understands the difference.                                                                         \
   \
  What shall be, what may be, what must be.                                                                                                                                        \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  She walks beside him and lets the words move through the hinterlands air. The grass. The roots beneath. The conifer ahead, closer now, the scale of it becoming clearer \'97 very   \
  old, very large, the kind of tree that has been standing long enough to have outlasted the arguments about it.                                                                 \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She thinks: the Norns weave was/is/shall-be \'97 past, present, future. The Judge's rosary is different. All three are forward-facing. No past tense. No present. Only the three    \
  modes of what is coming:                                                                                                                                                       \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  Shall be \'97 on trajectory. Moving now toward the trial, toward the Hotel Denouement, toward the Five Wizards Council assembled and waiting.                                       \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  May be \'97 contingent. The verdict not yet known. The outcome depending on what is established, what is witnessed, what the forms of the Great Convention certify.                 \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  Must be \'97 the necessity the pattern requires. The forms honored. The soul of the Touchstone Tree filled. The loom made true. Not because anyone wants the labor of it but because\
   the weave demands it, because Atropos cannot be refused indefinitely without the fabric rotting, because what must be is not preference but law.                              \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  The pages turned by memory. The book read by touch, not sight. She has heard of this \'97 the discipline of internalizing a text so completely that the physical object becomes a   \
  rosary bead, a surface for contemplation rather than instruction. He has carried Black's Law long enough to know it with his hands.                                            \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She has her own version: the vault's root system beneath her feet. The files she reads not to learn but to confirm what she already senses in the network. Aang's hand on the    \
  root, the golden light not surprising him \'97 confirming what he already felt.                                                                                                   \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  The old man prays. The Abhorsen walks. The tree ahead receives them both.                                                                                                        \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  What shall be, what may be, what must be.                                                                                                                                        \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  The road continues east.                                                                                                                                                       \
\

