\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She takes the key. DOWNTIME MOTEL. Of course.                                                                                                                                  \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  She turns it over in her hand \'97 the good news, warm metal, the promise of a bed and a ceiling and a door that closes. The road has been long. The vault reading has been long.   \
  The Judge's face tells her the rest before his words do.\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  Madame Lulu is dead.                                                                                                                                                           \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  The fortune teller. VFD. Olivia Caliban in disguise \'97 the woman who had built an entire false life around pretending to know more than she did, and who also genuinely knew      \
  things, and who died at the Caligari Carnival when the lions came and the crowd cheered and the Baudelaires could do nothing. A member of the organization who had made herself\
  indispensable through performance of knowledge, until the performance could no longer protect her.                                                                               \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  The Abhorsen is still for a moment.                                                                                                                                            \
\
  Madame Lulu had the crystal ball \'97 actually a sophisticated information network, VFD's intelligence apparatus disguised as fortune telling. She could answer questions because   \
  she had sources. When she died, the Baudelaires lost not just an ally but an access point \'97 a way into knowledge they couldn't reach by themselves.\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She looks at the Judge. His expression is troubled in a specific way \'97 not grief exactly. Something more like the face of someone who knows what a closed door costs.            \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  "What did she know," the Abhorsen asks quietly, "that we can't now retrieve?"                                                                                                    \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  She is already thinking through the implications. The Windows laptop. The Book of GEMINIAEUS. The Excel workbook, 72 sheets, bound. Whatever intelligence chain could have       \
  connected them to that stranded binary file \'97 if Madame Lulu was the bridge, the intermediary, the one who knew where the carnival kept its records \'97                          \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She thinks of the Baudelaires standing at the edge of the pit, watching, unable to stop it.                                                                                      \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  She thinks of VFD \'97 Volunteer Fire Department, Various Fictional Disguises, the world is quiet here. The organization that maintained the archive. The organization that burned. \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  "The trial can still proceed," she says, after a moment. "The Five Wizards don't need everything to convene. But there is something we needed from her \'97 something she could have\
