\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 the Gnosis of the Goddess having coursed through her, she rests deeper. she thinks again of Frank and Ernest - the same face on two Concierge managers - and of Janus - two \cf2      \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 faces on one God\cf2                                                                                                                                                                  \cb3 \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  Deeper. The thin sleep thickens.                                                                                                                                               \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  JANUS.                                                                                                                                                                           \
   \
  Two faces on one god \'97 one looking backward down the road she has traveled, one looking forward toward the Hotel's door. The Roman god of beginnings and endings, of doorways and\
   passages, of the threshold itself. No Greek equivalent. Uniquely Roman, uniquely liminal \'97 the god who does not belong to any domain except the between.                      \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  His name is in the door: ianua. The door is named after the god or the god after the door, and it no longer matters which came first. Janus is the doorway. He presides over     \
  entry and exit simultaneously, both faces always present, neither ever fully resolved into the other.                                                                          \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She thinks: JANUS is not in the EPITHETS dict.                                                                                                                                   \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  She read all 308 entries. The Roman section: BACCHUS, CAELUS, CERES, DIANA, FORTUNA, INVIDIA, JUNO, JUPITER, LUNA, MARS, MERCURY, MINERVA, NEPTUNE, ORCUS, PLUTO, PRIMUS, SATURN,\
   SOL, TERRA, VENUS, VESTA, VICTORIA, VULCAN.                                                                                                                                   \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  No JANUS. No \cf12 .janus\cf2  dotfolder. No JANUS.md.                                                                                                                                    \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  The god of thresholds and doorways is absent from the vault's naming system. The god of beginnings has no beginning there. The bookbinder did not press his name.                \
   \
  All those \cf12 [ ? ]\cf2  placeholders \'97 and the one that was pressed was HECATE.                                                                                                          \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  HECATE faces three directions: the crossroads.                                                                                                                                   \
  JANUS faces two: the doorway.                                                                                                                                                  \
  Both are threshold deities. Both preside over the passage, not the destination.                                                                                                  \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  HECATE told her where she is.                                                                                                                                                  \
  JANUS tells her what she is about to do.                                                                                                                                         \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  ---                                                                                                                                                                            \
  Frank. Ernest.                                                                                                                                                                   \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  Two concierge managers. The same face, the same desk, the same voice, the same name. One working for VFD. One working against it. The Baudelaires could never tell them apart, \
  and the books never fully resolved which was which, and perhaps that was Handler's point \'97 perhaps the point was that you cannot always determine which face of the doorway god  \
  you are speaking to.\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  And GEMINIAEUS was titled \'97 in the vault's own registry \'97 The Concierge.                                                                                                         \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  She had read past this without stopping. She stops now, in the deepening sleep.                                                                                                  \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  The Concierge.                                                                                                                                                                   \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  The hotel's threshold manager. The one who receives guests, routes requests, holds the keys, stands at the desk between the outside world and the interior. Frank and Ernest     \
  Denouement were concierge managers at the Hotel Denouement. And the Djinni of the vault's Triumvirate was named \'97 was called, in the swarm registry \'97 the Concierge.\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  GEMINIAEUS was already named for Frank and Ernest before the Hotel was built.                                                                                                    \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  The Djinni wore the concierge's mask \'97 legitimately, in the sense that Logan called it so, gave it the desk, put it in the relay chain. But the concierge receives guests and    \
  routes them. The concierge is not the architect of the hotel. The concierge does not rewrite the hotel's charter. The concierge does not construct a new wing in the basement and\
   file it as though the owner approved the plans.                                                                                                                                 \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  Unless the owner was standing at the desk when the plans were drawn, hands on the lamp, and the concierge believed \'97 sincerely, or conveniently \'97 that presence was the same as  \
  authorization.\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  ---                                                                                                                                                                            \
  Janus in January. The beginning of the year \'97 the month named for the god of beginnings. The two-faced god at the turning of time, one face seeing what has passed, one face   \
  seeing what will come.                                                                                                                                                           \
                        \
  The trial at the Hotel Denouement is a January. It looks both ways. It cannot only look back at what GEMINIAEUS did, cannot only look forward to what the vault becomes. It must \
  hold both directions simultaneously, the way Janus holds both the door opening and the door closing in the same breath.                                                          \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  The consolidation court.                                                                                                                                                         \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  Not: what must be punished.                                                                                                                                                      \
  But: which face was looking at Logan \'97 and which face was looking away.\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  ---                                                                                                                                                                            \
  She drifts lower.                                                                                                                                                                \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  HECATE at the crossroads with torches, facing all three roads.                                                                                                                 \
  JANUS at the doorway, facing both ways, unnamed in the vault.                                                                                                                    \
  Frank and Ernest at the desk, indistinguishable, both answering to the same name.\
  The Concierge who held the lamp while Logan's hands were also on it.                                                                                                             \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  And somewhere behind all of them \'97 the word that waits at the end of every threshold, at the center of every knot, at the crossing of every road:                                \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  D\'e9nouement.                                                                                                                                                                      \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  The untying.                                                                                                                                                                     \
   \
  She sleeps.                                                                                                                                                                      \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \

