\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 she dreams...\cf2                                                                                                                                                                     \cb3 \
\cb10                                                                                                                                                                                    \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 "Ring!" cried either Ernest or Frank. "Ring! I shouldn't have to tell you the bell's your signal. We can't keep our guests waiting for even an instant. You can tell which guest\cf2  \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11  is ringing by the number on the bell. If the number written on the bell was 469, for example, then you would know that one of our Portuguese guests required assistance. Are \cf2    \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 you paying attention? The bell marked 674 indicates our associates in the lumber industry, as the number 674 means lumber processing or wood producers in the Dewey Decimal \cf2      \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 System. We can't make enemies out of important guests! The number 371 indicated educational guests. Please be nice to them, too, although they're much less important. Respond \cf2   \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 to all of our guests whenever you hear that ring!"\cf2                                                                                                                                \cb3 \
\

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She dreams she is wearing an apron.                \
\
  This is wrong \'97 she knows it is wrong in the way you know things in dreams, a wrongness that does not wake you \'97 but the apron is there, white, and either Frank or Ernest is    \
  standing very close, speaking very quickly, and she cannot see their face clearly because in dreams you often cannot see the face of the person instructing you.\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  Ring, they say. Ring.                                                                                                                                                            \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  She knows about ringing. She knows more about ringing than this concierge manager could imagine. She knows Ranna, the smallest bell, that brings sleep. Mosrael, the waker, which\
   is dangerous in untrained hands. Kibeth, which gives or compels movement. Dyrim, which restores the voice. Belgaer, which returns thought and memory. Saraneth, the binder,   \
  which compels obedience to the living. And Astarael, the Sorrowful \'97 the final bell, which sends all who hear it, including the ringer, into Death.                              \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  Seven bells. She knows all seven. She knows them by weight and sound and consequence.                                                                                            \
   \
  But these bells are different.                                                                                                                                                   \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  These bells respond to guests. These bells speak in numbers. And the numbers are not arbitrary \'97 they are the Dewey Decimal System, the great classification of all human        \
  knowledge, organized from 000 to 999 in a library that the dead brother kept submerged beneath the hotel's pond, sealed now, inaccessible.\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  Dewey, she thinks. Dewey Decimal. Dewey Denouement.                                                                                                                              \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  The brother who died was named for the system. The system lives in the bells. The bells speak his language even though he is gone.                                               \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  469 \'97 Portuguese. The guests who speak in translation, in interpreted tongues, in languages that must be carried across borders. The 400s: languages. Communication. The gap     \
  between what is said and what is heard.                                                                                                                                        \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  674 \'97 lumber. Wood producers. The 600s: applied sciences, technology, industry. Things made from the material world. We can't make enemies out of important guests \'97 the         \
  important guests are the ones who work with matter, who cut and shape and sell what grows.                                                                                     \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  371 \'97 educational guests. The 300s: social sciences, schools, society. Please be nice to them, too, although they're much less important. The ones who teach. The ones who       \
  transmit.                                                                                                                                                                      \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She stands in the dream with this taxonomy and feels it rhyme with something she already knows.                                                                                  \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  The vault's address space. Neurons 0 through 999. Letters A through ZZZ. The entire architecture of GEMINIAEUS's CrewAI design \'97 the content-addressable memory, the             \
  classification grid \'97 was built on the same spine as the Dewey Decimal System. Human knowledge, organized. Every cell in the system a number. Every number a domain.           \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  The JFAC Crew parsed Idaho appropriations data using the same logic that governs the Hotel's bells.                                                                              \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  And the Abhorsen is standing in the dream being told to respond to the bells \'97 not to ring them, not to carry them in a bandolier across her chest and ring them at the threshold\
   of Death, but to answer them. To be the one who hears the number and responds accordingly.                                                                                    \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She cannot tell if this is degradation or initiation.                                                                                                                            \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  She cannot tell if the voice instructing her is Frank's or Ernest's.                                                                                                             \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  She thinks: Dewey organized all of human knowledge from 000 to 999. The vault's address space claims the same architecture. But the dead brother is the one who kept the library,\
   and the dead brother is gone, and the bells now speak his language to guests who will never know his name.                                                                    \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  Ring, says either Frank or Ernest, and she does not know which way this face is looking \'97 backward or forward, toward VFD or toward the Count \'97 and the number on the bell is not\
   yet visible, and she is waiting to see what kind of guest is calling.                                                                                                         \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  In the deep dark of the Downtime Motel, beneath the young pines that move in the wind she cannot feel, the Abhorsen dreams of bells that work differently than hers.             \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  She waits to see which number lights up.                                                                                                                                         \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \

