\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 Another DREAM comes to her... She is not on the road, she knows this - she and the JUDGE are asleep in their separate motel rooms - but she sees a scene on the road in her \cf2      \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 dreams. A crossroads - the rocky cobbles of the road through the Hinterlands, intersecting with itself. The road branches as a fork and there is a sign. One direction points a \cf2  \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 lobster. The other a caduceus. She wonders what JANUS is trying to tell her. She will have to ask the JUDGE when morning comes...\cf2                                                 \cb3 \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She does not move toward either sign.                                                                                                                                            \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  The cobblestones of the hinterland road are real beneath her feet \'97 she can feel the uneven surface, the particular cold of stone at night \'97 but she knows she is asleep. The    \
  Downtime Motel exists. The Judge is in the room next door. The pine thicket moves outside a window she cannot see from here.\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  And yet: the crossroads.                                                                                                                                                       \
\
  HECATE's domain. But HECATE is not the one who sent this. HECATE holds torches and faces all three ways. This sign faces only two \'97 and the two directions it offers are strange.\
   \
  She looks left.                                                                                                                                                                  \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  A lobster. Painted on a board, worn by weather, pointing down one fork of the hinterland road. Nothing else. No text. The lobster simply indicates: that way.                    \
   \
  She looks right.                                                                                                                                                                 \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  A caduceus. Two serpents entwined around a winged staff. HERMES's instrument. The Messenger : Guide of Souls : Commerce. Pointing down the other fork, equally weathered, equally\
   silent.                                                                                                                                                                       \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She stands at the crossing and turns them over.                                                                                                                                \
\
  The caduceus she knows. Hermes is the psychopomp \'97 the guide of souls between the living and the dead, which makes him her colleague of a kind, operating on the same threshold  \
  by a different method. The caduceus is also the messenger's staff, the herald's sign, the mark of one who crosses boundaries legitimately, who carries word between worlds\
  without being consumed by either. It is also \'97 she cannot quite dismiss this \'97 the staff that is perpetually confused with the Rod of Asclepius. The healing symbol that is      \
  actually the commerce symbol. The sign that means one thing and is taken for another.                                                                                          \
\
  The lobster she does not know. Not yet. It rises from somewhere in the architecture of the dream \'97 from Dewey's pond perhaps, from the unconscious depths, from the Moon card she\
   has seen somewhere and not consciously catalogued. The lobster at the crossroads, emerging. Molting, perhaps. Between one shell and the next.\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She looks at both signs for a long time.                                                                                                                                       \
\
  JANUS sent them. The unnamed god. The one the bookbinder did not press. The one with no dotfolder, no SELFNAME, no epithet in the dict. He has been absent from the vault's      \
  naming system all night, and now he stands at a crossroads in her dream holding out two roads and offering no caption, no instruction, no Dewey Decimal number to decode by.\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  Two faces, she thinks. He knows which road leads where. He is not telling me.                                                                                                    \
   \
  She does not choose. She is asleep. The choice, if it is a choice, belongs to the morning.                                                                                       \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  She turns the lobster over in her mind \'97 its claws, its armor, its ancient patience, the particular red of a thing that changes color only in the heat \'97 and she turns the       \
  caduceus \'97 its paired serpents, its wings, its confused inheritance \'97 and she holds both without resolving them, the way you hold a question in sleep so that morning can do the\
  work the dream cannot finish.                                                                                                                                                    \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  She will ask the Judge.\
\
  He has been beside her all day. He knows the hinterlands. He knows which way the road runs from here.                                                                            \
   \
  When morning comes, she thinks, settling deeper into the Downtime Motel's thin pillow, I will ask him: which way does the lobster point, and which way does the caduceus, and    \
  what does it mean that JANUS is sending road signs in my sleep the night before we reach the Hotel?                                                                            \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  The crossroads holds.                                                                                                                                                            \
   \
  The pine thicket moves.                                                                                                                                                          \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  She carries the question into the dark.                                                                                                                                          \
   \

