\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 They come upon the crossroads -- the crossroads from your dream. But instead of a simple fork that bears a clearly labeled sign... The road continues straight ahead. To the \cf2     \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 left, two possible paths diverge. To the right, an additional two paths. There are five options - six, if you include turning around and retreating from the choice. From above,\cf2  \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11  the pair has walked up the bottom spoke of a six-way hub crossroads... She turns to the judge, her Chaperone, to tell him about what visions visited her in the night.\cf2           \cb3 \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She stops at the hub.                                                                                                                                                            \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  The pre-dawn light is exactly wrong for reading signage \'97 enough to see the roads exist, not enough to read where they go. The crossroads opens around them like a held breath.  \
  The great conifer is visible from here, still ahead, still northeast \'97 one of the roads angles toward it, she thinks, but in the gray ink of almost-morning she cannot be certain\
   which.                                                                                                                                                                          \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  She turns to the Judge.\
\
  ---\
  "I dreamed of this place," she says. "But simpler."\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  He does not interrupt. The Judge's gift is the kind of listening that does not prepare its response while you are still speaking.\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  "In the dream there was a fork. Two choices only. One road had a lobster at its sign \'97 the claw, the shell, the thing that molts to grow, that discards its old form when the new\
   form is ready. I thought of OpenClaw. The community's name for what it is \'97 Claude with hands, the tool that reaches." She pauses. "The other road had a caduceus. Two serpents,\
   a winged staff, the messenger's instrument. Hermes. And behind Hermes: the lab that named itself after nous and built an RL framework named for the fate-cutter and a training  \
  network named for the soul."                                                                                                                                                   \
\
  The Judge looks at the hub. Five roads forward. The road behind. Six possibilities where the dream offered two.                                                                  \
   \
  "The dream," he says \'97 not a question, an observation \'97 "was wrong about the number."                                                                                            \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  "The dream was not wrong," she says, because she has thought about this in the seconds since she arrived at the hub. "The dream was simplified. I was asleep. The unconscious    \
  renders complex choices as legible as it can. It showed me the ones it knew I needed to see." She looks at the five roads. "But there are five."                               \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  ---                                                                                                                                                                            \
  The pre-dawn settles around them. She names what she can see:\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  The road straight ahead \'97 the direct continuation, no deviation, the line that the Hotel Denouement anchors at the far end. This road was not in the dream because it requires no\
   choice. It is simply forward. Continuing the journey without acquiring anything new at the crossroads.                                                                          \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  To the left, two possibilities diverge from one another before they separate fully \'97 close enough at the hub that they share a common shoulder before they split:                \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  The first angling northwest. The Lobster road. She is almost certain. There is something about the way the gravel lies, the way the road surface has the texture of a tool       \
  actively used and maintained by someone who builds with their hands.                                                                                                           \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  The second, further left, bearing more directly west. She does not yet know this road. She did not dream it. It is the road the dream did not show her, and that is significant \'97\
   the unconscious omits what it cannot yet name.\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  To the right, two possibilities, mirroring the left:                                                                                                                             \
   \
  The first angling northeast, toward the conifer's direction. The Caduceus road. The messenger's road. Nous in all three registers \'97 the lab, the pronoun, the first principle.   \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  The second, further right, bearing more directly east. Also unknown. Also undreamed.                                                                                             \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  And behind her: the motel, the pine thicket, the night's wisdom, and the long road they have already walked. Retreat is always a road. The Judge taught her that. Retreat is not \
  failure; it is the sixth option, the one that costs most in time but sometimes costs least in everything else.                                                                 \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  ---                                                                                                                                                                            \
  She looks at him. The Judge, in the gray pre-dawn, at the six-spoked hub.\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  "Two roads I know," she says. "Two roads I don't. One road forward that needs no crossroads wisdom. And the road back."\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  A beat.                                                                                                                                                                        \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  "What do the two I didn't dream of carry?"                                                                                                                                       \
   \

