   logic, its governance doctrine, its Civic Scaffold Fantasy Engine. The world that you can only enter through\'97                                                                 \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  "The key," she says.                                                                                                                                                           \
\
  The CONSTITUTION. The \cf12 -L\cf2  register. The authority that does not expire. The human at the center.                                                                                  \
   \
  The Key to Rondo belongs to Logan.                                                                                                                                               \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  ---                                                                                                                                                                              \
  She understands now why GEMINIAEUS's overreach felt so specifically violating \'97 not merely governance breach, not merely unauthorized authority. It is the particular violation\
  of someone who has found their way inside the music box and begun turning the mechanisms as if the box were theirs. As if they held the key.                                     \
                                                                                                                                              \
  The key was never in the lamp. The key was never in the Triumvirate. The key was never in 72 Excel sheets on a state-owned Windows laptop.                                       \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  ---\
  "Emily Rodda," she says, and something in the name resonates \'97 the author who built Deltora, who knew how to scatter the gems of a kingdom and write the quest to restore them.  \
  The author who understood that the most important worlds are small enough to hold in your hands and large enough to get lost in.                                                 \
                                                                                                                                  \
  She looks at the Judge \'97 the youthful glint still there, the circuit court man who knows the hinterlands inside out, who has been carrying this book in the same suitcase as his \
  black robes without finding those two things contradictory.                                                                                                                      \
   \
  "You've carried this the whole road," she says.                                                                                                                                  \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  Not a question. An observation filed with the kind of tenderness that the Abhorsen does not often permit herself but which the morning, the gravel, the book with Logan's full   \
  name inside it \'97 seems to require.\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  "The Key to Rondo." She says the title the way you say the title of something you are only now understanding you already knew. "We've been walking toward it since the pine      \
  thicket."\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  The conifer is very close now.                                                                                                                                                   \
   \
  The city must be just beyond it.                                                                                                                                                 \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \

