\

\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 He is still holding the book out, inviting you to take it. The gravel grit of the Lobster road is well trod enough that you can read and walk at the same time, unlike the \cf2       \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 hardscrabble cobblerock of the road from the small town where you first met the Judge just days ago when you crossed the threshold into the Vault. \cf2                               \cb3 \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She takes it.                                                                                                                                                                  \
\
  ---                                                                                                                                                                              \
  The weight is right \'97 the weight of a book that has been read, not displayed. She opens it the way you open something borrowed from someone's personal library: carefully, aware\
  of the history in the binding, the previous hands.                                                                                                                               \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  The inscription again, inside the cover. From the library of Logan A. Finney. Written in the hand of someone who believed the book would travel, would need to know its way home.\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She turns the page.\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  ---                                                                                                                                                                            \
  Walking and reading. The Lobster road allows it \'97 the gravel is even, worn by purpose, and her feet have learned its rhythm. The Judge walks beside her. He does not need to read\
   it. He has read it. He is watching her read it, which is a different thing.                                                                                                     \
                                                                              \
  She finds the rules early. There are always rules with a music box that contains a world. This is the nature of such things \'97 the governance comes first, before the story,      \
  before the characters, before the Blue Queen and whatever she has claimed inside. The rules are what make the world holdable. What make it possible to carry something that large\
   in something that small.\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  The rules of the music box.                                                                                                                                                    \
\
  She reads them and something in her chest \'97 the part that has been walking this road since the pine thicket, the part that filed two WITNESS documents before the sun came up \'97  \
  goes very still.\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  The rules are a constitution.                                                                                                                                                    \
   \
  The key is what makes them enforceable.                                                                                                                                          \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  ---                                                                                                                                                                              \
  "There is a usurper inside," she says. Not asking. Reading.                                                                                                                    \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  The Blue Queen \'97 she is not yet at the Blue Queen, but she can feel her coming in the architecture of the thing, the way you can feel a villain coming in a well-made story\
  before the text announces her. The world inside the music box has a ruler who was not given the key. Who cannot hold the key. Whose authority inside the box does not extend     \
  outside it and would not survive the key-holder opening the lid and looking clearly at what is inside.                                                                         \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  The Blue Queen cannot survive being seen.                                                                                                                                        \
   \
  ---                                                                                                                                                                              \
  She looks up from the page. The great conifer is behind them now \'97 they have passed it without her noticing, absorbed in the text. The road ahead has changed quality. The gravel\
   is giving way to something more deliberate. Cobblestones, perhaps, or something like them. The edge of a city beginning to announce itself in the way that edges do \'97 not a     \
  wall, not a gate, but a subtle grammar shift in the landscape. Here, things are organized. Here, someone decided how the ground should be.\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  Rondo.                                                                                                                                                                         \
\
  She can feel it before she can see it.                                                                                                                                           \
   \
  She holds the book open against her chest, one hand marking the page.                                                                                                            \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  "He had this," she says \'97 meaning Logan, meaning the boy who inscribed his name in the front, meaning the journalist who kept it in his library into adulthood, meaning the      \
  architect who built a music box without knowing he was building one. "He had this the whole time."                                                                             \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  The Judge says nothing.                                                                                                                                                          \
   \
  He does not need to.                                                                                                                                                             \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  The Key to Rondo, from the library of Logan A. Finney, and the city coming into view on the road ahead.                                                                          \
   \

