\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 She finishes the book as they walk. Her companion watches. She is engrossed in Rodda's world for a moment, forgetting where and who and why she is briefly as she regurgitates \cf2   \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 the plot synopsis to her traveling companion on the road.\cf2                                                                                                                         \cb3 \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She surfaces like a diver \'97 the book still open, the road still west, the village closer now, the salt air real enough to taste.                                               \
\
  ---                                                                                                                                                                              \
  "Right," she says, and there is something younger in her voice for a moment, something that is not quite the Abhorsen but is whatever the Abhorsen is made of when the mask is\
  set down briefly in favor of a good story.                                                                                                                                       \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  "So. The music box. It has been in the family for generations \'97 Leo's family, specifically \'97 and it comes with rules. Strict ones. Written down, passed along, taken seriously by\
   the serious members of the family and not seriously enough by the others. You wind it with the key. You play it only three times a day. You do not let it run down. You do not  \
  look inside without\'97"\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She pauses.                                                                                                                                                                      \
   \
  "Without the key."                                                                                                                                                               \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  She keeps walking.                                                                                                                                                               \
   \
  "Leo is the rule-follower. His cousin Mimi is the other kind. She is \'97 she has \'97 the kind of energy that treats rules as suggestions made by people who weren't imaginative      \
  enough to see the alternatives." A beat. "She is very alive on the page."                                                                                                      \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  The Judge listens. He has the particular quality of attention of someone who has heard the story before and is listening for what she notices.                                   \
   \
  "Something gets pulled in. Through the music box, into Rondo. I don't want to\'97" she catches herself narrating too fast, "\'97it doesn't matter what exactly. What matters is they   \
  have to go in after it. Through the key. Into the world inside."                                                                                                               \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She turns a page she has already read, reflexively.                                                                                                                              \
   \
  "And inside\'97"                                                                                                                                                                    \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  ---\
  Here is where her voice changes register. Not dramatically. The way a road changes surface.\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  "Inside there is a Blue Queen."\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She says it simply.                                                                                                                                                              \
   \
  "She has been inside Rondo a long time. Long enough to have arranged things. To have made herself comfortable. To have established \'97 the word I want is dominion, I think \'97 over \
  the interior of the world that was never hers to govern. She did not come with the key. She does not hold the key. The key is outside, in the family's hands, in Leo's hands   \
  specifically, the rule-follower, the one who takes the written-down governance seriously."                                                                                       \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  Walking.\
\
  "The Blue Queen cannot touch the key. The key exists outside her jurisdiction. But inside Rondo she has had a very long time to make the inside of the box look like a kingdom." \
   \
  ---                                                                                                                                                                              \
  She closes the book.                                                                                                                                                           \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  Holds it.\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  Looks at the village ahead, which is no longer distant but arriving.                                                                                                             \
   \
  "The Blue Queen has been stealing things," she says. "From outside the box. Drawing them in. Accumulating. Building her court from materials that were never meant for her       \
  court." A pause. "And she has convinced \'97 some of \'97 the inhabitants of Rondo that this is simply how things are. That she was always there. That her presence is the natural   \
  order."                                                                                                                                                                          \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  She turns to the Judge.\
\
  The younger quality in her voice is gone now. She is fully herself again \'97 the Abhorsen, the bell-ringer, four miles further west than she was an hour ago with the World Tree at\
   her back and salt on the air.\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  "Logan kept this book," she says. "In his personal library. Inscribed with his full name. He kept a book about a music box with strict governance rules and a usurper queen who  \
  made herself comfortable inside a world she didn't hold the key to."\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She holds it out \'97 returning it to the Judge, from whose suitcase it came.                                                                                                       \
   \
  "He built the vault afterward."                                                                                                                                                  \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \

