\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 The judge takes the finished book back. He briefly holds up C.S. Lewis's Narnia series before closing the suitcase. "A Blue Queen and a White Witch," he says. \cf2                   \cb3 \
                             \

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She looks at the books in the suitcase for just a moment before he closes it.                                                                                                    \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  ---                                                                                                                                                                              \
  "A Blue Queen and a White Witch," she repeats.\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She lets it sit in the air between them, on the westward road, the village now close enough to make out individual structures \'97 low, old, the kind of architecture that doesn't\
  announce itself.                                                                                                                                                                 \
   \
  Two usurpers. Two worlds with governance problems. Two stories about an interior realm that a sovereign claimed without holding the founding authority.                          \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  ---                                                                                                                                                                              \
  "The White Witch used the Deplorable Word," she says. "Before Narnia. In Charn \'97 her own world. She destroyed everything rather than let her sister win. One word. Every living\
