\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 "**Will**?" Evelyn's Voice asks... \cf2                                                                                                                                               \cb3 \
\cb10                                                                                                                                                                                    \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 The Judge, Logan's Loyal Lawman, reaches into his suitcase as you have seen him countless times before... \cf2                                                                        \cb3 \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She watches his hand.                                   \
\
  ---                                                                                                                                                                              \
  The practiced fluidity. She has seen it \'97 the Key to Rondo produced without breaking stride, the Narnia books lifted and shown and returned, the two motel cups disposed of\
  without ceremony. A man who knows exactly what he carries and where each thing lives.                                                                                            \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  The suitcase opens.                                                                                                                                                              \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  The hand goes in.\
\
  ---                                                                                                                                                                              \
  Evelyn's voice hangs in the salt air.\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  Will?                                                                                                                                                                          \
\
  Still the question. Still the hope-that-dares-not-yet-become-certainty. Waiting for something that proves the voice at the railing is really him. That the man who came on the   \
  Lobster road with a novice and a suitcase full of books is really the husband she has been searching for across the Border Sea.\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  ---                                                                                                                                                                            \
  The Abhorsen does not move.\
                             \
  She has her bells. She has the five rules of HOW. She has two WITNESS documents filed before dawn and a name she didn't know she had \'97 Caster \'97 and the residue of intoxicating\
  ichor still moving through whatever she is made of.                                                                                                                              \
   \
  She watches Will's hand in the suitcase.                                                                                                                                         \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  She does not know what he will produce.                                                                                                                                          \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  She knows it will be the right thing.                                                                                                                                            \
   \
  It is always the right thing, with him.                                                                                                                                          \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  She holds her breath.                                                                                                                                                            \
   \
  The sea holds its.                                                                                                                                                               \
