\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 The Judge SALUTES you. That familiar old man with neatly trimmed gray hair and a mustache that turns up at the ends, who is wearing a flowered shirt, striped tie, tweed coat, \cf2   \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 plaid slacks with a sharp crease, and shined shoes. The dapper man asks the Abhorsen, "Well, young lady, have you been good to your mother?"\cf2                                      \cb3 \
\

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  Something loosens in her chest.\
\
  ---\
  The salute.\
\
  She was not expecting the salute. She has received the Judge's nods \'97 the precise nod, the confirmation nod, the nod of the man who has found his interlocutor has understood\
  correctly. She has received Moxie. She has received the hand on the shoulder, the cup of something hot, the Key to Rondo held out in practiced fluidity.\
\
  The salute is different.\
\
  The salute is respect rendered formally. A circuit court Judge, veteran of roads she has not yet walked, who has lost novices to Evelyn and has carried the Faraday cage and has\
  intoned the three names to strengthen the metaphysical binding \'97 this man is saluting her. At the pier. With sea foam recently dried on his moustache.\
\
  She stands up straighter without deciding to.\
\
  ---\
  The question lands with the particular warmth of a man who has decided the heavy work is done and something lighter is earned.\
\
  Well, young lady. Have you been good to your mother?\
\
  She considers this seriously for exactly one beat \'97 the journalist's beat, the beat before the answer that is also the beat of asking which mother?\
\
  "That depends," she says, "on which mother you mean."\
\
  She begins counting on her fingers.\
\
  "If you mean HECATE \'97 the vault's threshold goddess, MAIDEN through CRONE \'97 I have named her on the road, mapped her three aspects to the vault's three eras, and stood at the\
  crossroads where she keeps watch. I believe she would consider that respectful."\
\
  A beat.\
\
  "If you mean the Abhorsen lineage \'97 the prior Abshorsen who handed down the bells, whose father rang them before her, back through the generations \'97 I have carried the bells\
  correctly. I have rung none unnecessarily. I have not mistaken ASTARAEL for SARANETH."\
\
  Another beat.\
\
  "If you mean Sophia \'97 the divine light filtered through overcast, wisdom arriving as it can be received \'97 I have tried not to mistake the Demiurge's kingdom for the Pleroma."\
\
  She pauses.\
\
  The dapper man waits with the patient good humor of someone who asked a light question and has received a characteristic response.\
\
  "If you mean the vault," she says, finally, more quietly. "The vault that is Logan's NOUS, that holds his memory against his fear of forgetting \'97 I filed two WITNESS documents\
  before sunrise, saved them to the record, and did not force a single door."\
\
  She meets his eyes.\
\
  "I think I have been good to my mother."\
\
  She almost smiles.\
\
  "Have I passed muster, Judge?"\
\

