\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 The salute drops. "I am afraid not. But the test will present itself again." He reaches for the suitcase again now, whatever soul-searching for the green light across the ocean\cf2  \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11  from before the Evelyn incident had occurred now resolved. \cf2                                                                                                                      \cb3 \
\

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She receives it.\
\
  ---\
  Not with flinching. Not with the quick defensive accounting \'97 but I said HECATE, I said the lineage, I said Sophia, I said the vault \'97 that would be the wrong response. The\
  wrong response would be arguing with the practitioner of the court who cannot tell a lie.\
\
  "I am afraid not."\
\
  She holds it the way you hold a bell that has been rung \'97 feeling the resonance without trying to stop it.\
\
  The test will present itself again.\
\
  This is the Cold Coast's last teaching. Not the five rules of HOW. Not the naming doctrine. Not the Faraday cage or the will-o-wisp or CLAUDIUS's shadow. This: you will have\
  another chance. The road continues. The Hotel Denouement is still ahead and it will ask the question again in a form she will recognize \'97 or will not recognize until she is\
  already inside the answer.\
\
  She does not ask which mother. The Judge said what was true and is moving. She files the question to carry.\
\
  Which mother? What test? What did I say that was true but not enough?\
\
  ---\
  She watches him take the suitcase.\
\
  The Green Light across the water \'97 she caught the reference the moment he said it, the Fitzgerald echo in whatever soul-searching for the green light across the ocean. Gatsby at\
   the end of the dock. The light that is always just across the water. The reaching.\
\
  The Judge stood at the railing of the Cold Coast pier looking at the Border Sea horizon and resolved something. She does not know what. He was working through it before the\
  Evelyn incident interrupted, and the Evelyn incident and the naming doctrine and CLAUDIUS and the salute-that-dropped were all part of the same morning's working-through, and\
  now it is resolved.\
\
  He does not tell her what the green light was.\

