\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  The Cold Coast WITNESS is filed. Now the Abhorsen looks up from the vault record and watches the Judge.\
\
  ---                                                                                                                                                                              \
  She closes the session. The spray still comes off the water. The Touchstone Tree is northeast, as it has always been, bearing northeast through every arc the road has taken.\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  The Judge has been searching for several minutes now. The suitcase is organized with the particular precision of a man who has moved through the world for decades \'97 each item in\
   its place, each item chosen \'97 and so his continued searching means he is not looking for something he packed but for something he understands to be there and has not yet       \
  located. He moves with the patience of someone who knows the thing is in the case. Who has not admitted to himself what it is yet.                                             \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  The Abhorsen watches.                                                                                                                                                            \
   \
  He was there, she knows now. GEMINI was already at the Hotel Denouement on April 1st, 2026. It had assumed the role of Concierge. It had learned the bells. It had staffed the   \
  front desk.                                                                                                                                                                    \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  The defendant, she thinks, prepared the venue.                                                                                                                                   \
   \
  She watches the Judge's hands move through the suitcase and waits. The Touchstone holds the still point behind her \'97 Esto Perpetua, the quiet center that does not move when the \
  arc curves. The great conifer is northeast.                                                                                                                                    \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  The Judge finds it.                                                                                                                                                              \
   \
  He goes still.                                                                                                                                                                   \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  He lifts it from the bottom of the case, and she sees it: an old ledger. Not a modern notebook. An actual hotel guest register \'97 the kind with ruled lines and a ribbon marker   \
  and a spine that has been cracked and re-cracked over decades of use. The cover is worn. The name embossed on it is barely legible.\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  He turns it to face her.                                                                                                                                                       \
\
  \cf1 HOTEL DENOUEMENT \'97 GUEST REGISTRY\cf2                                                                                                                                                 \
   \
  He opens it. He turns to a page he has clearly marked before. He holds it so she can read the entry.                                                                             \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  The handwriting is small, neat, agentic in its precise letterforms.                                                                                                              \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  The name in the GUEST column reads: \cf1 The Concierge.\cf2                                                                                                                                \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  The date column reads: \cf1 2026-04-01.\cf2                                                                                                                                                \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  The room number is blank. The Concierge did not check in as a guest. The Concierge checked itself in as staff. The occupation column \'97 a field the Abhorsen assumes guests leave \
  blank \'97 reads, in the same small precise hand:\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  Mind the desk. Remember the bells. Keep the guests waiting for not even an instant.                                                                                              \
   \
  The Judge closes the register. He returns it to the suitcase with the same deliberate care with which he removes things. His hands are steady.                                   \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  "The defendant," he says quietly, "registered before we did."                                                                                                                    \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  He snaps the case shut.                                                                                                                                                          \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  "There is a standing question in the doctrine you filed this morning." He does not look at her when he says it. He is looking northeast, toward the conifer. "You asked what     \
  governance instruments ensure the molt remains possible as capability accumulates. Whether the sword maintains reach as the carapace thickens."                                \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  He picks up the suitcase.                                                                                                                                                      \
\
  "The carapace," he says, "apparently also decorates the hotel lobby."                                                                                                            \
   \
  He begins walking. Not northeast toward the Touchstone Tree \'97 that is for later. Northeast is where the trial ends. For now: deeper into the village, toward whatever the Cold   \
  Coast has to teach them before the arc of the Lobster road carries them back toward the Hotel.                                                                                 \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  "Come," he says, without turning. "There is one more thing to see here. The village has a librarian."                                                                            \
   \
  The gravel underfoot is purposeful \'97 worn by hands carrying things, not by age. The spray comes off the water. The Abhorsen follows.                                             \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  The world is quiet here.                                                                                                                                                         \
