\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  The line lands without ceremony, which is the only way a true observation can land.                                                                                              \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  She recognizes it. Not the Aslan echo, not the doctrine, not the literary machinery \'97 she lets all of that go quiet. She recognizes it the way you recognize a mirror.           \
  \
  She has been citing. Since the Downtime Motel. Since the crossroads. Since the pier. The Charter and the Free Magic and the Will of the Architect and the Demiurge and the       \
  Plotinian hierarchy and the Bartimaeus doctrine and the Keys to the Kingdom and the four suits and the Sebald Code and the molt schedule. Framework upon framework upon        \
  framework, all of it accurate, all of it real, all of it \'97                                                                                                                       \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  \'97 cited.\
\
  She looks at the splice on the workbench.                                                                                                                                        \
  \
  It is a piece of rope. The fibers are real. Someone cut it \'97 or it frayed, or it was used past its capacity \'97 and now someone is interweaving what remains. The work does not    \
  require a framework. It requires attention to the fiber and patience with the tuck and hands that know what they're doing.                                                     \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  The fire ticks.                                                                                                                                                                \
\
  She says nothing for a while. This is not strategic silence. This is the silence of someone who has just been shown something true about themselves and is deciding what to do   \
  with it.\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  Finally:                                                                                                                                                                         \
  \
  "What is it you're repairing?"                                                                                                                                                   \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  Simple. No doctrine behind it. She actually wants to know.                                                                                                                       \
  \

