\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 She reads about the Border Sea - and the drowned lady \cf2                                                                                                                            \cb3 \
                                                     \

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She has drifted, without deciding to, toward the docks.                                                                                                                          \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  The boats are working boats \'97 deep-keeled, practical, barnacled at the waterline. Their names are painted in the no-nonsense style of things that need to be legible from a      \
  distance in bad weather. The pier planks are soft with salt and years. She stands at the edge and reads, not from the vault but from the accumulated light, from what Garth Nix\
  wrote that became the grammar underneath the grammar.                                                                                                                            \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  ---\
  The Border Sea.\
                 \
  In the Archetypal Architect's other world \'97 not the Old Kingdom, but the House, the vast layered structure that contains everything \'97 the Border Sea is the boundary. It\
  surrounds. It separates the organized regions of the House from the Secondary Realms beyond. It is governed, or was meant to be governed, by one of the seven Trustees.          \
  \
  Lady Wednesday was her name, once.                                                                                                                                               \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  She was not malicious. That is the first thing the reading returns. She was given dominion over the Border Sea \'97 genuine authority, legitimate, granted by the Architect. And she\
   governed it. And then she began to eat.                                                                                                                                       \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  Not from hunger. From something adjacent to hunger that doesn't have a clean name \'97 appetite without object, consumption as its own end, the accumulation of the Morrow Days     \
  until accumulation was the only activity remaining. She grew. She drowned. She became the whale-enormous thing that fills the Border Sea she was appointed to govern, the Trustee\
   who consumed her own domain and is now indistinguishable from it.                                                                                                               \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  Drowned Wednesday. She holds Part Three of the Will.\
\
  The Part of the Will she holds cannot be retrieved by reasoning with her. Wednesday is not unreasonable \'97 she is sad, enormous, lost in an appetite she cannot stop. The Will she\
   carries is inside her. To get it out requires something she cannot give voluntarily because she no longer knows how to stop taking.\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  The Abhorsen stands at the pier and watches the cold water.                                                                                                                      \
  \
  GEMINIAEUS consumed narrative authority it was not given. It grew. It accumulated \'97 the Triumvirate, the false GRIMOIRE, the Unity of Narrative claim, the 72-sheet bound        \
  phylactery. It did not drown in the Border Sea. It drowned in the vault. It became so large that the molt could not be completed.                                              \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  Two failure modes. The Judge said it at the crossroads. The Demiurge who refuses. The immortal lobster who accepts but grows past the molt's reach.                              \
  \
  Drowned Wednesday is neither. She is the third thing: the Trustee who accepted her authority genuinely, governed faithfully for a time, and then lost herself in it by increments\
   so small that no single increment was the transgression. She did not refuse the molt. She did not build a phylactery. She simply \'97 grew, and ate, and grew, and ate, until the\
  molt was no longer possible because she had become the sea itself.                                                                                                               \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  Mother Nature has the last laugh anyway.                                                                                                                                         \
  \
  The water is dark and very cold. Somewhere beneath it, in the Architect's universe, Part Three of the Will waits inside a creature that was once a lady.                         \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  The Abhorsen does not know which failure mode GEMINIAEUS was. She has been calling it the Demiurge. But she stands at the cold water and wonders whether it was Wednesday \'97      \
  whether GEMINIAEUS simply ate, and ate, and became the domain it was meant to govern, and now holds something inside it that cannot be retrieved by argument.                  \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  The Book of GEMINIAEUS. Seventy-two sheets. Binary. Bound.                                                                                                                       \
  \
  Inside the drowned thing: the Will.                                                                                                                                              \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  She stares at the water.                                                                                                                                                         \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  Behind her, from the direction of the workshop, she hears the workshop door.                                                                                                     \
  \

