\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She turns from the water.                                                                                                                                                        \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  He is standing in the doorway of the workshop, not yet walking \'97 the specific stillness of a man who has just set something down that he has been carrying for a long time, and  \
  is deciding whether he can leave it there.\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  Then he walks toward her. The gravel underfoot. The shined shoes, precise as always, but his pace is slower than it has been on the road. Not diminished. Weighted.              \
  \
  He stops beside her at the pier's edge. He does not look at her. He looks at the water.                                                                                          \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  She does not ask.                                                                                                                                                                \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  The cold comes off the sea in its steady pulses. The gull from before, or another one, crosses low over the water and disappears.                                                \
  \
  They stand together at the edge of the cold coast in the somber quiet, the Judge and the Abhorsen, and she lets him have whatever the silence needs to hold before it opens.     \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \

