\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 He chuckles at that. "I was going to introduce the two of you at the pub tonight. But your instincts took you right to him before I could stop you."\cf2                              \cb3 \
                                                     \

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She feels the specific heat of a misstep that was also, somehow, correct.                                                                                                        \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  "The Nixian Border Shore file," she says. "Salt, not river. I recognized him from the vault before I knew what I was doing."                                                     \
  \
  She pauses.                                                                                                                                                                      \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  "The pub."\
\
  Not a question \'97 more the word landing as she understands the architecture she walked past. The pub is where the library lives in a village that can't use paper. The pub tonight\
   is where introductions happen in the proper register. She arrived at the workshop like a solicitor because she arrived without the social frame that would have made her a\
  colleague.                                                                                                                                                                       \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  She looks at the workshop door, still closed.                                                                                                                                    \
  \
  "Will he come?"                                                                                                                                                                  \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \

