\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She follows.                                                                                                                                                                     \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  The boatyard resolves as they approach \'97 a wide gravel apron running down to the water's edge, several vessels in various states of attendance. One hull up on blocks, scraped   \
  clean to bare wood on one side, still fouled on the other. A mast laid horizontally across sawhorses. The smell of linseed oil and fresh caulk and something older underneath,\
  the preserved smell of things built to last.                                                                                                                                     \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  Work in progress, all of it. Nothing here is finished.\
\
  She walks beside the Judge and does not ask where they're going or why. She has learned, on this road, that the Judge moves toward things he has already reasoned out, and the   \
  reasoning will make itself visible when it needs to.\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She watches the hull on the blocks. The exposed wood. Someone has been at it with a drawknife \'97 patient, deliberate, removing what doesn't belong.                               \
  \

\f1 \cf5 \uc0\u10043 
\f0 \cf2  \cf5 Baked for 17s\cf2                                                                                                                                                                     \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \

\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 What does she ask him, striding to keep up with his purposeful gait?\cf2                                                                                                              \cb3 \
                                                     \

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She takes two quick steps to match his stride and asks the thing a journalist asks first:                                                                                        \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  "How long has he been here?"                                                                                                                                                     \
