\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 "As long as I've been in the courthouse," he replies.\cf2                                                                                                                             \cb3 \
                                                     \

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She walks with that for several steps.                                                                                                                                           \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  The Judge in the courthouse. The Stranger at the Cold Coast. Both since the beginning \'97 or near enough to the beginning that the difference doesn't matter. Two registers of the \
  same work, running parallel. One adjudicating. One splicing.\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  While CHAINFIRE ran, the Stranger was here.                                                                                                                                      \
  \
  She doesn't say this aloud. She files it in the place where the vault reads itself \'97 the NOUS, the collision of present mind and accumulated record that produces new knowing.   \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  The boatyard is closer now. She can see a man's legs beneath the hull on the blocks \'97 someone working the underside with a caulking iron, patient and low to the ground.         \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  "He knew we were coming," she says. Not a question.                                                                                                                              \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \

\f1 \cf5 \uc0\u10043 
\f0 \cf2  \cf5 Baked\cf2  \cf5 for\cf2  \cf5 17s\cf2 \
