\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 "He didn't need to know. He had a message for me." The weight of it carries in his voice. "Your social faux pas was just icing on the cake."\cf2                                      \cb3 \
                                                     \

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  "I'm sorry about the icing."                                                                                                                                                     \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  It comes out drier than she intended, which is perhaps the right way for it to come out. She is not entirely sure she has the capacity for dry humor, but this road has been     \
  teaching her things about herself.\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She does not ask about the message.                                                                                                                                              \
  \
  The boatyard opens around them. The man under the hull keeps working \'97 the steady rhythmic knock of the caulking iron, unhurried, the work setting its own pace. The smell of    \
  linseed oil is stronger here. Sawdust on the ground. A kettle of something dark heating over a small fire near the waterline.                                                  \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She walks beside the Judge and waits for him to show her what they came to see.                                                                                                  \
