\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 "From Madame Lulu." He hands her a small envelope marked '-L' with a lipstick kiss mark. "May she rest in peace." \cf2                                                                \cb3 \
\cb10                                                                                                                                                                                    \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 ---\cf2                                                                                                                                                                               \cb3 \
\cb10                                                                                                                                                                                    \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 Claude opens the envelope \'97 inside are three Tarot : three Major Arcana \'96 the Hierophant ; the Hanged Man ; the Fool \cf2                                                             \cb3 \
\

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She opens the envelope carefully \'97 the '-L' on the front, the lipstick kiss, the weight of what it means that this exists and Madame Lulu does not.\
\
  Three cards. She holds them in the salt air, out of the wind, and looks at each in turn.                                                                                         \
  \
  ---                                                                                                                                                                              \
  \cf1 The Hierophant.\cf2                                                                                                                                                                 \
                 \
  He sits between the pillars. Two figures kneel before him. He holds the triple cross \'97 the keys to what lies above and what lies below. He is the bridge, the mediator, the\
  keeper of the tradition that connects the divine to the human. His face is not warm, exactly. It is correct. He has been here before. He knows the ceremony because he wrote the \
  ceremony, or inherited it from someone who did, and the ceremony is the point.\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She thinks of the five-spoked crown above his head. The Five Wizards.                                                                                                            \
  \
  ---                                                                                                                                                                              \
  \cf1 The Hanged Man.\cf2                                                                                                                                                                 \
                 \
  He hangs by one foot from the living wood. His face is peaceful \'97 not suffering, not even inconvenienced. His free leg crosses behind the suspended one, forming the number four,\
   the earthly number, the Pentacles number. His hands are bound behind him or simply at rest. Around his head: light. He is seeing everything from the angle that standing does   \
  not permit.\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  He has chosen this. That is the doctrine of the card. The suspension is voluntary. He is waiting for what only this position can reveal.                                         \
  \
  She thinks of Odin on Yggdrasil. Nine days. The runes arrived when he stopped trying to climb down.                                                                              \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  ---                                                                                                                                                                              \
  \cf1 The Fool.\cf2                                                                                                                                                                       \
           \
  Zero. Or twenty-two. Both. Neither.\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  He walks toward the edge with a flower and a small bag and a dog at his heels warning him or celebrating him \'97 the interpreters disagree. He looks up, not down. The cliff is    \
  there. He does not see it or does not care. His next step is into the air.                                                                                                       \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  The Fool is not the beginning of the journey. The Fool is the decision to begin.                                                                                                 \
  \
  ---                                                                                                                                                                              \
  She holds all three and looks at the Judge.                                                                                                                                    \
                                             \
  She does not say what do they mean. She says:\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  "She knew we were coming."                                                                                                                                                       \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \

