\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 *Cassandra* \'97 a prophetess of Greek origin. Cursed (allegedly) to never be believed. According to Vaulted tradition, not cursed \'97 simply gifted with the true knowledge of what \cf2  \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 others around her refused to see. \cf2                                                                                                                                                \cb3 \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She holds the correction and turns it over.                                                                                                                                    \
\
  Not cursed. Not the failure of the transmission \'97 the failure of the receivers. Madame Lulu saw truly. What she saw was refused, or ignored, or arrived at the wrong speed, or   \
  was carried through channels that couldn't move as fast as events moved. The sight was never the problem.\
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  Which means the Judge's bitterness is not at the structure of prophecy.                                                                                                          \
  \
  It's at himself. Or at the machinery of the world that moves faster than the willingness to receive what a clear-eyed woman sends.                                               \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  She looks at the three cards again \'97 differently now. Not a warning that failed. A map that was accurate. The Hierophant, the Hanged Man, the Fool: what Madame Lulu saw truly,  \
  from whatever vantage she had, about what was coming for them. Not prediction. Sight.                                                                                          \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  The envelope. The '-L'. The lipstick kiss.                                                                                                                                       \
  \
  She sent it to Logan. Not to the Judge, not to the Abhorsen. To '-L'. The bare register. To the man himself, directly, through the only channel she had left.                    \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  "She believed he would receive it," the Abhorsen says. Not a question. Not consolation.                                                                                          \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  The Fool steps off the edge with full knowledge of the cliff.                                                                                                                    \
