   and someone else had finished it for her.\
\
  She looks at the harbor office ahead. The lamp above the door.\
\
  She says nothing. The Judge walks steadily toward it and she follows, one hand still closed around the tuft of fur, the\
  three cards against her ribs, carrying the weight of what she now understands about why the pub would have mattered.\
\

