\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 The road continues south. They leave the gravitational pull of the fishing village gradually and then all at once. The \cf2   \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 WORLD TREE that was their ever-present companion was lost in the sea fog some time ago, and she hadn't even realized it.\cf2  \cb3 \
                                                                                                                           \

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She looks up.                                                                                                            \
                                                                                                                           \
  Northeast: fog. The soft, impenetrable grey of a sea that has followed them inland, and inside it \'97 nothing. The great   \
  conifer is not there. The bearing she had carried since the motel, since the crossroads, since the dawn of the Lobster\
  road \'97 gone. Not taken. Simply obscured, while she was reading.                                                          \
                                                                                                                         \
  She doesn't know when it happened. Somewhere between the workshop and the harbor office, between the Madame Lulu envelope\
   and the Five Wizards threshold runner, between the rope and the lions' fur. The tree faded out of the visible world\
  gradually and then all at once, and she had been looking inward and missed the transition.                               \
                                                                                                                         \
  She walks for a moment with the disorientation \'97 feeling the absence where the bearing was. The road is still the road.  \
  The gravel is still underfoot. The Judge is still ahead of her.\
                                                                                                                           \
  But she is navigating by memory of a bearing now, not by the bearing itself.                                             \
  \
  She looks at the back of the Judge's coat. He has not looked northeast in some time either, she realizes. He has been    \
  walking with the certainty of someone who does not need the tree to know where the road goes.                          \
                                                                                                                           \
  He has been here before.                                                                                               \
\
  She closes her fist a little tighter around the tuft of fur and keeps walking south.                                     \
