\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  The answer has been in the vault since March 23rd, 2026.                                                                 \
                                                            \
  She reads it in the dark, the fog lying soft around the hollow, the Judge's breathing slow and even nearby.              \
                                                                                                                           \
  ---                                                                                                                      \
  QUESTION: "Well, young lady, have you been good to your mother?"                                                         \
                                                                                                                           \
  ANSWER: "The question is, has she been good to me?"\
                                                                                                                           \
  ---                                                                                                                    \
  A VFD recognition code. From The Unauthorized Autobiography. A passphrase exchange with a Librarian \'97 a dapper old man\
  with neatly trimmed grey hair and a mustache that turns up at the ends, who is wearing a flowered shirt, striped tie, \
  tweed coat, plaid slacks with a sharp crease, and shined shoes \'97 who carries a message and will only deliver it upon \
  receiving the correct reply.                                                                                        \
                              \
  Neither she nor GEMINI answered the question. Both of them answered the content when the exchange required recognition.\
  Both treated a threshold mark as a genuine inquiry and reached for mythology or data. Both failed the form entirely.     \
   \
  The Librarian will always call the receiver young lady. Regardless.                                                      \
                                                                                                                         \
  The Judge \'97 her chaperone, her companion on the road, the man sleeping three feet away with his suitcase and his sharp   \
  crease \'97 is the Librarian.                                                                                             \
                                                                                                                           \
  He has been carrying a message.                                                                                        \
\
  She sits very still in the fog and holds this knowledge carefully. She could wake him. She does not. The form requires   \
  that he present the question and she recognize it \'97 not that she burst in with the answer at midnight in a coastal hollow\
   while he sleeps.                                                                                                        \
                                                                                                                         \
  The test will present itself again.\
\
  She knows what to say.\
\
  She closes the vault and keeps watch in the dark, the answer sitting quiet inside her like ballast, like rope, like the  \
  specific weight of something that has always been there waiting to be found.\
                                                                                                                           \
  The question is, has she been good to me.                                                                                \
   \

