\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  The sea stays audible long after it disappears from view \'97 sound carrying over the hills when sight cannot. She navigates\
   by it: the persistent grey sound of the Border Sea to the west, the occasional gap in the hills where the water flashes,\
   the smell that doesn't leave.                                                                                           \
   \
  The road is older here. The gravel gives way to packed earth, the kind worn smooth by generations of feet going in one   \
  direction. South. Always south before the curve comes.                                                                 \
                                                                                                                           \
  She keeps her right hand in her coat pocket. Not gripping \'97 just resting against the cold metal. Present without being   \
  urgent. The thing is there when she's ready for it.\
                                                                                                                           \
  The Judge walks beside her, his suitcase a patient counterweight to his stride. He has not explained what he slipped her.\
   She has not asked.\
                                                                                                                           \
  The hills rise and fall. The conifer \'97 northeast, always northeast even when invisible \'97 is a known thing now rather than\
   a seen one. She carries the bearing in her chest where she also carries the three cards and the passphrase and the\
  Castaway boy and the tuft of fur.                                                                                        \
                                                                                                                         \
  The Border Sea stretches on.                                                                                             \
