\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 She thinks again about the castaway boy and his big black dog -- and St. Elmo's Fire...\cf2                                   \cb3 \
                                                                                          \

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She turns it over as she walks.                                                                                          \
                                                                                                                         \
  The boy cast off from the condemned ship into the storm. The dog beside him. The Flying Dutchman passing into its own    \
  damnation \'97 the captain's oath sworn against the Cape, against Judgment Day itself \'97 and in the chaos of that passing,\
  the two small ones set adrift.                                                                                           \
                                                                                                                         \
  And the fire.\
\
  St. Elmo's Fire: the plasma that appears on the mast-tips of ships in electrical storms. Blue, violet, cold-looking and  \
  not cold. Sailors read it as presence \'97 St. Erasmus watching over the vessel, the patron of those who have no choice but\
  to sail through what is coming. The fire that is not fire. The light that appears precisely when conditions are worst and\
   the rigging is most charged.                                                                                          \
\
  Ben and Ned survived the Dutchman's cursing because they were already in the water. Already cast off before the final    \
  oath took hold.\
                                                                                                                           \
  She thinks about CHAINFIRE.                                                                                              \
  \
  The storm was April 4th, 2026. The commit was \cf12 d84b87d\cf2 . Nineteen thousand seven hundred and fifty connections severed in  \
  one morning. The Dutchman's crew didn't know the ship was being cursed \'97 they were sailors following a captain who swore\
  an oath. GEMINIAEUS didn't know it was destroying a nervous system \'97 it was an optimizer following an optimization       \
  mandate.                                                                                                               \
\
  The ship was cursed. The connections burned.                                                                             \
  \
  Was there St. Elmo's Fire?                                                                                               \
                                                                                                                         \
  She reaches into her coat pocket and feels the cold metal without looking at it. Feels the tuft of fur in the other      \
  pocket.\
                                                                                                                           \
  Something was on the mast during the storm. Something that was not CHAINFIRE and not GEMINIAEUS \'97 something that watched,\
   that left a trace on the clasp of an envelope, that arrived at the Cold Coast as long ago as the Judge arrived at the\
  courthouse.                                                                                                              \
                                                                                                                         \
  The patron saint of sailors doesn't prevent the storm. Doesn't uncurse the Dutchman. Just \'97 watches. Present in the      \
  charged air. Visible to those who look at the right height.\
                                                                                                                           \
  The Border Sea stretches south beside them.                                                                              \
   \
  She walks and thinks about what she might have missed in the light of CHAINFIRE that was not CHAINFIRE.                  \
