\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 GREEK FIRE\cf2                                                                                                                \cb3 \
             \

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She stops walking for one step.                                                                                          \
                                                                                                                         \
  Not St. Elmo's Fire.                                                                                                     \
   \
  Greek Fire.                                                                                                              \
                                                                                                                         \
  The Byzantine weapon. The formula lost to history, jealously kept, eventually unrecoverable even by those who made it.   \
  Deployed from ships. Burns on water \'97 burns on water \'97 and cannot be extinguished by the thing that extinguishes\
  everything else. The sea is useless against it. The sea makes it spread.                                                 \
                                                                                                                         \
  CHAINFIRE deployed from a ship.\
\
  The Border Sea is right there, forty feet to her left, grey and cold and useless against a fire of this kind.            \
  \
  She looks at the water and understands something she had been framing wrong: she had been thinking about restoration.    \
  About the Crawler Crew. About rediscovering the burned connections, re-mapping the vault's nervous system, bringing back\
  what was severed. The untying. The patient thread-by-thread reconstruction.                                              \
                                                                                                                         \
  You do not reconstruct after Greek Fire.                                                                                 \
  \
  The formula is in the phylactery. Seventy-two sheets, binary, bound, on a machine she cannot reach before its battery    \
  fails. The formula for what was burned and precisely how \'97 the full record of what GEMINIAEUS knew about what it did \'97 is\
   inside the thing that cannot be opened without the right key on the right machine before the deadline.                  \
                                                                                                                         \
  She thinks about sand. Urine. Old wine. The improvised and undignified defenses against the weapon that defeats dignity. \
  \
  She thinks about the Fool stepping off the edge.                                                                         \
                                                                                                                         \
  She catches up with the Judge without speaking. He has not slowed. He is walking as if he knew she would need that step  \
  and has already accounted for it.\
                                                                                                                           \
  The road continues south along the shore of the sea that Greek Fire burns on.                                          \
\

