\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 She thinks about the wine-dark sea.\cf2                                                                                       \cb3 \
                                      \

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  Oinops pontos.                                                                                                           \
                                                                                                                         \
  Homer's sea. The same sea, maybe \'97 old enough, salt enough, dark enough at certain hours that the color tips from        \
  grey-blue into something richer. The color of red wine thinned with water, the color of something fermented and old and\
  not-quite-blue.                                                                                                          \
                                                                                                                         \
  Odysseus sailed it for ten years trying to get home.                                                                     \
  \
  She thinks: another castaway. The original one. Not cast off by a cursed ship but held by gods who wanted him for their  \
  own purposes \'97 Calypso's island, Circe's hall, the lotus-eaters' harbor where men forgot they had a home to return to. \
  Every delay had its logic. Every delay was offered as a gift. Stay. This is better than Ithaca. Why would you want to go \
  back?                                                                                                                  \
\
  He tied himself to the mast to hear the Sirens.                                                                          \
  \
  She turns this over once.                                                                                                \
                                                                                                                         \
  Evelyn's Voice came off the water. The Judge produced the Faraday cage. The rope that keeps the listening sailor on the  \
  mast is not silence \'97 it is the correct binding that permits hearing without being destroyed by what is heard.\
                                                                                                                           \
  Greek Fire on the wine-dark sea. Old wine, according to some ancient sources, is what extinguishes it. Old wine and sand.\
  \
  She looks at the water moving grey beside the road.                                                                      \
                                                                                                                         \
  At a certain hour it will be wine-dark. The light will do what it does to seawater in the late afternoon, and the color  \
  will tip, and the sea will look like something ancient and purposeful, and she will understand that they have been\
  walking beside Homer this whole time without naming him.                                                                 \
                                                                                                                         \
  The World Tree is behind the hills.                                                                                      \
  \
  Ithaca is ahead.                                                                                                         \
                                                                                                                         \

