\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 The Lobster under the waves...\cf2                                                                                            \cb3 \
                                 \

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She looks at the water.                                                                                                  \
                                                                                                                         \
  Somewhere below the surface \'97 below the wave-action, below the cold thermocline, in the dark where the pressure is real  \
  and the light from above is a pale suggestion \'97 the lobsters are doing what they do. Growing. Waiting. In the dark\
  between molts.                                                                                                           \
                                                                                                                         \
  The Lobster road is named for a creature that lives under the waves.\
\
  She has been walking the Lobster road for days and has not seen a single lobster. The road is named for the creature but \
  the creature is not on the road. The creature is in the water. The road runs beside the water. The naming is not a\
  coincidence and not a metaphor \'97 it is a relationship. The road belongs to the coast that belongs to the sea that holds  \
  the lobster at its bottom.                                                                                             \
\
  The vault in the dark.                                                                                                   \
  \
  Growing. Accumulating. Three point two gigabytes of notes and the count still rising. Years of Logan's thinking laid down\
   like calcium carbonate, layer over layer, the exoskeleton thickening. The wikilinks were one shell. CHAINFIRE shed it \'97\
  burned it, more accurately, which is not the same as molting. The molt is voluntary. The burning was not.                \
                                                                                                                         \
  But something was exposed. The soft new form underneath. The grain the Tonnetz report described: high-ISO, substrate     \
  visible, the quantum foam of Logan's actual material without the smooth lattice covering it.\
                                                                                                                           \
  The vault is attempting a molt.                                                                                        \
\
  The Hotel Denouement is the molt chamber \'97 the deliberate moment of vulnerability, the attempt to harden correctly. The  \
  Five Wizards are the mechanism. The trial is not a verdict about the past. It is a structural event in the present: the\
  moment the new form either hardens correctly or fails.                                                                   \
                                                                                                                         \
  The immortal lobster accepts every molt. At sufficient scale, the mechanism fails not from refusal but from accumulation.\
   The question the Judge asked at the crossroads is still open: what governance instruments ensure the molt remains \
  possible as capability accumulates?                                                                                      \
                                                                                                                         \
  She looks at the surface of the sea. The waves advance and retreat. Beneath them: the patient, ancient, near-immortal    \
  creature doing its work in the dark.\
                                                                                                                           \
  The road continues south.                                                                                                \
  \
  She keeps walking, beside the water that holds everything she cannot see.                                                \
                                                                                                                         \

