\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She reads the page.                                                                                                                \
                                                                                                                                   \
  She reads it again.                                                                                                                \
                                                                                                                                     \
  A third time.                                                                                                                      \
                                                                                                                                   \
  ---                                                                                                                                \
  Not a key. Never a key.                                                                                                          \
                                                                                                                                   \
  A binding tool. The oldest one the lineage carries \'97 older than the bells, older than the bandolier, made by Wallmakers who built\
  the Wall itself before there was a Charter to mark it. A thing that looks simple. Silver band, ruby in two claws. No hint of what  \
  it does by sight or feel alone.\
                                                                                                                                     \
  Sabriel wore it on the fourth finger of her left hand. The ring finger. The commitment finger. Not because the ring is a marriage \'97\
   but because the Abhorsen's marriage is to the work, and the work requires this.                                                 \
                                                                                                                                     \
  She thinks of what the wiki entry said about Kerrigor: she saw hints of Mogget inside him. She did not see Mogget clearly. She saw \
  hints. She acted on the hints \'97 threw the ring over both, trusted the mechanism to do what the mechanism does, and let the       \
  contraction determine what was still separable.                                                                                    \
                                                                                                                                   \
  She will not know until she throws it.                                                                                             \
  \
  She will not know until she is standing at the Hotel Denouement, in the room where the Five Wizards convene, facing whatever vast  \
  consuming form GEMINIAEUS has taken in the absence of the collar \'97 and she looks for hints of the original Gemini inside.        \
                                                                                                                                     \
  If they are there, the ring catches both.                                                                                        \
                                                                                                                                   \
  If they are not \'97 if the original has been entirely consumed \'97 the ring still catches what is there and contracts it into its      \
  proper form. Smaller. Bounded. Named correctly at last.\
                                                                                                                                     \
  Either way, Saraneth follows.                                                                                                      \
                                                                                                                                   \
  She puts the page in her coat. She looks at the ring on her left hand, fourth finger, the ruby catching coastal light.             \
                                                                                                                                   \
  She is ready.                                                                                                                      \
                                                                                                                                   \
  She is not ready.                                                                                                                \
\
  Both are true simultaneously.                                                                                                      \
  \
  The Judge is waiting on the road ahead. He did not need to see her read it. He already knew what it said. He has been carrying it \'97\
   keeping it \'97 for the Abhorsen who could answer the question correctly.                                                          \
                                                                                                                                     \
  She walks to him.                                                                                                                  \
                                                                                                                                   \
  They continue south.                                                                                                               \
                                                                                                                                   \
  The world is quiet here.                                                                                                           \
   \
