\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 She looks again at the metal in her hand -- no longer a trident. A Ring. A small silver band, with two claws, holding a ruby.\cf2       \cb3 \
\

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  ---\
  She stops walking.\
\
  ---\
  Not a trident.\
\
  She had assembled the shape from the cold and the darkness and the confidence of a reader who already knows the next chapter. Three\
   tines, she had thought. The 
\f2 \uc0\u55357 \u56625 
\f0 . The VAULT \'97 VOICE \'97 VOID pressed into copper. The symbol she had been reading toward.\
\
  She was wrong about the shape.\
\
  Two claws. A setting \'97 the kind made to hold something rather than to point toward something. The band is silver, thin, worn smooth\
   in the way that means years of being worn. And between the two claws, held and not crushed, catching the coastal light coming off\
  the Border Sea:\
\
  A ruby.\
\
  Small. Deeply red. Not the bright red of fresh blood or fire but the darker red \'97 the red of something seen through depth, the\
  color that requires light to enter and then holds it.\
\
  She stands with it in her open palm.\
\
  The trident reading had been elegant. Had assembled cleanly into the mythology they were walking through. Had confirmed what she\
  expected to find. That was the error \'97 she had read what she expected before she had read what was there.\
\
  Read before naming. HOW Rule One. She had violated it even while naming it as doctrine.\
\
  This is a ring. A ring is not a symbol of architecture. A ring is worn. Given. Passed from one hand to another at a threshold \'97 at\
  an engagement, a covenant, a death, an inheritance. A ring is what you press into someone's palm when you cannot say aloud what you\
   need them to carry forward.\
\
  The Judge \'97 a bachelor with no wife but the practice of the Law. That is what he said at the Cold Coast.\
\
  But someone gave him this. Or he was keeping it. Or it came to him across the long years of walking circuits between the Hotel\
  Denouement and the VFD Touchstones and the Downtime Motels of the world, accumulating the objects that the dead cannot take and the\
   living cannot yet hold.\
\
  Two claws. A ruby.\
\
  Two \'97 not three. Not the triune. Not the chorus. Two. The minimum number for a covenant. Logan and \'97\
\
  She does not finish the thought. Not yet.\
\
  She looks at the ruby for a long time. The color of:\
  the righteous fury in the caps-lock marginalia.\
  The Sword of Truth at the red edge.\
  Greek Fire burning on water.\
  The thing at the center of the VAULT \'97 VOICE \'97 VOID that she had missed because she was reading for the architecture and not for\
  the heart.\
\
  The two claws are not holding the ruby captive. They are keeping it from falling.\
\
  She closes her hand around it again. Carefully this time. Not the grip of someone taking hold of a tool. The grip of someone who\
  has been given something she does not yet understand and is responsible for not losing it before she does.\
\
  She looks up.\
\
  The Judge is waiting at the curve in the road. He did not turn around. But he stopped walking when she stopped.\
\
  He has been waiting.\
\
  The world is quiet here.\
\

