\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 She catches up to the JUDGE. He hands her a sheet of paper... Sabriel wears the ring on the fourth finger of her left hand.\cf2         \cb3 \
\cb10                                                                                                                                      \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 The **Abhorsen's ruby ring** is a [Wallmaker](https://oldkingdomwiki.fandom.com/wiki/Wallmaker "Wallmaker") creation designed to \cf2   \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 re-bind [Mogget](https://oldkingdomwiki.fandom.com/wiki/Mogget "Mogget"). If Mogget's collar has been removed either deliberately \cf2  \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 or accidentally, and he has been released as his true form, [Yrael](https://oldkingdomwiki.fandom.com/wiki/Yrael "Yrael"), the \cf2     \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 [Abhorsen](https://oldkingdomwiki.fandom.com/wiki/Abhorsen "Abhorsen") can use the ring to return him to servant and cat. When \cf2     \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 Yrael is released, and in close enough proximity, it will slowly expand until it can be thrown over his head. It then contracts, \cf2   \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 trapping him. Yrael is gradually forced into a shining white globule the size of a cat. The Abhorsen must then finish the process \cf2  \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 by ringing the [bell](https://oldkingdomwiki.fandom.com/wiki/Bells "Bells") \cf2                                                        \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 [Saraneth](https://oldkingdomwiki.fandom.com/wiki/Saraneth "Saraneth"), the Binder, after which the ring eventually takes on the \cf2   \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 red-leather appearance of Mogget's collar, and an answering miniature Saraneth is made. The white shape becomes a cat, who then \cf2    \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 coughs up a ruby ring.\cf2                                                                                                              \cb3 \
\cb10                                                                                                                                      \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 The ring looks simple enough: silver, with a ruby in the center held by two silver "claws." There is no hint to its vast magical \cf2   \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 power by sight or feel alone.\cf2                                                                                                       \cb3 \
\cb10                                                                                                                                      \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 It is how [Sabriel](https://oldkingdomwiki.fandom.com/wiki/Sabriel "Sabriel") managed to bind \cf2                                      \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 [Kerrigor](https://oldkingdomwiki.fandom.com/wiki/Kerrigor "Kerrigor"): he had "consumed" Yrael, but Sabriel saw hints of Mogget \cf2   \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 inside him, and she threw the ring over them both. They contracted into two conjoined hemispheres of black and white that became \cf2   \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 two cats, one black and one white. As Saraneth had shattered, however, she chose \cf2                                                   \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 [Ranna](https://oldkingdomwiki.fandom.com/wiki/Ranna "Ranna") the Sleeper to bind both of them, with the result that both sleep \cf2    \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 frequently afterward (though Ranna holds Kerrigor, now in cat form, much more tightly, only allowing him two brief wakings in \cf2      \cb3 \
