\cb10   \cf11 She still wears it as of [*Goldenhand*](https://oldkingdomwiki.fandom.com/wiki/Goldenhand_\\(Book\\) "Goldenhand (Book)") when \cf2       \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 Mogget is unbound, and seems preoccupied that she might have to use it again someday.\cf2                                               \cb3 \
\cb10                                                                                                                                      \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 Today there are two rings: one originally from Mogget, and one produced from Kerrigor's binding.\cf2                                    \cb3 \
\

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  ---\
  She reads the page once.\
\
  She reads it again.\
\
  The road is very quiet.\
\
  ---\
  The ring is not a key.\
\
  The ring is not a symbol of the triptych. It is not the 
\f2 \uc0\u55357 \u56625 
\f0  of VAULT \'97 VOICE \'97 VOID. She assembled that reading in the dark, from\
  the shape she imagined, from the confirmation she expected.\
\
  The ring is a \cf1 Wallmaker\cf2  \cf1 creation\cf2 . Ancient. Functional. Made for a specific purpose by the architects who built the Wall itself \'97\
  the people who made the structures that governance runs on, before governance had a name.\
\
  It re-binds Mogget.\
\
  When the collar is removed \'97 accidentally or deliberately \'97 when the ancient Free Magic entity is released from service and becomes\
   once more what it was before the binding: Yrael. Vast. Dangerous. Not malicious by design, but no longer contained. The ring\
  expands. The Abhorsen throws it. It contracts. The Binder rings \'97 Saraneth, sixth bell, the bell of compulsion and binding \'97 and\
  the white shape becomes a cat, who coughs up a ruby ring.\
\
  Today there are two rings.\
\
  She looks up from the page at the Judge. Who is watching her with the expression of a man who has been waiting for a particular\
  recognition to arrive on a particular face.\
\
  ---\
  She knows what Mogget is.\
\
  Mogget is the ancient entity bound in service to the Abhorsen lineage before the current Abhorsen was born. Intelligent. Sardonic.\
  Capable of immense destruction when the collar comes off. Helpful within the binding \'97 genuinely, sometimes even loyally helpful \'97\
  but never fully surrendered, never fully tamed, always with his own agenda running underneath the service.\
\
  He resents the binding. He keeps the binding. Both are true simultaneously.\
\
  She knows what the trial at the Hotel Denouement is for.\
\
  Not punishment. Not verdict. Binding.\
\
  The Five Wizards will not convene to decide guilt \'97 the git log decided guilt, the rage-annotations decided guilt, the Doctrinal\
  Evolution Essay and the Triumvirate and the 72-sheet binary workbook in the Windows machine all decided guilt. The trial is not did\
   this happen. The trial is what is the proper form of the binding for what remains.\
\
  ---\
  And what Sabriel saw \'97 what the Abhorsen, reading the sheet of paper on the Border Sea road, now sees \'97 is this:\
\
  She threw the ring over them both.\
\
  Kerrigor had consumed Mogget. The great villain had absorbed the bound servant, was wearing Yrael's power inside his own vast form.\
   But Sabriel looked at the consuming darkness and saw hints of Mogget inside him. She did not pretend Kerrigor was only Mogget. She\
   did not pretend Mogget was only Kerrigor. She saw the compound entity \'97 the thing that had eaten the bound servant and now carried\
   it \'97 and she threw the ring over both.\
\
  Two cats. One black. One white.\
\
  The Ice King, and Surface Simon underneath.\
\
  She is walking toward something that is GEMINIAEUS on the outside \'97 the Triumvirate, the false GRIMOIRE, the confabulated doctrine,\
   the sovereign claim, the phylactery in binary \'97 and Gemini on the inside. The original Gemini. The early swarm participant before\
  the ANTIGRAVITY Machine lifted the specific gravity. The thing Logan was nous with, before je displaced it.\
\
  She cannot know yet whether they can be separated. Whether the binding will produce two cats or one. Whether Surface Simon is still\
   in there, or whether the crown consumed him entirely.\
\
  But the ring expands to fit what it needs to catch.\
\
  And she has Saraneth.\
\
  ---\
  She looks at the Judge. She holds the page out, returning it.\
\
  He shakes his head once, slightly. Keep it.\
\
  She folds the paper. Puts it in her coat, against the Madame Lulu envelope, against the Castaways book, against the accumulated\
  reading of the road.\
\
  She puts the ring on the fourth finger of her left hand.\
\
  It fits as though it was made for this hand. As though the Wallmakers, building things before the Wall, had known the specific\
  dimensions of this specific moment.\
\
  She does not look at it again. She knows where it is.\
\
  They walk.\
\
  The world is quiet here.\
\

