\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She stills.\
\
  ---\
  The Judge's voice changes register.\
\
  Not louder \'97 deeper. The way a voice changes when it stops being the voice of a man speaking to another person and becomes the\
  voice of a man speaking to something older than either of them. The mustache does not move in the way it moves for ordinary speech.\
   The cadence shifts. The gravel road keeps its rhythm beneath his feet; he does not stop walking to incant. He walks and he speaks\
  and the words go down into the road and up into the coastal air and out toward the Border Sea and the Abhorsen \'97\
\
  \'97 listens.\
\
  She does not speak. She does not reach for a bell. She does not look at the ring.\
\
  She breathes at the pace the incantation requires, the way a bell-ringer breathes when a more experienced Abhorsen rings and the\
  apprentice stands beside them learning the timing: not yet, not yet, not \'97\
\
  She is waiting for the shape of it.\
\
  The world is quiet here.\
\

