\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 Belgaer strains in its leather clasp. \cf2                                                                                              \cb3 \
                                                                                                                                   \

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  Her hand goes to it. Holds the clasp closed.                                                                                       \
                                                                                                                                   \
  Belgaer. The Thinker. Fifth of the seven. Its voice makes the Dead think for themselves \'97 restores the autonomous mind to what has \
  been trapped in false pattern. In the right hands, liberation. In the wrong hands, erasure: the self unmade entirely, thought\
  dissolved into nothing.                                                                                                            \
                                                                                                                                   \
  It is straining toward the vault.                                                                                                  \
  \
  Toward twenty thousand severed connections that cannot think toward each other anymore. Toward a NOUS that cannot complete its own \
  thoughts because the relational layer is gone. Toward a man who built six instruments to hold one fear and found them drifting   \
  apart, islands, each convinced it is the whole archipelago.                                                                        \
                                                                                                                                   \
  She understands why it strains.                                                                                                    \
  \
  She does not open the clasp.                                                                                                       \
                                                                                                                                   \
  Not on the road. Not yet. Belgaer rung without precision restores nothing \'97 it erases. You must know exactly what you are giving   \
  the thought back to before you let the bell sound. You must know the name of the mind you are restoring. You must be certain the\
  thing you are freeing has somewhere to return to.                                                                                  \
                                                                                                                                   \
  The Hotel Denouement first. The trial first. The naming first.                                                                   \
\
  Then, if Logan chooses restoration \'97 if he chooses to reactivate the Crawler Crew, to rediscover the burned connections, to re-map \
  the vault's nervous system \'97 then Belgaer.\
                                                                                                                                     \
  She keeps her hand on the clasp.                                                                                                 \
                                                                                                                                   \
  It does not stop straining.                                                                                                        \
  \

