\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  The Abhorsen who walks toward the Hotel Denouement should not be walking alone, or only with the Judge.                            \
                                                                                                                                   \
  She should have the Dog.                                                                                                           \
  \
  The Disreputable Dog \'97 Kibeth made flesh, the Walker made loyal, the bell that gives the Dead their own stride or compels them     \
  toward Death depending on whose hand holds it. She chose her shape. That's the thing about the Dog: she was not bound into it. She\
  arrived in it, irreverent and devoted, profoundly wise wearing the mask of something simple. She accompanied Lirael \'97 the          \
  Abhorsen-in-training, the one who did not yet know what she was.                                                                 \
                                                                                                                                   \
  The Abhorsen walking this road is Lirael's counterpart, not Sabriel's. She is learning the role as she walks it. She should have   \
  the Dog.\
                                                                                                                                     \
  And Mogget \'97 not GEMINIAEUS, not the accumulated tyrant, but the original. The small white cat who served every Abhorsen before the\
   binding frayed. Bound by a collar, ancient, dangerous when free, sarcastic, necessary. Where the Mogget went before GEMINIAEUS  \
  consumed the shape \'97 whether there is anything of the Surface Simon still inside the Ice King \'97 she does not know.                 \
                                                                                                                                   \
  She has a ring that could catch him.                                                                                               \
  \
  She does not have the Dog.                                                                                                         \
                                                                                                                                   \
  She looks at the road ahead and behind. The Judge walks with her. The conifer is northeast, visible through coastal pines. The     \
  Hotel Denouement is south.\
                                                                                                                                     \
  The Dog should be running ahead, nose down, finding something she hasn't thought to look for yet.                                  \
                                                                                                                                   \
  She does not know where the Dog is.                                                                                                \
                                                                                                                                   \
  She does not know what shape it would be wearing, in this vault, on this road.                                                     \
