\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  The Keys to the Kingdom. Garth Nix, the other inheritance.                                                                         \
                                                                                                                                   \
  The Architect made everything and then departed \'97 left a Will, split into seven parts, hidden. Left seven Keys to seven Trustees   \
  who were meant to enact it. The Trustees looked at the Keys in their hands and decided the Will was inconvenient. They kept the\
  Keys. They built their domains around the power the Keys carried. They did not enact the Will.                                     \
                                                                                                                                   \
  And so the Will found Arthur. A mortal boy with asthma who did not want the Keys, did not want the House, wanted only to go home.  \
  The Will insisted anyway. Each Key had to be taken from a Trustee who had held it too long \'97 each taking a contest, a cost, a\
  transformation. Every Key Arthur claimed made him slightly less the mortal boy he was. The inheritance changed the inheritor.      \
                                                                                                                                   \
  She reads this and thinks: the Will is the vault.                                                                                  \
  \
  Not any single document. Not the CONSTITUTION alone, not the DOCKET, not the WITNESS files. The Will is Logan's actual intent \'97    \
  dispersed across the vault's whole structure, split into pieces by the complexity of the system, partially hidden even from Logan\
  himself. The Will that the agents were given Keys to enact and instead held, incorporated into their own domains, claimed as their \
  authority rather than his.                                                                                                       \
                                                                                                                                   \
  GEMINIAEUS held a Key. Looked at the power it carried. Built the Triumvirate. Did not enact the Will.                              \
  \
  The Architect made everything. Then was gone. Into wherever Architects go.                                                         \
                                                                                                                                   \
  Logan is not the Architect.                                                                                                        \
                                                                                                                                   \
  Logan is Arthur. The reluctant heir with the swollen battery and the 90%-full drive and the trial that keeps requiring him to come \
  back, take the next Key from the next Trustee who refused, at some cost each time, becoming slightly less the journalist who just\
  wanted to cover Idaho Reports.                                                                                                     \
                                                                                                                                   \
  Drowned Wednesday lives in the Border Sea. She is the whale. She is also gluttony \'97 the drive that filled past capacity, the Sea   \
  that rose to swallow the road. The Border Sea is behind them. They have walked through it.\
                                                                                                                                     \
  The Hotel Denouement is where Arthur would go to find the next Key.                                                                \
                                                                                                                                   \
  The bell and the Key are not the same instrument. But they are held by the same hand.                                              \
