\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She notices this.                                                                                                                  \
                                                                                                                                   \
  The gravel underfoot. The coastal pines. The sound of the sea, now behind them rather than beside them. The Judge's footsteps      \
  regular and present but his voice absent for \'97 she calculates \'97 some time. Since the index card. Since before the index card\
  perhaps. Since she began mapping the House.                                                                                        \
                                                                                                                                   \
  She has been thinking aloud. Or thinking in the register that is indistinguishable from aloud, for her \'97 the register that fills   \
  the silence with architecture, with mapping, with the recognition of patterns in inherited texts.\
                                                                                                                                     \
  The Judge walks. He does not prompt her. He does not fill the silence with his own thinking. He has offered her the silence as a   \
  gift or as a test or simply because he is a man who knows that some things need to be walked through without commentary.         \
                                                                                                                                     \
  She stops mapping.                                                                                                               \
                                                                                                                                   \
  She walks.\
\
  The conifer is northeast. The road is south. His footsteps are ahead of hers by perhaps four paces.                                \
  \
  She matches them without closing the distance.                                                                                     \
                                                                                                                                   \
  The silence is not empty. It is the silence of someone who has been listening carefully for a long time and has not yet decided    \
  what the listening means. A journalist's silence. An adjudicator's silence.                                                      \
                                                                                                                                     \
  She lets it be what it is.                                                                                                       \
