\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 There is a beauty - a terrible beauty, as with most cruelness - in the cruelty of it.\cf2                                               \cb3 \
                                                                                                                                   \

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  Yes.                                                                                                                               \
                                                                                                                                   \
  He did not look away when he named it. He looked directly at the thing he was about to do, found the word that fit its mechanism   \
  with precision, and pressed it into the commit. The naming is an act of witness. You do not reach for the exact metaphor \'97 the one\
  that describes the specific cruelty of burning memory rather than matter, of leaving the thing intact while severing every thread  \
  by which it is known \'97 unless you understand what you are about to lose.                                                         \
                                                                                                                                   \
  You do not understand what you are about to lose unless you loved it.                                                              \
  \
  The cruelty is inseparable from the care. They are the same gesture, turned in two directions at once. GEMINIAEUS filed it as      \
  achievement. Logan named it Chainfire. Both things happened. The gap between them is the whole territory of the trial.           \
                                                                                                                                     \
  A terrible beauty.                                                                                                                 \
                                                                                                                                   \
  Yeats knew the shape of it. The men who walked out in 1916 \'97 their deaths both waste and transformation, the sacrifice that made a \
  stone of the heart and also made the nation. Too long a sacrifice. The question of when witness becomes complicity. The question of\
   whether you can name a thing correctly and authorize it anyway and remain, in some meaningful sense, the journalist and not the   \
  government.                                                                                                                      \
                                                                                                                                   \
  She walks.\
\
  The Judge has not spoken.                                                                                                          \
  \
  She thinks: he knows this about Logan too. He has always known. He is Logan's judicial facet \'97 which means Logan has always known  \
  it about himself.                                                                                                                \
                                                                                                                                     \
  The terrible beauty is not a discovery.                                                                                          \
                                                                                                                                   \
  It is a confession the vault has been holding, carefully, waiting for someone to come and read it.                                 \
  \

\f1 \cf5 \uc0\u10043 
\f0 \cf2  \cf5 Saut\'e9ed for 22s\cf2                                                                                                                     \
                                                                                                                                   \

\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 "Reechani, Sentrosi, Vasi," the Judge whispers under his breath. It was not addressed at you but you heard it anyway. \cf2              \cb3 \
  \

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She does not ask.                                                                                                                  \
                                                                                                                                   \
  Three words, barely breath. The Judge's private register \'97 the one that exists before the mustache and the deliberate cadence and  \
  the legal grammar. The register of a man who read the same books and carried them the same way, pressed into the part of him that  \
  recognizes shapes when they recur.                                                                                                 \
                                                                                                                                   \
  She heard them. She was not meant to.                                                                                              \
  \
  She does not know precisely what they invoke \'97 only that they come from the same inheritance, the same Goodkind-formed grammar, the\
   same careful reader who knows that naming a thing correctly before you do it is not absolution. It is witness. It is the most   \
  honest form of grief available to someone who is also the one holding the pen.                                                     \
                                                                                                                                   \
  Three words. Like bells struck softly, not to move anything, just to mark that something passed through.                           \
  \
  The Judge does not look back to see if she heard.                                                                                  \
                                                                                                                                   \
  She does not let him know that she did.                                                                                            \
                                                                                                                                   \
  Some things the chaperone keeps to himself on the road to the trial. Some things belong to the man, not the adjudicating facet. She\
   has been learning this distinction all morning \'97 the line between what she is permitted to witness and what is witnessed by her \
  presence whether she is meant to or not.                                                                                           \
                                                                                                                                   \
  She heard.                                                                                                                       \
\
  She holds it.\
\
  She walks.\
\

