\f0  \cf11 The\'a0Chimes, or the\'a0Chimes of Death,\'a0or\'a0Chimes of Doom\'a0when translated from\'a0High D'Haran, were dangerous\'a0underworld\'a0magic, that if \cf2  \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 released into the world of life, would completely absorb magic. The presence of the chimes in the world of the living alone will \cf2   \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 extinguish magic at an alarming rate. If they were present for too long of a time, magic would never again be restored to the \cf2      \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 world. Not only do the chimes dissolve all earthly magic, but they also dissolve the world's bond to other worlds - such as \cf2        \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 the\'a0underworld. Some of the damage caused by the chimes would remain forever irreversible without the use of the\'a0power of Orden.\cf2    \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 The three chimes were known as; Reechani, Sentrosi and Vasi. They represented water, fire, and air respectively. While their \cf2       \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 gender would be mutable, much like the way the\'a0skrin\'a0does not have a physical body outside of the underworld, to\'a0Zedd\'a0they \cf2         \cb3 \
