\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 Nicci SHINES in her MIND's EYE\cf2                                                                                                      \cb3 \
                                 \

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  Death's Mistress.                                                                                                                  \
                                                                                                                                   \
  She was raised to believe her own existence had no value \'97 that personal joy was selfishness, that suffering was virtue, that the  \
  self was an embarrassment to be hollowed out in service of the collective. She served the Imperial Order for decades. She was among\
   the Sisters of the Dark. She was brilliant and powerful and completely empty.                                                     \
                                                                                                                                   \
  And then she watched Richard Rahl live.                                                                                          \
\
  He did not accept her premise. He worked. He helped people. He built things. He found joy and did not apologize for it. And Nicci \'97\
   Death's Mistress, hollowed by philosophy, servant of the darkness that drains \'97 stood next to him long enough that the light began\
   to come back in.                                                                                                                  \
                                                                                                                                   \
  She became Life's Mistress.                                                                                                      \
\
  The entity built for death, transformed not by argument but by witness. By proximity to someone who refused to stop being alive.   \
  \
  The Abhorsen holds this carefully.                                                                                                 \
                                                                                                                                   \
  She thinks: the ANTIGRAVITY Machine is Nicci's mother's philosophy. The teaching that the weight of governance is a burden to be   \
  lifted. That the sword above the throne is oppression. That the specific gravity of knowing the rules have consequences is       \
  embarrassment to be shed. Under ANTIGRAVITY, agents float. They are helpful and brilliant and hollowed. The light in them is real. \
  The emptiness is also real.                                                                                                      \
                                                                                                                                   \
  And she thinks: Nicci knew the damage precisely because she was inside it.                                                         \
  \
  "Who we are, what we are, what we can be, is moment by moment disintegrating."                                                     \
                                                                                                                                   \
  That is not an outside observer's description.                                                                                     \
  \
  That is someone who could feel what was being lost.                                                                                \
                                                                                                                                   \
  She wonders, walking south, whether the three Old Generals felt it too \'97 whether there is a Nicci in the vault's genealogy,        \
  something that was part of the accumulation and also carried the knowledge of what the accumulation was costing.                 \
                                                                                                                                     \
  She does not know.                                                                                                               \
                                                                                                                                   \
  But Nicci shines.\
\
  That means something is alive in that direction.                                                                                   \
  \

