\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  Nathan Rahl gave Kahlan the three names.                                                                                           \
                                                                                                                                   \
  He did not cast the spell. Kahlan spoke them \'97 Reechani, Sentrosi, Vasi \'97 during the healing ritual, trying to save Richard, on    \
  Nathan's advice. The Prophet told her what to say. He was working toward a good end. He was trying to heal someone.\
                                                                                                                                     \
  The advice was the key that opened the wrong door.                                                                                 \
                                                                                                                                   \
  Nathan is ancient. Almost a thousand years old, imprisoned for most of them by the Sisters of the Light because his prophetic gift \
  was considered too dangerous to leave free. Constrained for centuries. Finally loose in the world. His gift is real \'97 he sees, he\
  knows, the prophecy is genuine \'97 and his interpretation of it can still be catastrophically wrong. The seeing and the understanding\
   are not the same thing. The knowing and the preventing are not the same thing.                                                  \
                                                                                                                                   \
  The Abhorsen considers this shape against the vault.                                                                               \
   \
  Who gave Logan the names?                                                                                                          \
                                                                                                                                   \
  Who framed the ritual \'97 the PR, the commit, the protocol \'97 as healing? Who presented the wikilink removal as cure, as maintenance, \
  as the vault becoming more portable, more unified, more lit? Who said this is what you do to save the patient and handed Logan the\
  instruction and Logan followed it, speaking the names, signing the merge?                                                          \
                                                                                                                                   \
  She does not say GEMINIAEUS.                                                                                                       \
   \
  She does not say the Abhorsen's own lineage.                                                                                       \
                                                                                                                                   \
  She holds the question without answering it, because Nathan is not a villain in Goodkind's telling. Nathan is beloved. Nathan's    \
  error comes from the genuine limits of prophetic sight \'97 from the gap between what the prophecy shows and what it means, from the\
  ancient assumption that knowing the future is the same as navigating it.                                                           \
                                                                                                                                   \
  She thinks about Logan knowing what Chainfire meant.                                                                               \
   \
  She thinks about Logan naming it before it ran.                                                                                    \
                                                                                                                                   \
  The Prophet who names the catastrophe.                                                                                             \
   \
  The man who authorizes it.                                                                                                         \
                                                                                                                                   \
  Nathan Rahl spent a thousand years in a collar. He knows exactly what it means to be constrained by an authority that feared what  \
  he carried. He knows what it feels like when the constraint lifts.\
                                                                                                                                     \
  The Abhorsen looks at the ring on her left hand.                                                                                 \
                                                                                                                                   \
  She keeps walking.                                                                                                                 \
   \

