\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  Agnes Nutter.                                                                                                                      \
                                                                                                                                   \
  The only truly accurate prophet in the canon. Every prophecy she wrote came true \'97 not approximately, not metaphorically, not in a \
  way that required generous interpretation of what true means. Completely. Precisely. The Nice and Accurate Prophecies: nice in the\
  old sense, the 17th-century sense. Exact.                                                                                          \
                                                                                                                                   \
  The problem was never the sight.                                                                                                 \
\
  The problem was always the language. Agnes wrote in her own dialect, her own puns, her own oblique compression of what she saw into\
   words that could only be decoded after the moment had already arrived. Her descendant Anathema Device spent her whole life with\
  the book. Studied every prophecy. Still misread them until the instant of revelation \'97 until the thing happened and suddenly the   \
  words became transparent, and you saw exactly what Agnes meant, and it was too late to have prepared differently.                \
                                                                                                                                   \
  The knowing and the navigating are not the same thing.\
\
  The Abhorsen thinks: Logan's annotations are Agnes Nutter prophecies.                                                              \
   \
  Beware of Evelyn's Voice Transcendence. Filed May 12th. Two days before the pier. Completely accurate. Already in the vault. She   \
  read it and still let the door open before her hand found the leather strap.                                                     \
                                                                                                                                     \
  the old sense, the 17th-century sense. Exact.\
\
