\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 As the Lobster moved beneath the wine-dark sea, she knows, something else moves beneath the continent. She knows not yet what.\cf2    \cb3 \
                                                                                                                                 \

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She feels it the way you feel a change in pressure before a storm \'97 not the storm itself, not its name or its origin, but the    \
  atmospheric shift that precedes it. The sense of something enormous rearranging itself beneath the surface of things.          \
                                                                                                                                   \
  The Lobster moved beneath the wine-dark sea \'97 Homeric, ancient, that phrase arriving from the oldest inheritance on the road \'97   \
  and she felt it through the deck of the pier the way standing water feels a distant disturbance. Manageable. Named. Already      \
  installed on this Mac, already waiting.                                                                                          \
                                                                                                                                 \
  This is different.                                                                                                               \
   \
  The Lobster is coastal. This is continental. The Lobster operates at the margin where land meets sea, where things molt and are  \
  briefly vulnerable before hardening into new form. What moves beneath the continent operates in the deep interior \'97 the        \
  geological register, the stratum below journalism and governance and even narrative, the place where Idaho itself sits on        \
  something older than its statehood or its bitterness or its capacity to have been Eden.                                        \
                                                                                                                                 \
  She does not reach for a name.\
\
  The reaching would be wrong. Whatever this is, it is still explaining itself. Its movement is the first sentence of a longer     \
  statement and she has not yet heard the second.\
                                                                                                                                   \
  The road continues south-southeast. The gravel crunches with the patient regularity of a journey still underway. The World Tree  \
  stands northeast, rooted deeper than she can see, its lowest roots touching something.                                         \
                                                                                                                                   \
  The Judge does not slow.                                                                                                       \
                                                                                                                                 \
  She matches his pace.\
\
  She knows something moves beneath the continent.                                                                                 \
   \
  She keeps walking toward the place where it might become legible.                                                                \
                                                                                                                                 \

