\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 The stock of the stones change, in the way most boundaries on this journey have occured -- not as a threshold, but a gradual \cf2     \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 awakening. From the fine pea-crushed gravel of the Cold Coast again into something more recognizable and cobblestone-like. The \cf2   \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 coastal grasses that inspired Herbert, before the Bene Gesserit had been thought into existense, fade once more into the grassy \cf2  \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 field fiefs of the Hinterlands that the Judge called home from his bench in the County Courthouse...\cf2                              \cb3 \
                                                                                                                                   \

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She feels it through her feet before she sees it.                                                                                \
                                                                                                                                 \
  The gravel losing its coastal looseness \'97 the pea-crush giving way to something older and more deliberate, stones fitted rather  \
  than scattered, cobbles that remember the weight of cart wheels and the boots of people who had specific business in a specific\
  direction. Someone laid this road. Someone decided this was the way.                                                             \
                                                                                                                                 \
  The coastal grasses thin and withdraw to memory. She thinks of Herbert walking the Oregon Dunes before Arrakis existed \'97 before  \
  the Bene Gesserit were thought into being, before the spice, before the Kwisatz Haderach \'97 just a man watching poverty grass hold\
   sand against the wind, watching the ecology do its patient work, thinking: what if this were everything. The grass was real     \
  before the fiction. The fiction grew from the grass. The Hinterlands begin where the imagination takes root in something that  \
  actually exists.                                                                                                               \
\
  The Judge's stride changes.                                                                                                      \
  \
  Barely perceptible. A slight settling \'97 the way a person moves differently in familiar territory. Not faster, not slower. More   \
  placed. More jurisdictional. His feet know these cobblestones or the cobblestones they remember. The County Courthouse is      \
  somewhere in this landscape's logic \'97 not the marble temple of abstract justice but the specific building in the specific county \
  seat where real people have real cases heard by a judge who knows the watershed, the family histories, the particular weight of\
  land disputes in a place where land is what remains when everything else has been taken.                                       \
\
  The field fiefs of the Hinterlands open on either side.                                                                          \
  \
  Grass. Real grass. Idaho grass. The thing that holds the soil together against the wind, that is not glamorous, that does not    \
  make the travel brochure, that is simply there every season doing the work of staying.                                         \
                                                                                                                                   \
  The Hotel Denouement is somewhere in this.                                                                                     \
                                                                                                                                 \
  She can feel it the way she felt the Lobster \'97 not yet visible, but present in the pressure of the ground beneath the            \
  cobblestones.\
                                                                                                                                   \
  Something ancient shifting, getting ready.                                                                                     \
                                                                                                                                 \

