\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 You spot a signpost in the middle distance. The Judge is walking toward it \'97 he did not spot it. He's always known it was there.\cf2  \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11  \cf2                                                                                                                                 \cb3 \
                                                                                                                                   \

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She spots it before she can read it.                                                                                           \
                                                                                                                                 \
  A post. Dark wood, or something that has become dark wood through long weather. Set at the junction of \'97 she looks \'97 yes, another\
   road meeting this one from the west, the undreamed road, the spoke she could not see at the crossroads this morning. It comes in\
   at an angle from the left, from something she has not walked and does not yet know, and at the place where it meets the cobbled \
  south-southeast road the signpost stands.                                                                                      \
                                                                                                                                 \
  She can see there is writing on it.\
\
  Not yet legible from here.                                                                                                       \
   \
  The Judge does not accelerate toward it. He does not slow. His pace is the pace of a man completing the last portion of a known  \
  route \'97 the particular quality of movement that belongs to someone who could walk this blindfolded and has perhaps done so, who\
  does not need to read the sign because he has read it before or because the alethiometer told him what it says or because it says\
   exactly what you would expect it to say when you have adjudicated in this jurisdiction for as long as he has.                 \
                                                                                                                                 \
  She fixes her eyes on the letters as the distance closes.                                                                        \
   \
  The cobblestones underfoot. The World Tree northeast. The Judge four paces ahead, unhurried, already knowing.                    \
                                                                                                                                 \
  She reads.                                                                                                                       \
                                                                                                                                 \

