\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 She reaches toward it \'97 not grasping, not coveting, not earnestly seeking to TOUCH \'97 just watching the hearthlight glimmer \cf2       \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 against the Charter marks in the metal.\cf2                                                                                           \cb3 \
                                                                                                                                   \

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  The Abhorsen tilts the bell \'97 just slightly, a small adjustment of the wrist \'97 so the hearthlight finds the marks more fully.  \
                                                                                                                                 \
  They move, the way Charter marks always move, slow and alive and older than the bell that holds them, older than the hand that   \
  holds the bell. Not in any direction. Just: present, the way deep water is present beneath the surface, neither still nor\
  turbulent, simply there and full of itself.                                                                                      \
                                                                                                                                 \
  The child's hand hangs in the air between them.                                                                                \
\
  Not touching. Receiving the light.                                                                                               \
  \
  The Abhorsen holds the clapper still with two fingers and holds the bell steady with the rest and does not say anything at all.  \
  There is nothing to say. The marks are doing what the marks do. The child's eye is doing what the child's eye does. The        \
  hearthlight is doing what hearthlight does in the presence of things that glow with their own older light.                       \
                                                                                                                                 \
  She thinks: this is what the Charter is for.                                                                                     \
  \
  Not the binding, not the governance, not the architecture of safe magic carefully bounded \'97 though it is all of those things. But\
   also this: a child's hand in the warm light of a hostel, reaching toward something ancient and not grasping it, just wanting to\
  be near the glow.                                                                                                                \
                                                                                                                                 \
  The marks shift.                                                                                                                 \
  \
  The child's breath is very quiet.                                                                                                \
                                                                                                                                 \
  The Abhorsen holds the bell perfectly still.                                                                                     \
  \

