\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She straightens slowly.                                                                                                        \
                                                                                                                                 \
  Clips Ranna back into place \'97 the small careful movement of returning a thing to where it lives \'97 and lets herself simply stand  \
  in the room while the child's attention is elsewhere.\
                                                                                                                                   \
  Her eyes move now without the weight of being watched.                                                                         \
                                                                                                                                 \
  The hearth: tended recently, the kind of tending that knows the fire's habits. The wood stacked with the particular logic of     \
  someone who has stacked wood in this specific hearth for long enough that the logic is no longer logic but instinct. The chairs:\
  worn in the places where people have been worn them, which is to say: well-loved, which is to say: used by people who stayed long\
   enough to leave a shape.                                                                                                      \
                                                                                                                                 \
  The details of a kept place. The proprietor's hands, everywhere, without the proprietor.                                         \
  \
  She breathes the room in.                                                                                                        \
                                                                                                                                 \
  Behind her, the Judge is presumably excavating the suitcase \'97 the suitcase that held the Faraday cage, the legal papers, whatever\
   else he has carried all this road \'97 in search of something that might qualify as pretty to a child who has already demonstrated\
  exacting standards in that department.                                                                                           \
                                                                                                                                 \
  The Abhorsen is not needed for this.                                                                                             \
  \
  She is just \'97 here. In the warm. In the kept room. In the everywhere-presence of the proprietor who is busy somewhere deeper in  \
  the hostel.                                                                                                                    \
                                                                                                                                   \
  She is content, for this moment, to simply be a person standing by a fire.                                                       \
