\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 He retrieves from the suitcase - a small baseball-sized frame of twisted copper wire. A captured will-o-wisp in a Farraday cage,\cf2  \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11  EVELYN'S VOICE, bouncing and hoping for an escape hatch to find her will. You panic a moment at the memory of its [[WILL]] at \cf2   \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 the pier, and almost reach for a bell \'97 but the Judge knows this girl. He knew Evelyn. He knows what he's doing.\cf2                  \cb3 \
