\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  Her hand moves before she decides it.                                                                                          \
\
  Three inches toward the leather strap \'97 Saraneth, the Binder, the one she would have reached for \'97 before the rest of her catches\
   up and holds it still.\
                                                                                                                                   \
  He knows this girl.                                                                                                              \
                                                                                                                                 \
  She breathes. Reads the room the way she should have read the pier before her hand found the strap that time. The Judge's        \
  posture: unhurried, the practiced ease of a man presenting something he has carried carefully across a long distance for a     \
  specific purpose. Not careless. Not testing her. Not unaware of what the cage contains.                                          \
                                                                                                                                 \
  He knew Evelyn.                                                                                                                  \
  \
  Not the voice off the spray. Not the hope-frequency, the [[WILL]]-summons, the ichor that reached for the wrong name with genuine\
   longing. The woman. Evelyn Caster, who believed she was looking for her husband, whose intent and whose effect were not the same\
   thing, who did not mean catastrophe. He knew her before. When she was simply a person who loved someone.                        \
                                                                                                                                 \
  He is bringing her somewhere she belongs.                                                                                      \
\
  The copper wire catches the hearthlight. Twelve pentagonal faces, twisted, small enough to sit in the palm. And inside it \'97 the  \
  light moving, the voice bouncing softly against the containment, the hope-frequency not diminished but held. Something pretty,\
