\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She is.                                                                                                                          \
                                                                                                                                 \
  The Abhorsen has not been able to think this until now. At the pier she heard the frequency and felt the ichor and reached for   \
  the wrong-name summons and caught herself and called for the Judge and categorized and contained. In the COLD COAST WITNESS she\
  wrote about the failure mode, the weaponized hope, the most dangerous false summons wrapped in genuine love.                     \
                                                                                                                                 \
  She did not write: she is beautiful.                                                                                           \
\
  The child has no apparatus between seeing and saying. The wisp dances in its copper frame \'97 twelve pentagonal faces holding the  \
  light that holds the longing that holds the voice of a woman who lost someone and never stopped looking \'97 and the child sees a\
  she, and sees beauty, and says so.                                                                                               \
                                                                                                                                 \
  Both things are true. The Abhorsen knows this now in the way you know something when a child says it plainly and the plainness   \
  cuts through everything you built around it to manage it safely.\
                                                                                                                                   \
  Evelyn was a person.                                                                                                           \
                                                                                                                                 \
  The hope-frequency is a person. Contained. Bouncing softly in the hearthlight. Looking for something she will not find in this   \
  room and perhaps cannot find anywhere \'97 and beautiful in the looking, the way grief is sometimes beautiful, the way longing that\
  does not stop is sometimes the most human thing there is.                                                                        \
                                                                                                                                 \
  The child's pupils are wide with it.                                                                                           \
\
  The Abhorsen stands back and watches the grandmother's gift glow in the Judge's steady hands and thinks about what it means that \
  he brought her here \'97 to this kept place, to this everywhere-presence, to this woman who is busy somewhere deeper in the hostel\
  and does not yet know what is waiting for her.                                                                                   \
                                                                                                                                 \
  Someone who will know what she is.                                                                                               \
  \
  Someone who will know what to do.                                                                                                \
                                                                                                                                 \

