\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 He gently hands the girl the vessel. She takes it, gingerly - almost reverently, or as reverently as a child can comprehend to \cf2   \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 take something. "For your grandmother," he reminds her. "And don't tell Mother."\cf2                                                  \cb3 \
\cb10                                                                                                                                    \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 A cheeky grin breaks across her cherubic face \'97 a secret, one shared with a beloved co-conspirator. Even better than a doll from\cf2  \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11  a sweaty eve at the carnival.\cf2                                                                                                    \cb3 \
\cb10                                                                                                                                    \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 "We need two rooms for the night," he says. "Would you let her know?" The child nods. "Dinner tonight?" she asks. "Yes, please,"\cf2  \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11  the lawman replies. The young maiden turns her attention again to you. "Dinner?"\cf2                                                 \cb3 \
