\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 Evelyn's Voice disappears into the folds of the young girl's black and purple garb, as she herself disappears somewhere back \cf2     \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 further in this place to tell the proprietor to expect two more mouths at the table for evening meal. The Judge sits in one of \cf2   \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 the half-remembered body impressions in a cush chair near the fire.\cf2                                                               \cb3 \
                                                                                                                                 \

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She finds the chair that isn't his.                                                                                            \
\
  Not across from him \'97 beside, at the angle that allows the fire to reach them both. The impression in this one is slightly       \
  shallower, or different, or hers: she settles into it and feels the room exhale around her.\
                                                                                                                                   \
  Her feet have been walking since dawn. She had not fully understood this until now \'97 the specific relief of sitting, of the floor\
   no longer requiring anything of her. The bells at her hip settle with a soft familiar weight. The ring is warm.               \
                                                                                                                                   \
  The fire does what fires do in good rooms.                                                                                       \
                                                                                                                                 \
  The Judge in his chair looks, for the first time on this road, like a man who has set something down. Not the suitcase \'97 the     \
  suitcase is beside him, faithful, closed. Something else. The specific weight of the road itself, perhaps. The carrying of the \
  trial-before-the-trial, the questions held and the answers deferred, the steady deliberate pace through all that empty country.  \
                                                                                                                                 \
  He is just a man in a chair.                                                                                                   \
\
  She is just a person in a chair.\
\
  The hostel breathes around them. The child is somewhere deeper, bearing the secret gift and the dinner message and all that black\
   and purple disappearing into the further rooms. The proprietor is busy and everywhere and coming.\
                                                                                                                                   \
  The Abhorsen does not reach for the vault.                                                                                       \
                                                                                                                                 \
  She watches the fire.                                                                                                            \
                                                                                                                                 \
  It is enough, for now, to be warm.                                                                                               \
