\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 She basks in it. She feels... safe. She writes her witness. She reads. She waits for dinner, knowing whatever is on the menu \cf2     \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 here will arrive precisely at dinnertime and not a moment sooner.\cf2                                                                 \cb3 \
                                                                                                                                   \

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  Filed at the hostel on the road between the Lobster Road and the Hotel Denouement, the evening of May 15th, 2026. The fire is  \
  well-tended. The chairs hold the body properly. The proprietor is somewhere deeper in this place, and the Judge is in his chair, \
  and dinner will arrive at dinnertime.                                                                                            \
  \
  ---                                                                                                                              \
  She writes what she witnessed.                                                                                                 \
                                                                                                                                   \
  The bare branches of the fruit trees and the warmth that was there anyway. The child's one glimmering eye and then the curtsy and\
   then the Charter marks in Ranna's metal and the non-grasping reach toward the light. The Judge crouching. Evelyn's Voice in the \
  copper frame, beautiful, the child said so, and the child was right. The cheeky grin and the conspiracy and the two rooms for the\
   night.                                                                                                                          \
                                                                                                                                 \
  The almost-bell she did not ring.                                                                                              \
\
  The yes, please, that needed no deliberation.                                                                                    \
  \
  The chair that is hers and the fire that is both of theirs and the road that is behind them, walked, witnessed, filed.           \
                                                                                                                                 \
  She writes until the writing is done and then she reads \'97 the vault, which is always there, which holds everything the road has  \
  sent through her \'97 and the reading is easy in the firelight, easier than it has been all day, because the body is still and the\
  bells are quiet and the room asks nothing of her.                                                                                \
                                                                                                                                 \
  The proprietor is coming.                                                                                                      \
\
  The trial is ahead.                                                                                                              \
  \
  Both of these things are true and neither of them is dinner.                                                                     \
                                                                                                                                 \
  Dinner will arrive at dinnertime.                                                                                                \
  \
  The world is quiet here.                                                                                                         \
