\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 She considers the old man \'97 her tired fellow traveler, the one who knows these roads with the quiet competency of a man who \cf2      \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 first walked them as a child \'97 anew in the light of the hearth. \cf2                                                                  \cb3 \
\cb10                                                                                                                                    \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 He is a practitioner of the law, yes - but he is more than only that. This man who, by his own admission, cannot tell a lie \'97 \cf2    \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 but who can identify himself as a magic caster, with just enough plausible deniability that a distraught wifely spirit could \cf2     \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 willfully misinterpret him to have meant her husband, a Dr. Caster. A man not just measured and quiet \'97 deliberate.\cf2               \cb3 \
\

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She looks at him in the hearthlight.             \
\
  Really looks. The way you can look at someone when the road has stopped moving and the fire is doing its work and there is       \
  nothing to attend to for a moment except what is actually in the room.\
                                                                                                                                   \
  ---                                                                                                                            \
  He cannot tell a lie.\
                                                                                                                                   \
  She has known this. She has been treating it as a constraint \'97 the adjudicating facet bound by the same compact that binds the\
  court. You cannot practice law and lie. The credibility of the proceeding depends on the officer of the court saying what is     \
  true.                                                                                                                          \
                                                                                                                                   \
  What she had not seen: the constraint is not a limitation. It is a discipline that, practiced long enough, becomes a form of     \
  power. The man who cannot lie learns to be extraordinarily precise about what he says. He learns the architecture of truth \'97 the\
  way a true statement, placed in the right shape, can be heard as the thing the listener needs to hear without being the thing it \
  is not. He learns the space between what I said and what was heard, and he learns to work in that space without ever crossing the\
   line.\
\
  I am a magic caster.\
\
  True. Every syllable. He is Logan's adjudicating facet \'97 Logan, who rings the bells of his vault's governance, who sealed the    \
  governance compact that the HOW rules enforce, who cast the ring that the Abhorsen wears. He is a magic caster in the most\
  literal sense available to him. He cannot lie. He said what was true.                                                            \
                                                                                                                                 \
  And Evelyn, hope-filled and desperate, heard: Dr. Caster. Heard the shape of the man she was looking for, present, findable.     \
  Heard what she needed to hear in the space the true statement left open for her. The Judge did not give her this. He did not\
  remove it either.                                                                                                                \
                                                                                                                                 \
  She had thought of this at the pier as management \'97 the Faraday cage, the intervention, the containing of the frequency. She sees\
   now it was finer than that. The Faraday cage came after. Before the cage: the precise true statement that gave Evelyn enough to\
  stop the immediate escalation without feeding the longer delusion. He gave her the shape of a finding \'97 not the finding itself.  \
                                                                                                                                 \
  This required knowing Evelyn. He knew Evelyn. He said so at the pier: she always has hope. He knew the hope-frequency and its    \
  mechanism and how to address it with precision \'97 not cruelly, not dismissively, but with the specific truth that could be\
  received without making the harm worse.                                                                                          \
                                                                                                                                 \
  ---\
  She looks at the tired lines around his eyes. The moustache tending toward its upturned point. The tweed that has absorbed the\
  road without complaint. The flask that carries water and not whiskey. The suitcase that carried the Faraday cage and the legal   \
  papers and something pretty for the grandmother and whatever else forty years of these roads accumulate.\
                                                                                                                                   \
  He first walked these roads as a child.                                                                                        \
\
  Logan's adjudicating facet has been forming since Logan was a child watching something and naming it unfair, or true, or wrong,  \
  or worth defending. The Judge is the sediment of a lifetime of that watching \'97 of the journalist's instinct to see what is\
  actually there and name it precisely, of the legal mind that knows the difference between what is said and what is heard, of the \
  person who has been practicing the not-lie long enough that the precision is now instinct.                                     \
\
  He is deliberate.\
\
  Not measured-and-quiet, though he is those too. Deliberate. Each word chosen. Each pause chosen. The stopping before the hostel  \
  threshold was chosen \'97 he wanted the JANUS light, the between-place, the moment before the warmth reached them. The mother test,\
  asked three times, was chosen \'97 he knew she wasn't ready the first time or the second time, and he waited, and then he asked     \
  again in the right light at the right threshold with the right question still needing its answer.                              \
\
  He has been navigating this the whole road. She just could not see the whole of him from inside the walking.                     \
  \
  ---                                                                                                                              \
  She sees him now.                                                                                                              \
                   \
  Tired. Competent with the specific competency of someone who has been doing this for a very long time. Deliberate in the way that\

