\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  The Abhorsen looks up from the chair.                     \
\
  Something has changed. She cannot say what. The girl stands in the threshold between the deeper rooms and this room \'97 the firelit\
   room, the room with the chairs and the old man and the stranger \'97 and she is the same girl she was when she disappeared with\
  Evelyn's Voice folded into her garb. Same hair. Same black and purple. Same one glimmering eye now both glimmering.              \
                                                                                                                                 \
  But time has done something. Not much. Not enough to name. The way a face looks different after it has held a secret \'97 not       \
  because the face has changed, but because the face now contains something it did not contain before.\
                                                                                                                                   \
  She has been in the grandmother's room.                                                                                          \
  \
  The Abhorsen does not ask what the grandmother said. She does not ask what the child witnessed when Evelyn's Voice was placed in \
  the grandmother's hands. She does not ask what passed between the woman who is everywhere in this kept place and the small girl\
  who carries messages and gifts into the deeper rooms.                                                                            \
                                                                                                                                 \
  She reads.\
\
  The child is back. The child has been somewhere that the Abhorsen has not been. The child has seen something the Abhorsen has not\
   seen. The child is looking at the fire now, standing in the threshold, neither fully in the room nor fully returned to the\
  deeper hall \'97 standing in the JANUS space, in the between, neither the errand nor its aftermath.                                 \
                                                                                                                                 \
  The Abhorsen waits.\
\
  The fire does what fire does.\
\

