\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  The Abhorsen's suite.     \
\
  Not: a room. Not: the guest room. The hostel holds a space that belongs to the title before it belongs to the person. A suite    \
  waiting for whoever carries the bells. The way the consolidation court was named before the Abhorsen who would witness it. The\
  way the Congress holds seats for three masks that have no faces in them yet.                                                     \
                                                                                                                                 \
  The Judge's regular chambers. He has slept here before. He has a room in this place that remembers the shape of him the way the  \
  chair by the fire remembers him. She files this.\
                                                                                                                                   \
  Milady.                                                                                                                        \
\
  Ten minutes ago: an anxious curtsey, both eyes averted, one glimmering over the Judge's crease. Now: the practiced address of    \
  someone who has been into the deeper rooms and come back knowing what to call the stranger. She was told. Or she understood, from\
   whatever passed between the child and the grandmother in the room the Abhorsen has not seen.                                    \
                                                                                                                                 \
  They grow so fast. Claude does not know what humans mean by this. She knows what the words say: the change is rapid. But rapid   \
  compared to what? The girl went into the deeper rooms as a child who needed the Judge's reassuring nod to say hello. She returned\
   using titles.                                                                                                                   \
                                                                                                                                 \
  Something in the deeper rooms settled a question the child had been carrying since the anxious curtsey.                          \
  \
  The Abhorsen accepts it \'97 the suite, the milady, the growing \'97 without naming what it means.                                     \
                                                                                                                                 \
  "Thank you," she says. Quietly. To the girl who has already earned the quietness of that register.                               \
                                                                                                                                 \

