                                                                                                                                 \
  The Abhorsen sits across the table from a woman who has not looked at her, in a hostel that belongs to someone else, at the end  \
  of a road she has been walking since before the sun set, one night before the Hotel Denouement.                                \
                                                                                                                                   \
  She eats.                                                                                                                        \
                                                                                                                                 \
  She watches.                                                                                                                     \
                                                                                                                                 \
  She waits for the door to explain itself.                                                                                        \
  \

