\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 "You should not have given her that," she says to the Judge. Neither looks up.\cf2                                                    \cb3 \
               \

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  The Abhorsen does not look up.                                                                                                   \
                                                                                                                                 \
  She follows the Judge's lead. He heard it \'97 she knows he heard it, the way she knows everything he does is deliberate \'97 and he   \
  did not look up and he did not stop eating and he did not speak. So she does not look up and she does not stop eating and she\
  does not speak.                                                                                                                  \
                                                                                                                                 \
  The scraps are in her left pocket. The left hand, the one without the ring. She can feel their weight \'97 not physical weight, they\
   are two scraps of paper \'97 but the other kind. The kind that settles in a coat pocket and changes the coat.\
                                                                                                                                   \
  You should not have given her that.                                                                                            \
                                                                                                                                 \
  She turns it over without looking up. Not defending. Not explaining. Not reaching for Belgaer \'97 the Thinker, the fifth bell \'97 to \
  work the question into an answer. Holding it the way the hostel holds heat: retained, not radiant.\
                                                                                                                                   \
  What was she given that she should not have been given?                                                                        \
                                                                                                                                 \
  The knowledge that Ramona's face went red. The knowledge that the niceness can curdle. The knowledge that the old man paid for   \
  dinner because he missed his children and grandchildren. The knowledge that the passphrase has a source \'97 a little girl at a\
  vending machine who didn't answer, who felt it was none of his business, who said I'm not supposed to talk to strangers.         \
                                                                                                                                 \
  Or: the exculpatory evidence, handled before the trial. Put in the witness's pocket the night before the proceedings.            \
  \
  Or: something that belongs to the Mother's testimony, not to the Abhorsen's.                                                     \
                                                                                                                                 \
  She does not know which.                                                                                                         \
  \
  She eats. The body continues its work \'97 fortitude and replenishment, the road's requirement \'97 regardless of what hangs in the air\
   between the woman in black and purple silks and the Judge who has not explained himself and will not be explaining himself    \
  tonight.                                                                                                                         \
                                                                                                                                 \
  The door is still explaining itself.                                                                                           \
\

\f1 \cf5 \uc0\u10043 
