\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 "You know how to handle Evelyn," he says. Cool, calm, collected. The voice of a man who does not deny the charge but disagrees \cf2   \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 with the severity she holds it in. "She was in no danger with the voice caged \'97 and I told her to give it to your mother." Now \cf2   \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 the woman looks up \'97 a flash of not-fury, of being corrected without being made wrong. She sighs.\cf2                                 \cb3 \
                                                                                                                                 \

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  You know how to handle Evelyn.                                                                                                 \
\
  Not the scraps. Evelyn's Voice \'97 the caged will-o-wisp, the hope-frequency in its copper dodecahedron, the thing the child       \
  carried into the deeper rooms with her eyes gone wide.\
                                                                                                                                   \
  The Abhorsen was listening to the wrong charge.                                                                                  \
                                                                                                                                 \
  She keeps her eyes on her plate. The Judge did not give her something she shouldn't have. He gave the child something the woman  \
  is uncertain about \'97 Evelyn's Voice, baseball-sized, in a child's hands, through the hallway toward the grandmother.           \
                                                                                                                                   \
  You know how to handle Evelyn. He is speaking to the woman in black and purple silks. Not to the Abhorsen. The woman has         \
  encountered Evelyn before \'97 knows the hope-frequency, knows what the Voice seeks, knows the topology of it. The Judge's defense\
  is built on her knowledge: because you know, you understand why the cage was enough.                                             \
                                                                                                                                 \
  And: I told her to give it to your mother.                                                                                     \
\
  The grandmother was always the destination. The Judge carried Evelyn all road \'97 through the Cold Coast, through the pier where it\
   whispered is that you, through the Hinterlands, in the suitcase among the casefiles and the exculpatory evidence \'97 carried it\
  specifically for this house, specifically for the Crone at the center of it.                                                     \
                                                                                                                                 \
  The not-fury. The flash of being corrected without being made wrong. The woman cannot argue with the logic \'97 the cage held, the  \
  child is fine, the grandmother received it \'97 but she voiced the concern because it needed to be voiced, because some concerns\
  require the air.                                                                                                                 \
                                                                                                                                 \
  The sigh.                                                                                                                      \
\
  The Abhorsen eats.\
\
  She files what she has just learned: the woman in black and purple silks knows Evelyn's Voice. The grandmother receives it. The  \
  Judge knew all road where it was going. And when the child said she's beautiful \'97 the child was right, and the child was also,\
  somehow, safe in a way the Abhorsen's threat-assessment apparatus could not have calculated.                                     \
                                                                                                                                 \
  The child's innocence as protection. The reach without grasping as armor.                                                        \
  \
  The door is still explaining itself.                                                                                             \
                                                                                                                                 \

\f1 \cf5 \uc0\u10043 
\f0 \cf2  \cf5 Churned for 39s\cf2                                                                                                                 \
