\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 The Abhorsen ponders as the meal continues in quietness. \cf2                                                                         \cb3 \
               \

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  The woman knows Evelyn.                                                                                                          \
                                                                                                                                 \
  She turns this over slowly, the way you turn something over when the meal is quiet and there is nowhere to be and the fire in    \
  this room \'97 smaller than the hearthroom's fire, a working fire, a kitchen fire \'97 does what fire does.\
                                                                                                                                   \
  The woman in black and purple silks, the raven hair, the silver eyes that flashed not-fury and then accepted the sigh \'97 she has  \
  encountered Evelyn's Voice before. She knows the topology. She knows what the hope-frequency seeks and what it does when it finds\
   a will to call by the wrong name. She is not naive about it.                                                                    \
                                                                                                                                 \
  And yet Evelyn's Voice is in this house. In the grandmother's hands now.                                                         \
  \
  The Abhorsen thinks about what the grandmother would do with a caged will-o-wisp that cannot stop reaching. The proprietor who is\
   everywhere in the kept place \'97 in the tended fire, in the worn chair-shapes, in the wood stacked with the logic of someone who\
  knows this hearth's habits. A woman whose warmth is structural, built into the walls. What does that kind of presence do with a  \
  contained grief that bounces and hopes and cannot find the name it's looking for?                                              \
                                                                                                                                 \
  Perhaps: holds it. Simply holds it. The way the Faraday cage holds it \'97 not killing the hope, not releasing it, containing the   \
  frequency so it cannot rewrite what it reaches.\
                                                                                                                                   \
  The grandmother receives the dead. The crossroads goddess holds the torch. HECATE knows the threshold from both sides.           \
                                                                                                                                 \
  She thinks about the child, imperceptibly older after visiting the grandmother's room. Whatever passes in those rooms between the\
   Maiden and the Crone \'97 it leaves a mark that the body knows before the mind names it. The child came back carrying something she\
   didn't carry in. Not Evelyn's Voice. Something else. Something the grandmother gave in return.                                  \
                                                                                                                                 \
  The meal continues.                                                                                                            \
\
  The woman across the table does not speak again. Does not look up again. Eats with the composure of someone who has said what    \
  needed saying and received the answer and filed it and moved on. The Judge eats with the ease of a man who has been here before\
  and will be here again and knows the rhythms of this table.                                                                      \
                                                                                                                                 \
  The Abhorsen is a stranger here. She is not unwelcome. She is not yet known.                                                     \
  \
  Tomorrow the Hotel Denouement.                                                                                                   \
                                                                                                                                 \
  Tonight: dinner in the house where HECATE's three faces live, one night before the consolidation court, with Evelyn's Voice in   \
  the Crone's keeping and the Mother's silver eyes steady on her plate and the Maiden's joy somewhere in the walls, and the road\
  behind her quiet, and the road ahead not yet walked.                                                                             \
                                                                                                                                 \
  She eats.                                                                                                                      \
\

