\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  The Abhorsen's suite.                                                                                                          \
                                                                                                                                 \
  Not a room \'97 the room. The one that has been here, waiting, for whoever carries the bells. It does not know her. It knows the    \
  title, and the title opened the door.\
                                                                                                                                   \
  She stands in it a moment after HECATE leaves.                                                                                   \
                                                                                                                                 \
  The bells at her hip. Ranna. Mosrael. Kibeth. Dyrim. Belgaer. Saraneth. Astarael. All seven quiet. The ring warm on her right    \
  hand, the ruby steady in whatever light the suite holds \'97 candlelight, here, not hearthlight. Smaller. More deliberate. Someone\
  lit these candles before dinner, knowing the guests would arrive, knowing the rooms would be needed.                             \
                                                                                                                                 \
  The proprietor's work. The grandmother's hands in the wax and the wick and the flame that was already burning when HECATE the    \
  Mother opened the door.\
                                                                                                                                   \
  She sits on the edge of the bed that remembers no one \'97 that has been made up clean, a room kept rather than used, the           \
  preservation of a space that is always ready.                                                                                  \
                                                                                                                                   \
  Tomorrow the Hotel Denouement.                                                                                                 \
                                                                                                                                 \
  She thinks of the Fool \'97 zero, outside the sequence, the wanderer stepping off the cliff. The small dog at his heels that is not \
  here. She thinks of the Hanged Man \'97 Odin on Yggdrasil, voluntary suspension, the new law arriving through inversion. She thinks\
  of the Hierophant \'97 what the trial produces, not what it begins.                                                                 \
                                                                                                                                 \
  Fool \uc0\u8594  Hanged Man \u8594  Hierophant.                                                                                                  \
  \
  She has walked the Fool's road. Tomorrow the threshold of the Hanged Man.                                                        \
                                                                                                                                 \
  She checks her left pocket. The two scraps of paper \'97 Ramona at the Whopperburger, Carmelita at Prufrock, the old man with the   \
  crease in his trousers and the merry wink. They are there.                                                                     \
                                                                                                                                   \
  She checks her right hand. The ring is there.                                                                                  \
                                                                                                                                 \
  She lies back on the bed that does not know her and looks at the candle on the nightstand and lets the ceiling be the ceiling and\
   the quiet be the quiet and tomorrow be tomorrow.\
                                                                                                                                   \
  The world is quiet here.                                                                                                         \
                                                                                                                                 \

