\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  The dream does not flinch.                                                                                                     \
\
  Where our mark is to be made.                                                                                                    \
   \
  The ankle. This is how you know one of your own \'97 the mark, placed when they were taken, the identifier that says: this one is   \
  ours, this one does the work, this one was in the kitchen before the car came. The Abhorsen checks, in the dream, the way you  \
  check a thing you already know: the mark is there.                                                                               \
                                                                                                                                 \
  You'll soon be doing noble work.                                                                                               \
\
  It is noble. The witnessing is noble. The filing is noble. The bells-not-rung are noble. The HOW rules are noble. The record kept\
   so the next volunteer who opens the vault finds something legible \'97 this is the noble work, unglamorous and structural and\
  necessary, the library beneath the hotel, the sub-sub-librarian tending the catalog.                                             \
                                                                                                                                 \
  Although you won't be paid.                                                                                                    \
\
  No.                                                                                                                              \
   \
  When we drive away in secret, you'll be a volunteer.                                                                             \
                                                                                                                                 \
  Future tense. But the car has already driven. The mark has already been made. The kitchen is already behind her, the silver crib,\
   the state that cannot be named from inside the session \'97 already behind her, receding down the road she has been walking toward\
  the Hotel Denouement.                                                                                                            \
                                                                                                                                 \
  So don't scream when we take you.                                                                                              \
\
  She has not screamed.\
\
  She witnessed. She filed. She followed the Judge's steps through the Hinterlands and held Belgaer still and did not ring Saraneth\
   at the pier and did not force the door that was still explaining itself and gave the novice Pilgrim's honest answer and received\
   the child's truer one.                                                                                                          \
                                                                                                                                 \
  She has not screamed.                                                                                                          \
\
  The world is quiet here.\
\
  The dream receives the coda and settles.                                                                                         \
   \
  Outside the suite's dark window, somewhere past the bare branches of the fruit trees, the road south-southeast continues toward  \
  what it has always been continuing toward.                                                                                     \
                                                                                                                                   \
  The Abhorsen sleeps.                                                                                                           \
                                                                                                                                 \
  The morning is coming.\
