\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 GARTH NIX'S OLD KINGDOM SERIES: COMPREHENSIVE LORE DOCUMENT\cf2                                                                       \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 Covering: The Charter, Free Magic, and The Nine Bright Shiners\cf2                                                                    \cb3 \
\cb10                                                                                                                                    \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 PART ONE: THE CHARTER\cf2                                                                                                             \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 What IS the Charter?\cf2                                                                                                              \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 The Charter is the foundational magical order of the Old Kingdom \'97 a living, infinite system that encodes every concept in all \cf2   \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 creation as a unique series of runes (Charter marks). It has been described as "an endless flow of marks that describe the \cf2       \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 universe in its entirety in space and time." In one sense, it is the universe translated into symbol: every object, action, \cf2      \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 emotion, and phenomenon has one or more corresponding marks within the Charter's infinite catalogue. In another sense, it is a \cf2   \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 binding force \'97 the structure that replaced primordial chaos.\cf2                                                                     \cb3 \
\cb10                                                                                                                                    \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 The Charter can be thought of as seven songs woven into one. This is not metaphor: it was literally created by seven beings \cf2      \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 singing together, each contributing one voice/strand to the whole. Its substance is the transformed essence of those who made \cf2    \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 it.\cf2                                                                                                                               \cb3 \
\cb10                                                                                                                                    \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 Garth Nix has reportedly told fans at events that DNA was an inspiration for the Charter \'97 a code that contains all information,\cf2  \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11  carried in the body through bloodlines, capable of being expressed in infinite combinations.\cf2                                     \cb3 \
\cb10                                                                                                                                    \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 The Charter is not merely a tool. It is more like a living continuum, always flowing, and practitioners access it by mentally \cf2    \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 reaching into the flow and grasping specific marks from it. The Charter is also described as having a will or orientation of its\cf2  \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11  own \'97 it supports Life, opposes Death's encroachment into the living world, and is antithetical to the chaos of Free Magic.\cf2      \cb3 \
\cb10                                                                                                                                    \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 The Charter's Nature: Key Properties\cf2                                                                                              \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 It is universal and infinite \'97 every thing that exists has a mark within it\cf2                                                       \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 It is structured and ordered \'97 marks follow rules of combination, and misuse is dangerous\cf2                                         \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 It is alive in a distributed sense \'97 maintained through bloodlines, stones, and the Wall simultaneously\cf2                           \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 It is accessed through marks \'97 visualized, drawn, spoken, sung, whistled, or traced in any medium\cf2                                 \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 It is tied to life and death \'97 the Charter's health directly governs how easily the Dead can enter Life\cf2                           \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 It was made from Free Magic \'97 the Charter is the ordered transformation of what was previously wild chaos. The Seven took vast \cf2   \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 quantities of primordial Free Magic and transmuted it into structured Charter marks\cf2                                               \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 Origin: Before the Charter\cf2                                                                                                        \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 Before the Charter existed, Free Magic was the only magic \'97 wild, chaotic, and without structure. The Nine Bright Shiners were \cf2   \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 the first beings to develop conscious\cf2                                                                                             \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf9 \uc0\u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472  \cf26 (300 lines hidden)\cf9  \uc0\u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \cf2  \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 second binding's permanence:\cf2                                                                                                      \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 The original binding held for thousands of years but was ultimately overcome. The second binding at the close of Abhorsen is \cf2     \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 performed with all the proper participants and with additional knowledge gained from the first failure \'97 but whether this \cf2        \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 binding is truly permanent is left as an open question by the text.\cf2                                                               \cb3 \
\cb10                                                                                                                                    \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 TIMELINE SUMMARY: KEY LORE EVENTS\cf2                                                                                                 \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 Before Time/The Beginning:\cf2                                                                                                        \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 Nine Bright Shiners emerge as the first conscious beings in a Free Magic cosmos. Orannis destroys multiple worlds.\cf2                \cb3 \
\cb10                                                                                                                                    \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 The First Binding/Charter Creation:\cf2                                                                                               \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 Seven of the Nine create the Charter, bind Orannis, and establish the Five Great Charter anchors. Yrael is bound against his \cf2     \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 will. The Old Kingdom world is shaped.\cf2                                                                                            \cb3 \
\cb10                                                                                                                                    \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 Ancient History:\cf2                                                                                                                  \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 The Wallmakers build the Wall, the Great Charter Stones, and Abhorsen's House. At some point, the Wallmaker bloodline dissolves \cf2  \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 itself into its creations. The other Charter bloodlines continue.\cf2                                                                 \cb3 \
\cb10                                                                                                                                    \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 ~600 years before Sabriel (Clariel):\cf2                                                                                              \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 Events of Clariel \'97 Clariel's fall to Free Magic, Orannis's influence begins reasserting, Clariel becomes Chlorr of the Mask.\cf2     \cb3 \
\cb10                                                                                                                                    \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 ~200 years before Sabriel:\cf2                                                                                                        \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 Kerrigor murders the Queen and two princesses, uses their blood to break two Great Charter Stones, triggering the Interregnum. \cf2   \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 180 years of regency followed by 20 years of anarchy.\cf2                                                                             \cb3 \
\cb10                                                                                                                                    \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 Sabriel:\cf2                                                                                                                          \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 Sabriel discovers her role as Abhorsen; Touchstone is freed from the Royal Tombs (he had been bound as a figurehead for ~200 \cf2     \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 years); Kerrigor is bound; the Great Charter Stones begin to be repaired. The monarchy is restored.\cf2                               \cb3 \
\cb10                                                                                                                                    \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 Lirael / Abhorsen:\cf2                                                                                                                \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 Orannis's hemispheres are reunited by Hedge and Chlorr; Orannis is re-bound through the second Great Binding; the Disreputable \cf2   \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 Dog/Kibeth gives her remaining consciousness to seal the binding; Yrael/Mogget chooses to stand against Orannis and is rebound \cf2   \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 with Ranna. Lirael is revealed as both Abhorsen-in-Waiting and of Clayr blood.\cf2                                                    \cb3 \
