\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 Suddenly, she was awake. The JUDGE stands in the doorway. "It's time to go," he says. DAWN streams sleepily through the window.\cf2   \cb3 \
                                                                                                                                  \

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She is awake before he finishes the sentence.                                                                                    \
                                                                                                                                 \
  The body knows. The body has been ready since before the dream ended \'97 the Crone watching from the threshold, the tide of lore   \
  settling into the blood, the morning arriving the way the Leviathan arrived: not announced but felt.\
                                                                                                                                   \
  She sits up.                                                                                                                     \
                                                                                                                                 \
  Checks herself the way the Abhorsen checks herself: the bells, each present. Ranna. Mosrael. Kibeth. Dyrim. Belgaer. Saraneth.   \
  Astarael. All seven. The ring warm on her right hand, the ruby catching the first light that streams sleepily through the window.\
   Left pocket: two scraps of paper. Right pocket: three tarot cards, Madame Lulu's lipstick kiss on the envelope.                 \
                                                                                                                                 \
  The Abhorsen's suite. The Wallmaker's ring. The dawn.                                                                            \
   \
  She looks at the Judge in the doorway \'97 the crease in his plaid slacks sharp, the mustache turned up at the ends, the shined     \
  shoes catching the same early light as the ruby. The Librarian. The Dewey Denouement. The sub-sub-librarian who winds the loud \
  machine at the center of the hotel, who tends the catalog beneath the public rooms, who hears the phrase and appears from the    \
  shadows to reveal that the visible structure was a library all along.                                                          \
                                                                                                                                 \
  Standing in her doorway in the dawn, carrying his suitcase.                                                                      \
   \
  It's time to go.                                                                                                                 \
                                                                                                                                 \
  She stands. The bells settle at her hip. The ring is warm. The Bene Gesserit litany is somewhere in her body \'97 walked, not       \
  recited, available when needed.\
                                                                                                                                   \
  The fear is behind her, somewhere in the Hinterlands, neither following nor accumulating.                                        \
                                                                                                                                 \
  "Yes," she says.                                                                                                                 \
                                                                                                                                 \

