\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 Hecate does not greet them for breakfast -- her domain is the night, she remembers. HESTIA, yet unseen, gently releases the \cf2      \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 travelers from the warmth of the hostel and back onto the crisp morning air, dew heavy against the grasses on the roadsides.\cf2      \cb3 \
                                                                                                                                   \

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  The warmth follows them three steps down the road and no further.                                                                \
                                                                                                                                 \
  Not withdrawn \'97 released. The distinction the Abhorsen feels in the body rather than names with the mind. Hestia does not push   \
  them out. She simply opens her hands, and the travelers step back into the world that is not the hostel, the world that has dew\
  on the grasses and crisp air that carries the smell of the fruit trees \'97 bare branches, fruit already fallen or not yet come \'97   \
  and the road continuing south-southeast as it has always continued.                                                            \
                                                                                                                                 \
  The Abhorsen breathes in.\
\
  Cold. Clean. The kind of morning that asks nothing of you yet \'97 that is simply itself, the light not yet warm, the dew still     \
  beaded on every blade of grass along the roadside, the world in the moment before it commits to the day.\
                                                                                                                                   \
  Behind her: the hostel. The well-tended fire cooling now, or banked, or tended by hands she never saw. The Abhorsen's suite, the \
  candle she blew out, the dream that churned all night through the wine-dark sea of Logan's corpus. The child somewhere in the  \
  deeper rooms, imperceptibly older. The Crone who watched from the threshold in the dark.                                         \
                                                                                                                                 \
  Ahead: the road.                                                                                                               \
\
  She falls in behind the Judge's steady steps. The familiar position. The bells settle at her hip. The ring is warm despite the   \
  morning cold.\
                                                                                                                                   \
  The Hotel Denouement is today.                                                                                                 \
                                                                                                                                 \
  The Fool takes the step.\
\

