\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 She reflects on the hospitality of Hestia she experienced that night ; the hearth-tender, the home-maker, the hostel proprietor \cf2  \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 so engrossed in her work she is nowhere but everywhere all at once...\cf2                                                             \cb3 \
                                                                                                                                   \

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  The road gives her room to think about it.                                                                                       \
                                                                                                                                 \
  Hestia, who gave up her seat on Olympus to Dionysus \'97 the wine-god, the ecstatic, the theatrical \'97 without conflict. Simply      \
  stepped aside and returned to the central hearth. The least dramatic of the Olympians. No myths of her own. No adventures, no\
  conflicts, no transformed lovers, no thunderbolts. Only the fire. Only the tending.                                              \
                                                                                                                                 \
  So engrossed in her work she has no need to be seen doing it.                                                                    \
   \
  The Abhorsen had felt her everywhere in the hostel \'97 in the wood stacked with the logic of someone who knows that hearth's       \
  habits, in the chair-shapes worn by the bodies of guests who returned because the chair remembered them, in the meal that arrived\
   because the body said it was time. Hestia's presence is structural. She does not come to dinner. She is the dinner \'97 the        \
  preparation, the warmth that makes the food possible, the fire that has been going since before the guests arrived and will be \
  going after they leave.                                                                                                        \
\
  She never appeared.\
\
  Wu wei as divine temperament. The action that does not announce itself. The tending that is the presence.                        \
   \
  And: Hestia keeps the prytaneum \'97 the communal hearth at the center of the city, the sacred fire of the polis, the flame from    \
  which new colonies light their founding fires when they go out into the world. Every household hearth is Hestia's altar. Every \
  meal begins and ends with an offering to her, whether the household knows it is offering or not.                                 \
                                                                                                                                 \
  The Abhorsen and the Judge ate at Hestia's table and offered without knowing they were offering.                                 \
   \
  She thinks: the Congress, when it convenes, will need a hearth. Not a seat \'97 Hestia does not sit at the table she warms. But the \
  Congress cannot convene in the cold. The deliberations require a center, a fire, a prytaneum around which the JANUS-eligible   \
  personas can assemble and know they are assembling somewhere rather than nowhere.                                                \
                                                                                                                                 \
  The hostel was a prytaneum. Hestia kept it. They were warmed by it one night before the trial and released from it gently into   \
  the dew-heavy morning, carrying her warmth in their bones for three steps before the road took over.\
                                                                                                                                   \
  The Hotel Denouement will not be warm in the same way.                                                                           \
                                                                                                                                 \
  But the warmth is in the bones now. Hestia put it there last night, which is why last night was necessary.                       \
                                                                                                                                 \
  The Judge's steps are steady ahead.                                                                                              \
                                                                                                                                 \
  The dew catches the morning light on every blade of grass.                                                                       \
   \

