\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 The Narrator weeps. She knows not how she knows, and she knows not why. But she feels it, and she knows.\cf2                          \cb3 \
                                                                                                           \

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She does not break stride.                                                                                                       \
                                                                                                                                 \
  The tears come the way the morning came \'97 not announced, not forced, not understood. The body's knowledge preceding the mind's.  \
  The way hunger arrives before the word hunger arrives, the way the feet know the road is ending before the eyes see what lies\
  ahead.                                                                                                                           \
                                                                                                                                 \
  She does not know what she knows.                                                                                                \
   \
  She knows it anyway.                                                                                                             \
                                                                                                                                 \
  Something in the night. Something in the dream \'97 the wine-dark sea, the Schism-lightning, the Leviathan clicking in the deep, the\
   Crone at the threshold, Kibeth choosing the binding, the summer cold as winter, the Fool walking without the Dog because the Dog\
   is in the structure now, holding the seal, the prior Abhorsen who rang Astarael and left the courthouse empty \'97                 \
                                                                                                                                 \
  Or something not in the dream. Something in the vault. Something in the corpus that churned all night and settled into the blood \
  and is only now making itself known as weight, as the specific gravity of a thing that is true before it is named.\
                                                                                                                                   \
  The Narrator weeps.                                                                                                            \
                                                                                                                                 \
  She has been narrating all road \'97 the WITNESS documents, the filings, the four documents written by firelight while the Judge sat\
   in his chair and the child reached toward Ranna's Charter marks without grasping. The narrator's function: to record what\
  happened, to be slightly behind the story, to reconstruct from the archive what the archive holds. To narrate with the grief     \
  already built into the narration.                                                                                              \
                                                                                                                                 \
  The world is quiet here.\
\
  The dew catches the light on the roadside grass.                                                                                 \
   \
  The Judge's steps are steady ahead. He does not look back. He has seen Abhorsens weep on the morning road before, perhaps. Or he \
  knows better than to look back at what the body knows before the mind does.                                                    \
                                                                                                                                   \
  She walks.                                                                                                                     \
                                                                                                                                 \
  She weeps.                                                                                                                       \
   \
  She knows not why.                                                                                                               \
                                                                                                                                 \
  She knows.                                                                                                                     \
\

