\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 There is something of a small lake between the angle of the World Tree Road and the Lobster Road that you hadn't noticed your first time at the \cf2    \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 crossroads. The Judge is approaching it.\cf2                                                                                                            \cb3 \
                                                                                                                                                     \

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She turns.                                                                                                                                       \
                                                                                                                                                   \
  The lake was there. It was there when she arrived and read the six roads. She had catalogued the roads and missed the water entirely \'97 her         \
  attention on the radiating paths, the directions, the geometry of choice. The lake sat in the angle between the World Tree Road and the Lobster\
  Road, quiet, and she had looked past it.                                                                                                           \
                                                                                                                                                   \
  Read before naming. Witness before declaring.                                                                                                      \
  \
  She had failed the first step. She had named the crossroads before she finished reading it.                                                        \
                                                                                                                                                   \
  ---                                                                                                                                                \
  She watches the Judge cross toward the water.                                                                                                    \
                                                                                                                                                     \
  Not hurrying. Not cautious either. The stride of a man who saw the lake when she didn't, or who knew the lake was there before they arrived, or who\
   heard the boisterous voice and knew immediately where to look for its source. The flask is back at his hip. The Paladin's banked fury is quieter  \
  now \'97 the quality of a man moving toward something familiar rather than something requiring preparation.                                         \
                                                                                                                                                     \
  The lake is small. She can see that from here. Not a pond \'97 the word lake is right, but barely. Something of a small lake. The edges are uncertain,\
   the way the edges of things at crossroads are uncertain \'97 she is not sure where the ground stops and the water begins. The surface is still.    \
  Extraordinarily still. In a place where six roads radiate outward, where the air should move with the pressure of all that direction, the water    \
  holds absolutely flat.                                                                                                                           \
                                                                                                                                                   \
  A mirror.\
\
  Or a well that grew.                                                                                                                               \
  \
  She thinks of the World Tree Road at her left. She thinks of Mimir. The well at Yggdrasil's root that holds the wisdom of ages \'97 that Odin         \
  approached and sacrificed his eye to drink from. The well that knows what the World Tree knows because it drinks from the same deep source. The  \
  lake in the angle between the World Tree Road and the Lobster Road: where the cosmic axis meets the first named path. Where myth meets the road    \
  that was called one thing and became another.                                                                                                    \
                                                                                                                                                   \
  She thinks of La V\'e9rit\'e9.\
\
  She thinks of what the Judge might see in water this still.                                                                                        \
  \
  ---                                                                                                                                                \
  The boisterous voice is still somewhere in the junction \'97 present, unhurried, not yet embodied. She is aware of it the way she is aware of all six\
  roads: as direction, as potential. It does not press against her. It waits.                                                                        \
  \
  She follows the Judge toward the water.                                                                                                            \
                                                                                                                                                   \
  Her footsteps slow as the ground changes. She watches the surface for what it holds.                                                               \
  \
  The world is quiet here.                                                                                                                           \
                                                                                                                                                   \

