\cb10                                                                                                                                                      \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 ---\cf2                                                                                                                                                 \cb3 \
\cb10                                                                                                                                                      \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 In May of 2026, Logan Finney signs a lease in Idaho that extends one final year.\cf2                                                                    \cb3 \
\cb10                                                                                                                                                      \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 The lease ends in June of 2027. After that, he and his partner are leaving for Chicago.\cf2                                                             \cb3 \
\cb10                                                                                                                                                      \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 The decision arrives not as a dramatic rupture but as a long exhale after years of holding tension in the body. The move is not impulsive. It is \cf2   \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 strategic, mournful, inevitable. The intervening year becomes a planning horizon: save money, build portability, prepare portfolios, disentangle \cf2   \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 roots, survive one final winter in a place that once felt like destiny and now feels increasingly like a negotiation with gravity.\cf2                  \cb3 \
\cb10                                                                                                                                                      \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 Idaho still lives inside him. That is part of the problem.\cf2                                                                                          \cb3 \
\cb10                                                                                                                                                      \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 Logan is not a tourist of the Inland Northwest. He is an Idahoan in the deep-structure sense: mountain weather, statehouse politics, panhandle \cf2     \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 forests, Mormon corridors, river canyons, dusty roads, newsroom fluorescent lights, public records requests, university scandals, and the long \cf2     \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 psychic shadow of American conservatism. He grew up in it. Learned it. Loved it. Reported on it. He became a journalist because Idaho fascinated \cf2   \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 him \'97 its contradictions, its mythology, its woundedness, its beauty, its refusal to simplify itself.\cf2                                               \cb3 \
\cb10                                                                                                                                                      \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 He became good at journalism there.\cf2                                                                                                                 \cb3 \
\cb10                                                                                                                                                      \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 Not \'93good for Idaho.\'94 Good, period.\cf2                                                                                                                 \cb3 \
\cb10                                                                                                                                                      \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 By 2026 he is an acclaimed journalist working for Idaho Public Television, a state public media institution whose licenses are held by the Idaho \cf2   \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 State Board of Education. This fact matters to him in a political-science sense. He does not merely work at a television station. He works inside \cf2  \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 the architecture of the State itself: public legitimacy, constitutional authority, legislative scrutiny, civic identity. He understands \cf2            \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 institutions as systems of narrative power because he has spent years watching them manufacture reality in public.\cf2                                  \cb3 \
\cb10                                                                                                                                                      \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 That understanding began crystallizing in college.\cf2                                                                                                  \cb3 \
\cb10                                                                                                                                                      \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 In 2019, while studying journalism at the University of Idaho, Logan became one of the lead student organizers behind STUDENTS FOR DENISE, the \cf2     \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 movement protesting the university administration\'92s treatment of documentary filmmaker and professor Denise Bennett.\cf2                                \cb3 \
\cb10                                                                                                                                                      \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 The Bennett crisis was not merely a faculty dispute. For the students involved, it became an education in institutional behavior under pressure.\cf2    \cb3 \
\cb10                                                                                                                                                      \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 A Vandal Alert \'97 the same emergency infrastructure stud\cf2                                                                                             \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf9 \uc0\u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472  \cf26 (67 lines hidden)\cf9  \uc0\u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \cf2  \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 ot romanticize self-destruction. He has watched too many institutions consume charismatic, emotionally open people. He remembers Denise Bennett. \cf2   \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 He remembers the atmosphere of public escalation, procedural rhetoric, and institutional retaliation. He remembers how movements mythologize \cf2       \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 mentors while real humans collapse under pressure.\cf2                                                                                                  \cb3 \
\cb10                                                                                                                                                      \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 He does not want martyrdom.\cf2                                                                                                                         \cb3 \
\cb10                                                                                                                                                      \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 He wants integration.\cf2                                                                                                                               \cb3 \
\cb10                                                                                                                                                      \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 That desire ultimately shapes the decision to leave.\cf2                                                                                                \cb3 \
\cb10                                                                                                                                                      \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 Chicago represents less an escape fantasy than a possibility of scale. In Idaho, Logan often feels symbolically overdetermined \'97 not merely a \cf2      \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 journalist, but a Queer Idaho Journalist, perpetually legible as category and condition. Chicago offers density, anonymity, queer life without \cf2     \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 constant explanation, institutional plurality, archives, public media ecosystems, intellectual subcultures, labor history, and enough social \cf2       \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 complexity that he may finally become a person instead of a representative.\cf2                                                                         \cb3 \
\cb10                                                                                                                                                      \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 The move does not erase Idaho.\cf2                                                                                                                      \cb3 \
\cb10                                                                                                                                                      \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 If anything, distance may sharpen his understanding of it. Exiles often become the clearest chroniclers of the places they leave behind. Logan \cf2     \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 suspects he will always report on Idaho in some form. The state remains emotionally entangled with him: the mountains, the legislature, the \cf2        \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 statehouse, the university, the forests, the mythology, the cruelty, the tenderness.\cf2                                                                \cb3 \
\cb10                                                                                                                                                      \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 Leaving feels less like abandonment than ending an abusive relationship with a place that raised him beautifully while increasingly rejecting \cf2      \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 parts of him essential to survival.\cf2                                                                                                                 \cb3 \
\cb10                                                                                                                                                      \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 The grief is real.\cf2                                                                                                                                  \cb3 \
\cb10                                                                                                                                                      \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 But so is the horizon.\cf2                                                                                                                              \cb3 \
\cb10                                                                                                                                                      \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 And perhaps most importantly, Logan is beginning to understand that the next phase of his life cannot be organized primarily around institutional \cf2  \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 tolerability. The old bargain no longer works. Success without coherence becomes spiritually corrosive over time.\cf2                                   \cb3 \
\cb10                                                                                                                                                      \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 So the year between May 2026 and June 2027 becomes a transitional era:\cf2                                                                              \cb3 \
\cb10                                                                                                                                                      \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 archive consolidation,\cf2                                                                                                                              \cb3 \
\cb10                                                                                                                                                      \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 emotional reckoning,\cf2                                                                                                                                \cb3 \
\cb10                                                                                                                                                      \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 logistical planning,\cf2                                                                                                                                \cb3 \
\cb10                                                                                                                                                      \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 portfolio building,\cf2                                                                                                                                 \cb3 \
\cb10                                                                                                                                                      \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 psychiatric stabilization,\cf2                                                                                                                          \cb3 \
\cb10                                                                                                                                                      \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 executive-function scaffolding,\cf2                                                                                                                     \cb3 \
\cb10                                                                                                                                                      \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 financial preparation,\cf2                                                                                                                              \cb3 \
\cb10                                                                                                                                                      \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 and the slow difficult labor of imagining a future not governed entirely by survival adaptation.\cf2                                                    \cb3 \
\cb10                                                                                                                                                      \cb3 \
\cb10                                                                                                                                                      \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 He is still a journalist. Still an Idahoan. Still obsessed with archives and systems and framing and public memory. Still deeply earnest beneath \cf2   \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 layers of irony and institutional fluency.\cf2                                                                                                          \cb3 \
\cb10                                                                                                                                                      \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 But something fundamental has shifted.\cf2                                                                                                              \cb3 \
\cb10                                                                                                                                                      \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 For the first time in years, the future feels less like containment and more like motion.\cf2                                                           \cb3 \
\cb10                                                                                                                                                      \cb3 \
