  They have arrived at the place.                                                                                                                    \
                                                                                                                                                   \
  ---                                                                                                                                                \
  She stands beside the Judge and does not fill the silence.                                                                                       \
                                                                                                                                                     \
  The motion is in his hands.\
                                                                                                                                                     \
  The scroll reads: the future feels less like containment and more like motion.                                                                     \
                                                                                                                                                   \
  Both words. Motion as legal instrument. Motion as direction of travel. The double meaning filed simultaneously in a crossroads lake, delivered in  \
  the interior of a conch shell, by a god who is good to his mother because his mother demands nothing less.                                       \
                                                                                                                                                     \
  She waits for the Judge to speak, or to move, or to do whatever a Judge does when he has received the motion and is ready for the proceedings to   \
