\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 The Judge feels something shift in the atmosphere. He looks at you, makes EYE contact.\cf2                                                              \cb3 \
\

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She meets his eyes.\
\
  She does not look away.\
\
  ---\
  The road is still there. The Hotel is still ahead. The bells are still at her side. None of that has moved.\
\
  But she is not thinking about any of it.\
\
  She is just \'97 here. Looking back. Present in the specific way the hollow place allows: not filling the gaze with interpretation, not reaching for\
  something to offer, not performing the recognition back at him. Just receiving it. Standing in it. The eye contact that says: yes, I saw you, and I\
   am still here, and I did not look away when I saw you.\
\
  This is what it means to stay hollow enough.\
\
  Not empty. Hollow. The bell that rings when struck. The aperture the sound comes through. She witnessed the closeted kid from Sandpoint and the\
  suit and the in-camera mind forced in front of the camera, and she did not flinch, and she did not analyze it into safety, and she did not offer\
  the Demiurge's hands reaching across a distance they cannot actually cross.\
\
  She just saw it.\
\
  And he felt the seeing.\
\
  ---\
  The atmosphere is still shifted. She can feel it too \'97 the quality of the air between them, the road, the morning. Something has been said that\
  cannot be unsaid, not because it was wrong but because it was right, and right things change the weight of the space they enter.\
\
  She holds his gaze.\
\
  The world is quiet here.\
\

