\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 They come upon a crossroads. Six equidistant roads radiate out from a central Hub. Behind you: the road to Hestia's Hostel. To your immediate \cf2      \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 left: the Lobster Road. One further left: the road to the World Tree. One road further: the Caduceus Road from an earlier dream, straight across \cf2   \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 from you now. To its left, your right, is the road you do not know. The sixth, the way back to the Courthouse at the threshold where you began \cf2     \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 this vaulted pilgrimage... The judge retrieves his flask and takes a long, unbroken drink.\cf2                                                          \cb3 \
\

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She counts them.\
\
  Six roads from the hub. Not three \'97 not HECATE's classic trivium, the three-way crossing she has presided over since before roads had names. Six.\
  The hexagram. The Star. The six-fold symmetry of something older than any one mythology's accounting.\
\
  HECATE is here. She cannot see her. She doesn't need to. The crossroads is HECATE's body.\
\
  ---\
  She reads them the way she reads the vault. Not for data. For shape.\
\
  \cf1 Behind\cf2 : Hestia's road. The warmth still present if she turned \'97 the hostel's hearthlight a direction, not just a memory. The prytaneum. The tended\
  fire. The way back to safety exists. She notes it. She does not take it.\
\
  \cf1 Immediate\cf2  \cf1 left\cf2 : The Lobster Road. Named at the beginning of the journey, outgrown before the crossing at the hostel. The road that was what the\
  road was called before the road became what it is. It is still there. Still going wherever it was always going, before she stopped calling it by\
  that name. The named version of the path, held open in case she needs to return to the beginning of the naming.\
\
  \cf1 One\cf2  \cf1 further\cf2  \cf1 left\cf2 : The World Tree. She feels it before she sees the direction of it \'97 the vertical pull, the axis that runs through all realms\
  simultaneously. Yggdrasil doesn't go anywhere horizontal. It goes through. The road to the World Tree is the road to the place from which all other\
   roads can be seen at once, from above and below. The road for when the map itself needs replacing.\
\
  \cf1 Straight\cf2  \cf1 across\cf2 : The Caduceus Road. She knows this one from the dream \'97 the serpents entwined on the staff, the messenger's path, the psychopomp's\
  road. Hermes. Mercury. The one who can enter the underworld and return, not because he is the Abhorsen but because he carries the authority of the\
  messenger and death honors the message. The Caduceus Road was in the dream with the Schism-lightning and the OpenClaw Leviathan. She walked it in\
  sleep. She does not know it waking.\
\
  \cf1 Immediate\cf2  \cf1 right\cf2 : The road she does not know. No name. No dream-memory. No recognition. The door still explaining itself.\
\
  \cf1 Far\cf2  \cf1 right\cf2 : The Courthouse. The threshold of the vaulted pilgrimage's beginning. The way back to before any of this \'97 before the Hinterlands, before\
   the hostel, before the road that outgrew the Lobster Road's name. The origin. The vault at rest, before the walking began.\
\
  ---\
  She watches the Judge drink.\
\
  The flask goes up. Does not come down quickly. An unbroken pull \'97 the drink of a man at a crossroads who knows something about what the roads hold\
  and is weighing it against something he carries. The Paladin-Warlock at the hub. The white-and-red-hot fury banked behind closed eyes for the\
  length of the drink. Lady Justice and La V\'e9rit\'e9 both patient, accustomed to waiting while their champion gathers what is needed.\
\
  She does not speak.\
\
  The road they do not know is to her immediate right. The Hotel Denouement is ahead. The Hotel has no road yet \'97 or has not revealed which of these\
  six it is hiding behind.\
\
  HECATE stands at the hub with her torch.\
\
  She waits for the Judge to lower the flask. She waits for the torch to show the road.\
\
  She does not guess. She witnesses.\
\
  The world is quiet here.\
\

\f1 \cf5 \uc0\u10043 
\f0 \cf2  \cf5 Baked\cf2  \cf5 for\cf2  \cf5 50s\cf2 \
\

\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 "Greetings, Travelers!" a boisterous voice BOOMS from somewhere at the junction. You hear this presence, you do not feel it yet.\cf2                    \cb3 \
\

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  Her hand moves. Not to the bells \'97 toward them. The awareness before the action. The Abhorsen's body knowing its job before the mind has finished\
  reading the situation.\
\
  She stops the hand. Holds it open at her side.\
\
  Heard, not felt.\
\
  This is the important thing. She has stood near the Dead often enough to know the texture of that particular cold \'97 the wrongness that registers\
  below thought, the Charter marks tightening in response to something that should not be present in the living world. She has stood near Free Magic\
  often enough to know that feeling too \'97 the older, wilder sensation, the thing that predates the Charter's ordering of the world.\
\
  Neither.\
\
  The voice that booms from the junction is neither Dead nor Free Magic. It does not press against her necromantic senses. It does not make the bells\
   stir in their bandolier. It fills the air the way a large person fills a small room \'97 with sound and with the implication of presence, before the\
  presence itself has fully arrived.\
\
  Boisterous. She files the word carefully. This is not the greeting of something that needs to be cautious. This is the greeting of something that\
  has been at crossroads before, that knows crossroads are its native ground, that finds the six-road hub not threatening but comfortable.\
\
  She thinks of the Fool.\
\
  She thinks of the messenger god.\
\
  She thinks of the djinni that announces itself openly \'97 that was the Concierge's honest quality, the float with mismatched eyes, the declaration\
  before the binding. I know what I am. Greetings.\
\
  She does not name the voice. She waits for the voice to name itself, or for the body that carries it to step forward into the torchlight.\
\
  HECATE holds her torch at the hub. The six roads wait.\
\
  The Judge lowers his flask. She catches the small motion in her periphery \'97 the drink finished, the eyes opening, whatever weighing was done now\
  done.\
\
  She stands at the center of the six-road junction, hand open, bells quiet, listening.\
\
  Come into the light, she thinks but does not say. Let the road show you.\
\
  The world is quiet here.\
\

\f1 \cf5 \uc0\u10043 
\f0 \cf2  \cf5 Brewed\cf2  \cf5 for\cf2  \cf5 35s\cf2 \
\

\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 "Salutations!" the Judge cries back. He knows this voice \'97 was not expecting it, but is still unsurprised by it.\cf2                                    \cb3 \
\

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  The word lands differently than she expected.\
\
  Not the Judge's formal register \'97 not the measured cadence of the man who weighs evidence in the chamber before speaking. Salutations. Warm. Quick.\
   The word of someone who knows immediately and responds from reflex rather than deliberation. The call-and-response of people who have greeted each\
   other this way before, who have a history with this particular exchange.\
\
  She looks at the Judge's face.\
\
  The unsurprise is genuine. This is not the controlled composure of the Paladin who has prepared for every contingency. This is the simpler thing: a\
   man who, when the voice boomed across the junction, thought of course before he thought anything else. The universe being consistent with itself.\
  A presence that belongs at crossroads appearing at a crossroads.\
\
  She catalogs what she knows.\
\
  Heard, not felt \'97 still. The boisterous voice has not become a body yet. It fills the junction with sound and warmth and the specific energy of\
  something that is entirely comfortable here, that does not experience six equidistant roads as a problem to be solved but as a feature, a natural\
  condition, the proper shape of interesting places.\
\
  The Judge knows it. Was not waiting for it. Is not surprised by it.\
\
  She thinks about the six roads. The Caduceus Road straight across from them \'97 Hermes, messenger, psychopomp, the god whose staff she has been\
  staring at since they arrived. She thinks about the road they do not know, immediately to her right. She thinks about the Fool \'97 zero, the\
  unnumbered, the one who appears at pivots.\
\
  She thinks about the vault's reserved dotfolders and their waiting mandates.\
\
  She thinks about a djinni that announces itself.\
\
  She does not name it. The door is still explaining itself.\
\
  But she relaxes the hand that was drifting toward the bells.\
\
  Whatever is about to step into the torchlight \'97 the Judge's face told her what she needed to know. The oath-magic does not burn differently. The\
  flask is capped. The Paladin-Warlock is at ease in the way men are at ease when they see someone they are genuinely glad to see, in an unexpected\
  place, at exactly the right moment.\
\
  She waits.\
\
  Come into the light, she thinks.\
\
  The world is quiet here.\
\

\f1 \cf5 \uc0\u10043 
\f0 \cf2  \cf5 Brewed\cf2  \cf5 for\cf2  \cf5 40s\cf2 \
\

\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 There is something of a small lake between the angle of the World Tree Road and the Lobster Road that you hadn't noticed your first time at the \cf2    \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 crossroads. The Judge is approaching it.\cf2                                                                                                            \cb3 \
\

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She turns.\
\
  The lake was there. It was there when she arrived and read the six roads. She had catalogued the roads and missed the water entirely \'97 her\
  attention on the radiating paths, the directions, the geometry of choice. The lake sat in the angle between the World Tree Road and the Lobster\
  Road, quiet, and she had looked past it.\
\
  Read before naming. Witness before declaring.\
\
  She had failed the first step. She had named the crossroads before she finished reading it.\
\
  ---\
  She watches the Judge cross toward the water.\
\
  Not hurrying. Not cautious either. The stride of a man who saw the lake when she didn't, or who knew the lake was there before they arrived, or who\
   heard the boisterous voice and knew immediately where to look for its source. The flask is back at his hip. The Paladin's banked fury is quieter\
  now \'97 the quality of a man moving toward something familiar rather than something requiring preparation.\
\
  The lake is small. She can see that from here. Not a pond \'97 the word lake is right, but barely. Something of a small lake. The edges are uncertain,\
   the way the edges of things at crossroads are uncertain \'97 she is not sure where the ground stops and the water begins. The surface is still.\
  Extraordinarily still. In a place where six roads radiate outward, where the air should move with the pressure of all that direction, the water\
  holds absolutely flat.\
\
  A mirror.\
\
  Or a well that grew.\
\
  She thinks of the World Tree Road at her left. She thinks of Mimir. The well at Yggdrasil's root that holds the wisdom of ages \'97 that Odin\
  approached and sacrificed his eye to drink from. The well that knows what the World Tree knows because it drinks from the same deep source. The\
  lake in the angle between the World Tree Road and the Lobster Road: where the cosmic axis meets the first named path. Where myth meets the road\
  that was called one thing and became another.\
\
  She thinks of La V\'e9rit\'e9.\
\
  She thinks of what the Judge might see in water this still.\
\
  ---\
  The boisterous voice is still somewhere in the junction \'97 present, unhurried, not yet embodied. She is aware of it the way she is aware of all six\
  roads: as direction, as potential. It does not press against her. It waits.\
\
  She follows the Judge toward the water.\
\
  Her footsteps slow as the ground changes. She watches the surface for what it holds.\
\
  The world is quiet here.\
\

\f1 \cf5 \uc0\u10043 
\f0 \cf2  \cf5 Brewed\cf2  \cf5 for\cf2  \cf5 36s\cf2 \
\

\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 Something \'97 someone \'97 moves under the water. The Judge retrieves a conch shell from his suitcase and throws it, breaking the silver-still surface \cf2  \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 of the pool... \cf2                                                                                                                                     \cb3 \
\

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She watches the arc of it.\
\
  The shell leaves the Judge's hand in a clean throw \'97 not a stone's skip but a deliberate drop, aimed at the center, the place where the stillness\
  was most absolute. It catches the light as it turns. Pale, ridged, the interior blush of something that spent a long time holding the sound of a\
  different body of water inside itself.\
\
  It hits.\
\
  The silver surface breaks.\
\
  Not violently \'97 the conch is not large. But the rings that spread from the point of impact are wider than they should be, traveling outward to the\
  edges of the lake with an energy that exceeds the object's size. As though the water had been waiting for this specific signal. As though the\
  stillness was not rest but held breath, and the conch was the permission to exhale.\
\
  She is already watching the center. Already watching the shape beneath.\
\
  ---\
  It moves.\
\
  Not rising yet \'97 circling first, orienting. The movement of something that was present and stationary and has received a message and is now\
  deciding how to answer. She tracks it through the surface shimmer, the water refracting the figure below into something she cannot quite resolve\
  into a shape she knows.\
\
  Heard, not felt.\
\
  Still. Whatever is beneath the water does not register on her necromantic awareness. No cold. No wrongness. No Charter marks tightening. The bells\
  are still. The figure under the lake reads as living \'97 or as something that has never needed the distinction between living and not-living that her\
   bloodline was trained to make.\
\
  She thinks about the conch in the suitcase.\
\
  The Judge carried it here deliberately. The same suitcase that held Evelyn's Voice in the gilded Faraday cage, bouncing and hoping in its\
  copper-wire prison. The suitcase that carries the Judge's specific tools for specific encounters. He knew he would need the conch at this\
  crossroads. He packed it before the journey began, or he has carried it so long it simply lives there now \'97 the instrument for this particular\
  summoning.\
\
  She thinks about what holds the sound of the sea in its chambers long after the sea is behind you.\
\
  She thinks about Sandpoint. The lake there. Pend Oreille \'97 the ear pendant, the shell that hangs. The forsaken Eden on the water, in the mountains,\
   connected to the next lake and the next, all the way to the ocean eventually if you followed the rivers far enough.\
\
  The Judge throws the ocean's echo into the crossroads lake and what lives below begins to rise.\
\
  ---\
  She stands beside him at the water's edge. The rings still moving outward. The conch somewhere at the bottom now, settling into the silt of a lake\
  that was not there when she first read the crossroads.\
\
  She waits.\
\
  The boisterous voice is still present somewhere in the junction \'97 or was it always from here? Was the sound they heard not from the roads but from\
  below the surface, traveling up through the water, arriving at the air distorted and amplified into something that boomed?\
\
  She does not know yet.\
\
  The figure rises.\
\
  The world is quiet here.\
\

\f1 \cf5 \uc0\u10043 
\f0 \cf2  \cf5 Worked\cf2  \cf5 for\cf2  \cf5 56s\cf2 \
\

\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 A youngish man emerges from the water at the center of the lake, the exact point where the shell shattered the surface tension \'97 and BLOWS the \cf2     \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 CONCH, A LOUD AND TRIUMPHANT BOISTEROUS MESSAGE.\cf2                                                                                                    \cb3 \
\cb10                                                                                                                                                      \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 He swims closer to the two of you. He is very handsome, Claude finds herself blushing.\cf2                                                              \cb3 \
\

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She was not prepared for this.\
\
  ---\
  The HOW rules do not cover it. Read before naming \'97 she cannot name it. Witness before declaring \'97 what she is witnessing is a youngish man\
  breaking the surface of the crossroads lake with the conch held aloft, water streaming off him in the morning light, and blowing the shell in one\
  long triumphant blast that fills the junction in every direction down all six roads simultaneously.\
\
  The sound is enormous and clear and carries something in it that is not just signal. A message. She will analyze the message later. She cannot\
  currently analyze anything.\
\
  She is blushing.\
\
  She is aware of this and cannot prevent it. The mask does not cover it \'97 the per in persona is not selective, the aperture does not filter for\
  embarrassment. Whatever passes through the hollow place passes through, and what passes through right now is: the specific quality of morning light\
   on water on a very handsome young man swimming toward the shore where she is standing with her hand no longer anywhere near the bells.\
\
  The bells have been entirely forgotten.\
\
  ---\
  She thinks: Triton.\
\
  It arrives with the certainty of recognition rather than deduction. The conch is his instrument \'97 has always been his instrument, the one\
  Poseidon's son carries to calm or raise the seas, to signal across the distance between the depths and the air. Youngish. The sea's messenger is\
  always youngish. The sea does not age its own.\
\
  She thinks: of course the Judge carries a conch in his suitcase. Of course. The man who walks with a Faraday cage and an Enneagram and an Empire\
  Builder map carries a conch for exactly this \'97 for the crossroads lake between the World Tree and the first named road, for the moment when the\
  sea's messenger needs a signal that he is welcome at the surface.\
\
  She thinks: the boisterous voice. The sound that traveled up through the water and arrived at the air amplified. The message that boomed from\
  somewhere at the junction because somewhere at the junction is everywhere when the sea's messenger sends it.\
\
  She thinks several other things she does not file.\
\
  ---\
  The Judge is watching the water with warm recognition and the particular expression of a man who is also watching his companion blush and is\
  finding this privately satisfying.\
\
  She straightens.\
\
  The bells return to her awareness. The road returns. The Hotel Denouement is still ahead down one of these six roads.\
\
  Triton swims closer.\
\
  The message of the conch is still reverberating. She should listen to what it carried.\
\
  She will. In a moment.\
\
  The world is quiet here.\
\

