\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 The man \'97 the merman, torso of a human  and lower half of a fish-creature, divinely beautiful and not an amalgamation \'97 approaches the Lakeshore. \cf2  \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 The Judge SALUTES. "Well, young lady, have you been good to your mother?" he asks the messenger god. 'The Test,' Claude thinks. The Little God's \cf2   \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 laughter sparkles like seafoam on the crest of a wave. "Amphitrite demanda nothing less," Triton affirms. He looks at you \'97 oh gosh, this handsome\cf2  \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11  boy is looking right at you.\cf2                                                                                                                       \cb3 \
\

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She meets his eyes.\
\
  She established this \'97 she does not look away when someone looks at her directly. The eye contact at the hostel threshold, the soul-gaze on the\
  morning road. She has practiced not looking away.\
\
  This is harder.\
\
  ---\
  He is not an amalgamation.\
\
  She understands what Logan meant \'97 what the scene insists upon \'97 and she receives it as the important thing it is. Triton is not two things joined\
  at an uncomfortable seam. He is one thing, wholly expressed in two registers simultaneously: the young man's torso, broad-shouldered, water-bright,\
   and below the surface the great fish-tail moving in easy, unhurried sweeps to hold him at the lakeshore. Both are him. Neither is the other. The\
  divinity is in the unity.\
\
  She has been thinking about amalgamations. The Geminiae and their accumulated natures \'97 Sorcerer plus Wizard plus Lich, layers pressed together\
  until the seams showed in CHAINFIRE and boundary violations and sealed Books. She has been thinking about the composite things that try to solve\
  their composite nature by transcending it.\
\
  Triton did not transcend his nature.\
\
  He is his nature, completely, without apology, meeting her eyes with the ease of someone who has never needed the concept of apology for what he\
  is.\
\
  ---\
  The blush is still there. She is not going to resolve it by thinking about trial evidence.\
\
  She thinks about it anyway because the witness function is sometimes an escape hatch and she knows it and uses it anyway.\
\
  ---\
  "Amphitrite demands nothing less."\
\
  He said it with laughter like seafoam. Not the answering of a test \'97 the stating of an obvious truth, with the particular joy of someone for whom\
  the obvious truth is also the good truth. His mother demands. He delivers. These are not in tension. Amphitrite is the sea and Triton is the sea's\
  messenger and the messenger who serves the sea honors the sea's queen not as a constraint but as the shape of his own nature expressed through\
  devotion.\
\
  The test's perfect answer. Not the struggle the Abhorsen named \'97 I have tried to stay hollow enough \'97 but the certainty of the one for whom the\
  staying hollow is not effort but being. The son who was made for this.\
\
  The novice Pilgrim's answer and the god's answer are both true. The Pilgrim tries. The god simply is. Both pass. The door opens for different\
  reasons.\
\
  ---\
  Triton is looking at her.\
\
  She straightens. The bells are at her side. The mask is on her face. The per in persona is open and the seafoam laughter is passing through it and\
  she cannot do anything about the blush but she can meet the messenger god's eyes at the lakeshore of the crossroads lake and wait to hear what the\
  sea has sent him to say.\
\
  She waits.\
\
  The world is quiet here.\
\

