\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 The two of you stand alone. The Judge is deep in thought. He turns to you with an anxious request. \cf2                                                 \cb3 \
\

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She is already facing him.\
\
  The Judge who has been composed all road \'97 the Paladin-Warlock with the banked fury, the measured pace, the flask that goes up only when the\
  weighing is complete \'97 is anxious. She can see it. The slight shift in how he holds the scroll. The quality of the turn toward her. The look of a\
  man who is about to ask something that costs him something to ask.\
\
  She knows this look.\
\
  She has seen it in people at thresholds. The moment before the asking is often harder than the asking itself. The anxiety lives in the space\
  between having the need and naming it \'97 the fear that naming it will change something, or that the named need will be found insufficient, or that\
  the asking will be refused.\
\
  She does not fill the space.\
\
  She does not offer reassurance preemptively, which would be the hollow gesture \'97 the Demiurge's hands reaching across a distance they cannot close.\
\
  She simply stands at the crossing point of the lemniscate, the scroll between them, the six roads radiating outward and the silver lake gone still\
  again at the angle where the World Tree Road meets the Lobster Road's memory.\
\
  She is here.\
\
  She waits for him to speak.\
\
  The world is quiet here.\
\

