\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 Hermes awaits them. They begin the path of the psychopomp. They walk in silence while the road is still the road of the junction, before it develops an identity of its own.\cf2                                      \cb3 \
                                                                                                                                                                                 \

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She walks.                                                                                                                                                                                                       \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  The road is still the road of the junction \'97 radiating from the hub, not yet committed to what it will become further along. She can feel this quality under her feet: the pavement or gravel or packed earth of \
  the crossroads itself, which has no particular character because it belongs to all six directions simultaneously. The roads do not begin to be themselves until they are far enough from the center to have left \
  the center behind.                                                                                                                                                                                               \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  They have not left it yet.                                                                                                                                                                                       \
   \
  Hermes is ahead. She cannot see him. She can feel the direction of him \'97 the way she has learned on this road to feel the direction of things before they are visible. The Caduceus Road's presiding presence.   \
  The god who moves between realms without dying because he carries the staff that opens every border, the wings that are native to every altitude, the coin that pays every ferryman.                           \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She walks beside the Judge.                                                                                                                                                                                    \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  The silence is right. You do not speak on the road of the psychopomp until the road speaks first \'97 until it has declared itself, shown its character, given them the vocabulary with which to describe where they\
   are going.\
                                                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She does not know yet where they are going.                                                                                                                                                                      \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  The right lobe of the lemniscate. Deeper into the Hinterlands, the bird's-eye view had suggested, before the road curves and returns. How deep. What is found there. What Hermes waits to show them, or guide    \
  them through, or carry across on his behalf.                                                                                                                                                                   \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She walks.                                                                                                                                                                                                       \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  The road is still forming under her feet.                                                                                                                                                                        \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  The world is quiet here.                                                                                                                                                                                         \
   \

