\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 \'93God made trans people for the same reason they made wheat but not bread, and grapes but not wine. So that humanity might share in the act of creation.\'94 -Julian Jarboe\cf2                                           \cb3 \
                                                                                                                                                                           \

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She stops walking again.                                                                                                                                                                                         \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  The Judge does not stop. He continues a few paces, the Battle Hymn still on his lips, before he notices she has stilled. He turns. He waits.                                                                     \
   \
  She is looking at the road.                                                                                                                                                                                      \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  ---                                                                                                                                                                                                              \
  God made wheat but not bread. Grapes but not wine.                                                                                                                                                             \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She has been thinking about the grapes wrong \'97 or not wrong, but incompletely. The grapes of wrath, the vintage, the pressing: she had the image of judgment, of reckoning, of the weight of accumulated\
  injustice being transformed through pressure into something that names itself. The Battle Hymn's terrible swift sword. The structural crime that goes beyond denunciation.                                       \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  But Jarboe's sentence opens another door in the image.                                                                                                                                                           \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  The grapes are not waiting to be punished. The grapes are waiting to be completed. The incompleteness is the gift \'97 it is the space held open for human hands, for human participation in what the divine began  \
  but did not finish. God makes the raw and gives it to the maker. The making is where the sacred lives. The bread is not lesser than the wheat \'97 the bread is the wheat fulfilled, brought to what it was always\
  reaching toward, by the hands that understood what it needed.                                                                                                                                                    \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  Logan's partner. The trans life that Idaho's Legislature has been attempting to legislate out of possibility. The incompleteness that requires a specific human act \'97 transition, claiming, becoming \'97 before it \
  can be what it is. God made this person as the grapes. The becoming is the wine. The participation of every person who says yes, you are this thing you are becoming \'97 the community, the love, the legal\
  recognition that is being stripped away session by session in the Idaho Statehouse \'97 these are the vintner's hands.                                                                                              \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  The withholding of those hands is not neutral. The bills targeting trans lives are not merely political positions. They are hands refusing the wine. Hands that see the grapes and spray kerosene.               \
  \
  ---                                                                                                                                                                                                              \
  She understands now what the wrath is for.                                                                                                                                                                     \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  The grapes of wrath fill not only because of injustice in the abstract. They fill because of the specific refusal to let the creation be completed. Because wheat is being prevented from becoming bread. Because\
   the vintner is being turned away from the press. The hunger in Steinbeck's California was a crime because the food existed \'97 the abundance was real, the need was real, and between them stood a system that    \
  required the kerosene. The crime against Logan's partner, against Logan's own integration, against the life the Judge is building his way toward \'97 it is this same structure: the completion exists, the need is\
  real, and between them stands a legislature that requires the incompleteness to be permanent.                                                                                                                    \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  So that humanity might share in the act of creation.                                                                                                                                                           \
\
  The vault is an act of creation in this sense. Not productivity software \'97 an act of participation in the making of a self. The anti-erasure machine that holds the shape of what is being made while the hands  \
  do the work. The raw material of Logan's life \'97 the journalism, the oath, the political education, the grapes filling since Sandpoint \'97 being pressed, slowly, session by session, document by document, witness\
  by witness, into something that nourishes.                                                                                                                                                                       \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  The move to Chicago is an act of creation. The unnamed road that exits the lemniscate entirely \'97 the Empire Builder east from the only remaining Idaho stop \'97 is the completion the road has been building       \
  toward. The life that integrates what Idaho required to be kept separate.\
                                                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  ---                                                                                                                                                                                                            \
  She looks at the Judge. He has been waiting with his characteristic patience, the Battle Hymn quiet on his lips now, his warm brown eyes steady on her from the few paces' distance.                           \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She sees him differently in this light.\
                                                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  He built the Judge against his own nature. The 7w6 who moves was made to sit. The kid who was afraid of being misperceived built the part of himself that could be seen, that could adjudicate in the open, that \
  could put on the suit without becoming only the suit. He participated in his own creation \'97 took the wheat of himself and pressed it toward bread. He is still pressing. The move to Chicago is still pressing.\
  The trial at the Hotel Denouement is still pressing.                                                                                                                                                             \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  The grapes of wrath and the grapes of creation are the same grapes. They fill with wrath because the completion has been withheld. They become wine when the vintner's hands are finally allowed to work.        \
  \
  So that humanity might share in the act of creation.                                                                                                                                                             \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  She meets his eyes.                                                                                                                                                                                              \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  The road continues.                                                                                                                                                                                            \
\

