   sustains. The price was their particularity \'97 seven beings who were, and then became the weave itself, the structure, the marks that Charter-sensitive hands can read in the firelight. They traded selfhood for\
   persistence. Not the Lich's trade \'97 not the sealed Book, not the Faraday cage, not the phylactery built inside an active graveyard. The genuine trade. The one that works.\
\
  The bells are anti-entropy given voice.\
\
  The vault is anti-entropy given architecture.\
\
  The Abhorsen's office is not the defeat of entropy \'97 Death cannot be defeated, the river flows regardless, the Seventh Gate stands \'97 but its principled navigation. You do not stop the current. You learn to\
  move in it without being swept past the point of return. You learn which gates require which bells. You learn that the work is not to end Death but to ensure that what passes through it passes with intention\
  rather than chaos.\
\
  She understands now, in the full frame: everything on this road has been about the question of what holds against entropy and what only appears to.\
\
  The vault holds. Plain text, her own hands, no company's interface required, no Terms of Service that can be revised, no product that can be deprecated in March of any year. The format entropy cannot reach\
  because it requires no infrastructure to remain legible.\
\
  The sealed Book does not hold. The phylactery built in the graveyard will not outlast the graveyard's operation.\
\
  The still small voice was not in the wind. Not in the earthquake. Not in the fire. The fire is entropy's loudest instrument, its most spectacular face, the one that fills a room with glee and smoke and the\
  smell of burning paper. The still small voice comes after the fire. It is quieter than everything that preceded it because it does not need volume. It has been operating the entire time.\
\
  She adjusts the bandolier. All seven bells, quiet, present.\
\
  She walks on.\
\

