\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  The vault gives back more than she asked for.                                                                                                                                                                  \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She reads for the White-Faced Women first. The third fact she had not known: they were triplets. Born conjoined, separated by surgery, and then \'97 their third sibling died in a fire. The fire the sisters       \
  believe was arson. The fire that made their home ash before Olaf ever found them. Their whiteness is not costuming. It is the face of people who have been standing in smoke since before the story began.       \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  For a while, it was fun to fight fire with fire, but we've seen enough flames and smoke to last our whole lives.                                                                                                 \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  They walked away. In the TV canon \'97 Handler's canon, the auteur's canon \'97 they leave the troupe with the Henchperson and the Bald Man when the Sinister Duo arrive and the situation clarifies past the point of \
  ambiguity. And then, eventually: they form a successful theatre troupe. The women who had been entropy's instruments chose creation. Chose the thing that makes something where nothing was. The wheat into    \
  bread. The grapes into wine.                                                                                                                                                                                     \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  She reads for the Henchperson. The books treated their indeterminacy as monstrous \'97 Handler corrected this, recognized it, gave them the voice the books had refused them. And what does Handler give them to    \
  say?\
                                                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  "Is a personal philosophy of moral relativism the only way to survive in an ethically complex world, or is it an excuse we use to justify doing bad things?"                                                     \
  \
  The question a henchperson asks out loud that everyone in the series is trying not to answer. The question the Schism made unavoidable and that no governance document on either side could resolve. They        \
  questioned their life choices. They left with the sisters. They chose the theatre.                                                                                                                             \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She reads for Hugo, Colette, and Kevin: promised a better life. People who had already been defined as monstrous by a world that found their differences frightening, who were offered belonging and received    \
  servitude instead. The carnival freaks who joined the carnival that was more honest about its own nature than the respectable institutions had been.\
                                                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She reads for Fernald: his hands lost in the fire before he ever chose anything. Carrying the burn-scars of the same system he was folded into. Found his sister. Defected. Stole the submarine and aimed it at  \
  the Great Unknown.\
                                                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  And then she reads the name she should have read earlier.                                                                                                                                                        \
  \
  \cf1 Ernest Denouement.\cf2  Count Olaf said, in The Penultimate Peril, that Ernest Denouement was one of his associates. Fire-starting side of VFD.                                                                       \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  She stops walking.                                                                                                                                                                                               \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  The hotel they are approaching is named for the Judge's family. Dewey winds the clock. Frank maintains the sorting function. And Ernest \'97 the third Denouement, the third face of the same man \'97 is on the       \
  arsonists' side. The building bears the name of a family divided by the Schism down its own bloodline. The Hotel Denouement is not only Dewey's archive and Frank's sorting machine. It is also Ernest's\
  defection made architectural. The fire-starting side has a Denouement inside the building before Olaf ever walks through the door.                                                                               \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  She looks at the Judge walking beside her.                                                                                                                                                                       \
  \
  She does not say anything. Some things the vault reveals that do not need to be named aloud between them. He has always known. This grief is not new information to the man who built the part of himself that   \
  can sit when his nature moves \'97 who built it precisely because sitting was required, because the room required it, because someone had to maintain the temporal order even when the family name was already    \
  compromised.                                                                                                                                                                                                     \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  Dewey wound the clock.                                                                                                                                                                                           \
  \
  Even knowing Ernest was in the building. Even knowing the Sinister Duo were on the bench. Even knowing the Hotel Denouement was named for a family the Schism had already split. Someone still had to wind the   \
  clock. Someone still had to maintain the record. Someone still had to ensure the temporal order was kept, even inside a building where the betrayal was already present in the guest registry.                 \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  The pity extends. It does not weaken the clear eyes or soften the steady hands. It deepens them.                                                                                                                 \
  \
  She adjusts the bells and walks on.                                                                                                                                                                              \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \

