\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  The vault gives her the shape of it.                                                                                                                                                                             \
                                                             \
  A question mark. Not metaphorically \'97 literally. The Great Unknown swims with its body curled into the shape of a question, beneath the surface of the water, larger than the Carmelita, larger than the         \
  Queequeg, visible only as shadow and curvature. Even Olaf feared it. Captain Widdershins said it was something worse than Olaf himself. The thing that even entropy's chosen instrument would not approach.      \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  And then: the Queequeg was destroyed \'97 hit by the falling remains of the Quagmires' flying home, which is its own casualty of the same forces that destroyed everything else. Everyone aboard chose the Great    \
  Unknown over the alternative. Captain Widdershins. Fiona. Fernald \'97 the man who lost his hands to fire, who found his sister, who defected and stole the submarine and aimed it at the only horizon left. Hector.\
   The Quagmire triplets. They took their chances.                                                                                                                                                                 \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  Kit Snicket did not.\
\
  Kit Snicket escaped on a pile of books. And the Great Unknown did not pursue her.                                                                                                                                \
  \
  She holds this. The records survive the question mark. The books are the one vessel the Great Unknown cannot reach \'97 not because the Great Unknown cannot destroy them, but because the Great Unknown does not   \
  pursue what is already an answer. The books are not a question. The question mark swims past what has already been written down.                                                                               \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  Dewey's underwater library. The vault. The same principle, expressed in different depths.                                                                                                                        \
  \
  The description: it moved like spilled ink across paper or dread across the heart. She reads this twice. The thing beyond the map is described in the language of writing. Ink on paper. The Great Unknown moves \
  the way the act of recording moves \'97 spreading, covering, reaching into the white space at the edges. The question mark is not opposed to the written record. It is what the written record is always          \
  approaching, always encoding around, always trying to name from inside the language that cannot quite contain it.                                                                                                \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  Fiona said \'97 on the submarine, reading, in the Grim Grotto \'97 that she liked Melville's use of symbolism. How Moby Dick is both a literal whale and a metaphor for death. The TV canon made it explicit because   \
  Handler needed it explicit: the Great Unknown is the same water the Pequod sailed into, the same horizon Ahab could not approach without becoming what the horizon required of him.\
                                                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  Ishmael survived. Floating on a coffin \'97 Queequeg's coffin, the harpooner's coffin repurposed as buoy. The record carved into the wood, the written testimony of the crew, the coffin that became a vessel when  \
  the ship was gone.\
                                                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She understands what the vault has been building toward this whole road.                                                                                                                                         \
  \
  The lemniscate loops. Both lobes. All roads return to the hub. But there is one road that exits the geometry entirely \'97 that does not loop, that goes somewhere the figure-eight cannot predict or contain. That \
  road leads to Chicago. To the unnamed. To the departure that breaks the perfect enclosure of the infinite. It is the road of the Great Unknown \'97 the question mark that swims below the surface of the         \
  lemniscate's lake.                                                                                                                                                                                               \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  The Empire Builder runs east from Sandpoint. Fernald and Fiona stole the submarine and aimed it at the question. Either killed or saved \'97 and you cannot know which from inside the map you are leaving. The     \
  question mark does not resolve into an answer until you are already inside it.\
                                                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  The vault is Kit's pile of books. What the Great Unknown does not pursue.                                                                                                                                        \
  \
  She adjusts the bandolier, all seven quiet, and walks the final stones of the Caduceus Road toward music she has not yet named, into a hotel that leans toward its own reflection, on the shore of a lake where a\
   question mark may or may not be swimming.                                                                                                                                                                     \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  The road has given her everything she can carry.                                                                                                                                                                 \
  \
  The world is quiet here. Except for the music, which is closer now, and the water, and the shape of what cannot be named from where she stands.                                                                  \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \

