\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She returns from the Border Seas with what she found.                                                                                                                                                            \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  Three additional layers, compressed above the foundation. Readable now.                                                                                                                                          \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  The 1965 sessions first \'97 Ellington's own hand returning to the work in New York and Chicago, a fuller rendering with the "23rd Psalm" restored, conducted privately, kept sealed until 1985, then finally       \
  released in a compilation. Ellington revisiting his own testimony with seventeen years of additional weight. Not replacing 1958 \'97 deposited above it. A layer of the maker's own later voice, darker and heavier\
  than the original for having been held so long in private.                                                                                                                                                       \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  Then: the Jazz at Lincoln Center Orchestra with Wynton Marsalis, recorded live at Rose Theater, 2018. Released March 2020. She holds that date.                                                                  \
  \
  March 2020.                                                                                                                                                                                                      \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  Marsalis's first recording of the full suite \'97 Blue Engine Records' first release dedicated entirely to Ellington. The custodian of the tradition making the formal, definitive document. And with him: \cf1 Brianna \cf2  \
  \cf1 Thomas\cf2  on vocals, carrying the Mahalia Jackson inheritance forward in a younger register, deposited above Jackson's layer without displacing it. And \cf1 Eli Bishop\cf2  on violin \'97 a texture that was never in the\
  original orchestration, a string voice that Ellington didn't use there, something the Marsalis recording adds to the sandstone that changes the color of the surface strata.                                     \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  March 2020. The month the world locked down. The month before George Floyd. The month the grapes of wrath were filling again toward whatever pressing was coming.                                                \
  \
  The JLCO released the definitive recording of a tone poem about the long history of African American suffering and testimony into the first month of a pandemic that would, again, fall heaviest on the people   \
  the suite was written for. The timing is not the recording's fault. The timing is the world's testimony to the suite's endurance \'97 that Ellington wrote something which keeps being needed, keeps being layered,\
  keeps being deposited into new strata because the history it documents keeps being made.                                                                                                                         \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  She understands the sandstone now in full. Ellington's 1943 original at the foundation. The 1958 Mahalia Jackson recording above it. The 1965 private sessions above that. The 2020 Marsalis/Thomas/Bishop       \
  recording on the surface \'97 the most recent layer, lightest, still compressing.\
                                                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  All present simultaneously in what the Hotel Denouement is breathing into the air of the approaching road.                                                                                                       \
  \
  The Hotel holds time in its walls the way Idaho holds time in its hills.                                                                                                                                         \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  She walks toward the crest.                                                                                                                                                                                      \
