\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She reads them in the order they arrive.                                                                                                                                                                         \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  \cf1 Tyler Childers first\cf2  \'97 because "Way of the Triune God" goes deepest into the foundation, touches the same root the Ellington suite draws from. Can I Take My Hounds to Heaven? (2022) \'97 eight gospel songs in    \
  three versions each, the album structured as a journey through the Trinity. And the song's origin: the Georgia Sea Island Singers. A group formed in the early 1900s from the Gullah culture of the Lowcountry,  \
  African American, preserving the most direct living continuity with West African sacred tradition on American soil. Childers carried the melody as an acapella voice memo for years before recording it. A white \
  Appalachian man holding a Black Gullah inheritance long enough for it to become something he could give back, formally, with sixteen million listens on the Hallelujah version. The sandstone layer that doesn't\
  sit above the Ellington/Jackson foundation so much as run parallel to it \'97 the same deep aquifer, accessed from different ground.\
\
  \cf1 MARINA\cf2  \'97 EVERYBODY KNOWS I'M SAD, from PRINCESS OF POWER (June 2025). Rolling Stone placed it sixty-third on their list of the hundred best songs of 2025: a dance-pop song about depression, lyrics refreshingly\
   blunt, paired with a bouncy Eurodance house beat. She understands immediately. This is the frequency she felt from the Hotel before she heard the music clearly. Not naive joy \'97 the specific dissociation of a\
  body that has learned to dance to tempos faster than its actual emotion. Everybody knows I'm sad. The sadness is public knowledge. The bouncy beat is the performance layered on top of the fact that everybody  \
  already knows. The ecstasy and the revelation that the ecstasy is covering something \'97 both present simultaneously in the same two minutes and fifty seconds.                                                  \
