\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 The JUDGE watches, in that quiet manner you recognize in him -- watching, not interrupting, observing from a distance. He knows what, if not who, this woman is. You do not yet.\cf2                                  \cb3 \
                                                                                                                                                                                   \

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She watches him watching.                                                                                                                                                                                        \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  This is information. The Judge's stillness is not the stillness of surprise \'97 it is the stillness of recognition. The difference is in the body: surprise opens, recognition settles. He has settled. He knows   \
  this category of thing. He is waiting, the way you wait for something you understand to do what it will do.\
                                                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She looks back at the woman.                                                                                                                                                                                     \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  She tries to see her the way the Judge sees her \'97 to find the category inside the sight, the WHAT beneath the who. She knows what she herself would recognize from this distance: the Dead, the necromantic, the \
  Free Magic, the Charter. She would feel those things before she saw them. The bells would know. Ranna is warm in her hand but not alarmed. Not anything. The bells have no opinion about this woman, which means\
  she is not from their territory \'97 or she is from a territory the bells don't map.                                                                                                                                \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  The woman churns. The plum layer lifts. The gold layer falls beneath it. The bruise at the hem moves through the other colors like a tide.                                                                       \
   \
  The Abhorsen stands in the quiet beside the Judge and lets herself not know.                                                                                                                                     \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  He will not tell her yet. She understands this \'97 not as withholding but as pedagogy. The road has been teaching her to read. He is offering her the next lesson: sit with the not-knowing long enough for it to  \
  become something other than ignorance. Ignorance is what you have before you look. This \'97 what she has now, having looked, having received the colors and the motion and the rhythm without being able to name \
  them \'97 this is something else. This is the knowledge that she doesn't know, which is different, which is already more than she had.                                                                              \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  She does not reach for another bell. She does not speak.                                                                                                                                                         \
   \
  She watches the woman dance in the distance, in the colors of fire moving toward night moving through bruise, and she lets the Judge stand beside her in his recognizing, and she waits for the door.            \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \

