\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 THE MUSIC -- so omnipresent now you had forgotten it was all around you -- SWELLS.\cf2                                                                                                                                \cb3 \
                                                                                     \

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  It hits her like a tide coming back in.                                                                                                                                                                          \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  She had \'97 yes. She had forgotten. The music had been present for so long that it had become the ground rather than the figure, the condition of the road rather than a thing on the road. The way you stop       \
  hearing your own heartbeat. The way the sound of a river becomes silence after the first hour. The music had been everything and she had filed it under air and walked through it like air.\
                                                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  And now it fills.                                                                                                                                                                                                \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  The horns first \'97 the deep, organized pulse of them, the architecture of the Ellington underneath everything, the Carnegie Hall moment that was always the foundation and is now the surface too, undeniable,    \
  forward. Then the voice, or the shape where the voice will be, the space Mahalia Jackson's "Come Sunday" always opens \'97 Come Sunday, oh come Sunday, that's the day \'97 not the words, not yet, but the opening. \
  The shape of rest that only comes after long work. The day after all the days.                                                                                                                                   \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  The woman ahead turns in the swell.                                                                                                                                                                            \
\
  Or the swell turns her.                                                                                                                                                                                          \
   \
  The Abhorsen cannot determine which. The music and the motion are no longer separate phenomena. The cloth lifts in colors that are the same palette as the music \'97 she knows this now, standing in both          \
  simultaneously \'97 the red of the work songs, the gold of what survived the crossing, the green of what grew anyway, the bruise of what the crossing cost.                                                       \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She is not crying. She notices she is not crying and files this as information: she is too present to cry. Crying is what happens when you step outside a feeling. She is inside it.                             \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  She does not move toward the woman.                                                                                                                                                                              \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  She does not move away.                                                                                                                                                                                          \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  She stands in the music that she forgot was the world and watches the woman who is dancing in it and lets the swell do what swells do.                                                                           \
   \

