\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 You see a WOMAN on the horizon... The JUDGE has not noticed her yet --- She is in the distance, only yet a figure with no identifying qualities other than the shape of her gender at arm's length.\cf2               \cb3 \
\

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She sees her before she registers that she has seen her \'97 the way the eye catches motion or presence at the edge of attention before the mind has been consulted.\
\
  A woman. The horizon. The Hotel behind her or ahead of her \'97 the distance makes the geometry uncertain. Only the shape, at arm's length: the silhouette that carries gender in its bearing, in the way it stands\
  or moves or simply is.\
\
  The Abhorsen does not name her.\
\
  The HOW rules are not a discipline she imposes on herself in this moment \'97 they are what she is on this road, what the road has made her. She reads before she names. She witnesses before she declares. The\
  woman on the horizon is not yet a name. She is a presence. A fact. A door that has not yet begun explaining itself.\
\
  She slows her pace almost imperceptibly.\
\
  Her hand moves \'97 not to the bells. To the ring. The wallmaker's ruby, warm and steady, the anchor rather than the motion. She presses one finger against it and holds.\
\
  The Judge has not noticed. He is looking at the road ahead, or at the Hotel \'97 she does not check. She does not want him to look yet. Not because she needs to protect him from the sight, but because she wants\
  to have already seen the woman by the time he sees her. She wants to have already read what she can read from here before the Judge's recognition shapes her own.\
\
  She looks.\
\
  The figure does not move toward them with urgency. Does not move away. She is simply there, the way certain presences are simply there \'97 as if the road had always contained her and the Abhorsen is only now\
  arriving at the point where she becomes visible.\
\
  The Abhorsen thinks: I should know who this is.\
\
  She does not know yet.\
\
  She walks. She watches. She does not ring anything. The Hotel is ahead and the woman is between them and it, or beside it, or standing at its threshold \'97 the distance is still too great for certainty.\
\
  She waits for the door.\
\

