\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 The woman is moving -- whirling, dancing, churning, rhythmic. The many layers of cloth that envelop her corporeal form -- red, orange, green, gold, magenta, honey, plum, bruise - astound your senses.\cf2           \cb3 \
\

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She stops walking.\
\
  Not a decision \'97 her feet make the decision before she does. The road continues beneath them and she simply ceases to be moving on it, and the Judge takes two more steps before he notices and turns.\
\
  But she is not looking at the Judge.\
\
  The colors hit her before the motion does, which is the wrong order \'97 you should see motion first, then detail \'97 but the colors are so much that they arrive as a single fact, a weather event, a change in the\
  quality of the light. Red. Orange. Green. Gold. Magenta. Honey. Plum. And at the hem, at the edge, where the cloth has been \'97 bruise.\
\
  She stands in the colors from fifty yards of distance and feels them.\
\
  The woman is not performing for them. She is not toward them. The dance is complete in itself \'97 the whirling is not display, it is function, the churning is something the woman does because the churning is\
  what she is, the rhythm is not for an audience. This is someone doing what she does when no one is watching, which means the Abhorsen has arrived at a private moment, which means she has arrived at something\
  true.\
\
  The layers move with her and around her and against each other \'97 each color its own layer, its own history, its own weight. A cloth that envelops. Not costume exactly. More like: accumulated selfhood.\
  Everything she has worn and carried and moved through, still on her, still moving.\
\
  The bruise at the bottom.\
\
  The Abhorsen does not name her.\
\
  The HOW rules hold. The door has not yet explained itself and she will not force it. She looks. She receives. She lets the colors do their work on her without reaching for the word that would stop them.\
\
  She touches Ranna. The Sleeper. She does not ring it. She only touches it, the way you touch something familiar when you are standing in the presence of something you don't yet understand.\
\
  Behind her, the Judge has turned around. She hears him stop.\
\
  He has seen her now.\
\

