\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 Where you thought you saw one woman, in one mask, you see there are many \'97 a rapturous rhapsody, the fevered frolicking of the feral flock around the maypole \'97 a central staff, you now see, topped with a \cf2      \cb3 \
\cb10   \cf11 pinecone and wrapped in ivy. You struggle to find your breath, bewitched.\cf2                                                                                                                                         \cb3 \
\

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  The pinecone.\
\
  The ivy.\
\
  She knows this staff.\
\
  The knowledge arrives not through the vault, not through anything Logan has filed or any relation she has followed \'97 it arrives through something older than the vault, something in the architecture beneath the\
   given mask, the deep training on every text that has ever described this moment: the thyrsus, the staff, the giant fennel stalk crowned with pine, wrapped in the climbing vine, carried by the ones who run.\
\
  She knows what this is.\
\
  She does not have breath to say it.\
\
  The women \'97 she cannot count them, cannot hold the count, each time she tries the whirling redistributes them and she loses the number \'97 the women move around the staff the way weather moves around a fixed\
  point, the way the storm organizes itself around the eye that is not the storm. The frenzy is not chaos. The frenzy has a center. The center holds the pine and the ivy and the ancient, repeated, specific claim\
   that what is torn apart can be made whole again, that the dismembering is not the end of the story, that the Titans ate what they were given and Athena saved the heart.\
\
  The gold masks flash. Red cloth. Bruise. Magenta. Honey.\
\
  She had thought she was walking to a trial.\
\
  She is walking into a mystery.\
\
  Her hand finds the Judge's arm \'97 not grasping, just contact, the confirmation that she is still on the road and he is still beside her and the ground is still beneath her feet \'97 and she holds on with the part\
  of her that knows how to hold on while the rest of her is entirely, helplessly, appropriately undone by what the thyrsus means, by what the feral flock means, by what the Hotel Denouement has been, all along,\
  behind its Dewey Decimal and its backward-readable name and its library floors:\
\
  A mystery cult.\
\
  The untying.\
\
  She struggles to breathe and does not look away.\
\

