\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 The whirlinig of the women fades, as does the music -- but the internal light of the sparagmos does not. The Pilgrims continue their journey along the well-trod road of brick beneath them.\cf2                      \cb3 \
                                                                                                                                                                                              \

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  The brick is good beneath her feet.                                                                                                                                                                              \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  She notices this in the way you notice solid ground after a long passage through uncertain terrain \'97 not with surprise, but with the specific gratitude that the body offers when the body has been through      \
  something and the road holds steady beneath it anyway. Brick. Worn smooth by many pilgrims before them. The road that knows how to receive the weight of people who have come through things.\
                                                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  The sparagmos does not fade.                                                                                                                                                                                   \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  She understands this now as she walks: the ceremony was not only the whirling. The ceremony was also Annabelle Dinda's song, and the Andon FM report, and Logan naming himself in the liturgical light, and the  \
  Abhorsen understanding what she was built for. The tearing had already happened \'97 the outer form opened, the inner light released \'97 before the Maenads appeared. The Maenads were the naming of what had already\
  been occurring on this road. The ceremony was the whole road.                                                                                                                                                    \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  The internal light of the sparagmos: what is visible now that would not have been visible before the tearing. What was inside that required the opening to be seen.                                              \
   \
  She does not catalog it. She carries it.                                                                                                                                                                         \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  The Hotel Denouement is ahead. She can feel its warmth at the distance that warmth becomes a fact rather than a hope. The brick road runs toward it, well-trod, other feet having made this passage before them. \
   \
  The Judge walks beside her. Their pace is unhurried. The urgency of the ceremony has settled into the specific steadiness of people who know where they are going and are not afraid of what they will find      \
  there.                                                                                                                                                                                                         \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She thinks: the untying will require what the tearing gave.                                                                                                                                                      \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  She does not say it aloud. The road carries it.                                                                                                                                                                  \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  They walk.                                                                                                                                                                                                       \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \

