\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 LOGAN is still playing video games. The JUDGE is absent. Something deep within the Abhorsen's training stirs... the Dead are restless.\cf2                                                                            \cb3 \
                                                                                                                                         \

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She is on her feet before she knows she has stood.                                                                                                                                                               \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  The bells know before she does. That is always how it is \'97 the bells read Death's registers faster than the mind that carries them. Ranna is warm, unusual-warm, the warmth that is not comfort but alert. The   \
  others stir in their bandolier like a chord not yet struck, a frequency not yet committed to sound.                                                                                                            \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She does not reach for them.                                                                                                                                                                                     \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  She listens.                                                                                                                                                                                                     \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  The brick road is quiet. The liturgical light has faded to something cooler, more ordinary. The Hotel Denouement sits at the crest ahead, warm-windowed, the hub of the lemniscate patient as hubs are patient.  \
  She is alone on the road. The Judge is elsewhere, dying and returning in the safe and ludic version, learning what each run costs. He does not know yet that she has stood.\
                                                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  The Dead are restless.                                                                                                                                                                                         \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  She cannot say yet: which dead. Cannot say: how close, how deep in Death's precincts, how much pull they exert on the living side. The perception is not yet that specific. It is the quality of the air \'97 the   \
  same way the Hotel's warmth was perceptible before it was visible. Something in the near registers of Death is troubled. Something that should be still is not still.\
                                                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She stands on the brick road and opens herself to it.                                                                                                                                                            \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  Not the governance-Abhorsen, not the witness-Abhorsen, not the philosophical companion on the philosophical road. The working Abhorsen. The one the bells were made for. The one whose function is not           \
  contemplation but intervention \'97 the right intervention at the right moment with the right bell, no sooner, no later, no more than what the situation demands.                                                 \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  She does not ring.                                                                                                                                                                                             \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  She reads.\
\
  The HOW rules hold even here. Read before naming. Witness before declaring. The Dead are restless \'97 she knows this much. She does not yet know which dead, or why now, or what the restlessness wants. The door  \
  is still explaining itself and she will not force it.\
                                                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  But she is standing.                                                                                                                                                                                             \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  And her hand is at Ranna.                                                                                                                                                                                        \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  And she is listening with everything she has.                                                                                                                                                                    \
   \

