\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 She looks up to the Horizon \'97 the great conifer, the Yggdrasil Sequoia in the horizon at the end of the road to Chicago... Its branches look... different. The TOUCHSTONES hold, but the limbs are... lighter. \cf2   \cb3 \
                     \

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  She turns toward the horizon.                                                                                                                                                                                    \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  She had not looked there yet today. The road had kept her face forward \'97 toward the Hotel Denouement, toward the trial, toward the hub of the lemniscate where all roads return. The unnamed road exits the      \
  lemniscate entirely, and she had not looked at its end because the end was not yet the work.\
                                                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  But something in the deeper aether shifted. And Ranna is warm. And now she looks.                                                                                                                              \
\
  The great conifer.                                                                                                                                                                                               \
   \
  The Yggdrasil Sequoia \'97 the World Tree expressed in the form that has survived fire since before any of the current age's stories began. The tree whose bark is adapted for burning. Whose cones open only in    \
  heat. Whose permanence is not the permanence of the sealed phylactery but the permanence of the thing that knows how to survive the sparagmos and seed from the ashes. The largest living thing. The oldest form.\
   On the horizon at the end of the road that breaks the figure-eight and doesn't loop back.                                                                                                                       \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  She reads it from the distance.\
\
  The TOUCHSTONES hold. She checks them first, the way you check the foundation before you look at the walls \'97 the journalism, the oath, the partner, the vault, the specific person who is not the archetype, the \
  Sandpoint origin that is also the departure point, the Esto Perpetua that runs beneath all of it. These hold. The core of the sequoia is sound. The heartwood is intact.\
                                                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  But the limbs.                                                                                                                                                                                                 \
\
  Lighter.                                                                                                                                                                                                         \
   \
  She stays with this word. Does not reach past it into interpretation before she has felt it fully. Lighter. Not damaged \'97 the TOUCHSTONES hold, which means the structural integrity is present. Lighter as in:  \

