\f1 \cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095 
\f0  \cf11 The Judge gets that wry grin \'97 the one Logan feels creep across his lips when something appropriately named also happens to sound a little bit goofy. "BEEF-STACK." He chuckles.\cf2                                  \cb3 \
                                        \

\f2 \cf11 \uc0\u9210 
\f0 \cf2  The Abhorsen's composure holds for approximately one second.                                                                                                                                                     \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  Then she also laughs.                                                                                                                                                                                            \
   \
  Not the liturgical register \'97 the other kind, the kind that surprises her, the kind that arrives before she decides to let it. She laughs the way she reached for his arm in the Maenads: without deciding to.   \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \
  "BEEFSTACK," she repeats, tasting it. It sits in the mouth like a word that has no business being important and is anyway. Something Yrael committed while 322 gigabytes moved across a wire. Something that laid\
   ghost OIDs to rest. Something with that name.                                                                                                                                                                 \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                   \

